E["item:ahanu-s-leather-goods"] = {t="item",n="Ahanu's Leather Goods",z="thunderbluff",s="Ahanu's Leather Goods carries Thunder Bluff's leatherwork to the Crossroads. Ahanu sends finished leather armor and supplies to the Barrens for travelers there.",h="Ahanu's Leather Goods carries Thunder Bluff's leatherwork to the Crossroads.",sec={{t="Trade Across the Mesas",b="Ahanu prepares leather goods for trade beyond Mulgore. In Thunder Bluff, the leatherworker turns raw hides into finished apparel and gear for Jahan Hawkwing, a merchant at the Crossroads in the Barrens. The plains make overland travel slow, so the tauren send the parcel by air. Tal and Devrak's trained wind riders carry goods swiftly across long distances.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside Ahanu's Leather Goods?",a="Ahanu's parcel holds finished leather goods made from raw hides in Thunder Bluff. The practical armor and equipment are ready for sale to travelers.",al={"what are the leather goods","ahanu parcel contents","whats in the bundle"},it="item"},{q="Who receives this parcel?",a="Jahan Hawkwing receives the parcel at the Crossroads. He sells finished goods to the hunters, warriors, and adventurers passing through the central Barrens.",al={"who gets the leather goods","where does it go","jahan leather delivery"},it="target"},{q="Why is this package flown via wind rider?",a="Ahanu sends the parcel by wind rider because carrying heavy trade goods down the lifts and across the Barrens takes time. She directs the couriers to Tal, Thunder Bluff's wind rider master, to show how winged couriers can carry cargo quickly to distant posts such as the Crossroads.",al={"why fly the package","wind rider delivery thunder bluff","flight master package"},it="motive"},{q="What is Ahanu's Leather Goods?",a="It is a bundle of finished leather wares crafted in Thunder Bluff. The parcel is bound for the settlement of the Crossroads in the Barrens, meant to supply trade among the growing numbers of travelers gathering there.",al={"what is ahanus leather goods","ahanus leather goods item"},it="identity",add="32785653"},{q="Where do Ahanu's Leather Goods come from, and who made them?",a="The goods were prepared by Ahanu, a leatherworker plying his craft high atop the mesas of Thunder Bluff. He assembled the finished wares out of raw hides sent to him from the Barrens.",al={"who made ahanus leather goods","origin of ahanu leather goods"},it="origin",add="962e36b1"},{q="Why does anyone want Ahanu's Leather Goods?",a="Jahan Hawkwing requested the parcel to sell to patrons passing through the Barrens. The Crossroads has become a bustling hub filled with wandering hunters and adventurers, creating a lively demand for quality, freshly crafted leather gear.",al={"why deliver ahanus leather goods","who wants ahanu leather goods"},it="why_wanted",add="6d92aaf6"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see how this delivery connects Mulgore, your ancestral homeland, with Horde territories across the Barrens."},kw={"ahanu","crossroads","devrak","jahan hawkwing","leather goods","tal","thunder bluff","wind rider"},rel={"npc:ahanu","npc:jahan-hawkwing","quest:6363","quest:6364","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:crossroads","npc:devrak"},src={"Ahanu's Leather Goods","Tal the Wind Rider Master (Classic)","Return to Jahan"}}
E["item:arikara-serpent-skin"] = {t="item",n="Arikara Serpent Skin",z="thunderbluff",s="At Darkcloud Pinnacle, Arikara is summoned and slain, leaving a scaled hide behind. Carried to Whitereach Post, the skin proves the wind serpent was defeated.",h="At Darkcloud Pinnacle, Arikara is summoned and slain, leaving a scaled hide behind.",sec={{t="Trophy of a Summoned Wrath",b="Arikara is a formidable wind serpent tied to ancient tauren legend. Rumor says she seeks retribution against Cairne Bloodhoof as tauren ways change. Under Elder Magatha Grimtotem's direction, champions prepare enchanted Incendia Powder. They light the sacred fire atop Darkcloud Pinnacle's burial bluffs, drawing the spirit-beast into the physical realm. Stripping Arikara's hide leaves the Arikara Serpent Skin, proof of her death.",sp=0},{t="A Troubling Revelation",b="At Whitereach Post, Motega Firemane receives the skin as proof that Arikara is dead. Magatha Grimtotem insisted the serpent hunted Cairne Bloodhoof out of ancestral rage. Yet the slain creature leaves Motega bewildered: why would such a spirit threaten their High Chieftain? The pelt settles the immediate danger, but Motega is left questioning Magatha's interpretation.",sp=1,bt={"q4821.5"}}},faq={{q="What is the Arikara Serpent Skin?",a="The Arikara Serpent Skin is the scaly hide taken from Arikara, a legendary wind serpent summoned and defeated atop Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles.",al={"serpent skin","arikara skin","what is this skin"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the Arikara Serpent Skin?",a="Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post wants the skin and the remainder of the Incendia Powder as proof that Arikara no longer threatens anyone.",al={"who takes the skin","who turn in to","who wants arikara skin"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why was Arikara summoned in the first place?",a="Magatha Grimtotem claimed changes in tauren traditions angered the ancestral serpent Arikara, who stalked High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. She ordered the beast drawn forth and slain before Cairne could be harmed.",al={"why summon arikara","why kill arikara"},it="motive"},{q="Where does one obtain the skin?",a="The skin comes from Arikara after she is summoned with enchanted Incendia Powder cast onto the sacred fire of life, on a burial needle within Darkcloud Pinnacle.",al={"where to get arikara serpent skin","arikara location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where does the Arikara Serpent Skin come from?",a="The skin is taken directly from the corpse of Arikara, a vicious wind serpent spirit summoned at Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles. Magatha Grimtotem enchants Incendia powder that, when cast upon the sacred fire of life where the dead are buried, calls Arikara forth so that she may be slain and stripped of her hide.",al={"arikara skin origin","where did arikara serpent skin come from","who made arikara skin"},it="origin",add="d099bc06"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the skin mark a clash between ancient myths and current leadership. Magatha Grimtotem's claims about Cairne Bloodhoof leave the tribes uneasy.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know enchanted powder cast on a sacred fire can force an ancestral spirit-beast into the physical realm."},kw={"arikara","cairne bloodhoof","darkcloud pinnacle","incendia powder","motega firemane","serpent skin","whitereach post"},rel={"quest:5088","npc:motega-firemane","item:incendia-powder","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:whitereach-post","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","quest:5062","zone:thousandneedles"},src={"Arikara Serpent Skin","Arikara (quest)"}}
E["item:cenarion-lunardust"] = {t="item",n="Cenarion Lunardust",z="thunderbluff",s="Turak Runetotem gives Cenarion Lunardust to young tauren druids on Thunder Bluff. They use it to awaken Lunaclaw at an ancient Moonkin Stone between Mulgore and the Barrens.",h="Turak Runetotem gives Cenarion Lunardust to young tauren druids on Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Rite of Body and Heart",b="Cenarion Lunardust carries the Cenarion Circle’s blessing for druids ready to join the Druids of the Claw. At the Moonkin Stone west of Camp Taurajo, the dust calls Lunaclaw, a sacred beast bound to test each initiate. Defeating the guardian tests strength and resolve. The trial teaches the young druid the strength of body and heart needed to take the form of a bear.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Cenarion Lunardust used for?",a="Sprinkle Cenarion Lunardust over the Moonkin Stone in the hills between Mulgore and the Barrens, west of Camp Taurajo. The dust summons Lunaclaw, whom initiates must defeat to prove their strength.",al={"what does lunardust do","how to use cenarion lunardust","lunardust purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Cenarion Lunardust?",a="Turak Runetotem, the druid trainer on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, gives the dust to tauren druids undertaking the trial of bear form.",al={"who gives lunardust","where to get cenarion lunardust","turak runetotem dust"},it="identity"},{q="What happens if you lose your Cenarion Lunardust?",a="If you lose the dust or fail against Lunaclaw, return to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff for another pouch.",al={"lost lunardust","need more lunardust","where to get another lunardust"},gp=true},{q="Why must a druid face Lunaclaw?",a="A druid faces Lunaclaw, protector of the stone, to test physical strength and inner resolve. By defeating the beast, an aspiring Druid of the Claw learns the lessons of body and heart needed to wield the Great Bear Spirit’s power.",al={"why fight lunaclaw","who is lunaclaw","purpose of lunaclaw"},it="motive"},{q="What is Cenarion Lunardust?",a="Cenarion Lunardust is a sacred powder crafted by the Cenarion druids, entrusted only to initiates who have demonstrated their dedication. When sprinkled upon the ancient Moonkin Stone near the border of the Barrens and Mulgore, the dust's magic summons forth Lunaclaw, testing whether a young druid possesses the strength of body and heart required to walk the path of the Claw.",al={"what is lunardust","cenarion lunardust lore","cenarion dust"},it="identity",add="ca885fb9"},{q="Why does anyone want Cenarion Lunardust?",a="Only aspiring druids seek this dust, as it serves as the key to summoning Lunaclaw at the Moonkin Stone. Without it, the guardian will not appear, leaving an initiate unable to face the trial and claim the spiritual strength needed to become a true Druid of the Claw.",al={"why need lunardust","who wants cenarion lunardust","why use lunardust"},it="why_wanted",add="d52557a0"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you use this dust in the rite of passage that opens the way to bear shapeshifting.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you receive the dust as a young Shu'halo, deepening your bond with the Cenarion Circle’s teachings, nature, and Kalimdor’s wild spirits."},kw={"body and heart","cenarion lunardust","druid of the claw","lunaclaw","lunardust","moonkin stone","turak runetotem"},rel={"quest:6001","npc:turak-runetotem","zone:barrens","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","topic:druid"},src={"Cenarion Lunardust","Body and Heart (Horde)"}}
E["item:cloven-hoof"] = {t="item",n="Cloven Hoof",z="thunderbluff",s="Deep in Thousand Needles, the Galak centaur guard the Cloven Hoof within a sacred flame at Splithoof Hold. Tauren scholars seek to understand the strange energy rising from the relic.",h="Deep in Thousand Needles, the Galak centaur guard the Cloven Hoof within a sacred flame at Splithoof Hold.",sec={{t="A Sacred Centaur Relic",b="At the heart of Splithoof Hold, the Galak centaur keep the Cloven Hoof in an ancient brazier. Magical fire surrounds the relic, and blessed water must quench the flame for a moment before anyone can handle it. The centaur clans are divided and violent, yet their care for the brazier points to a ritual bound to their origins. At Freewind Post, Rau Cliffrunner and other tauren observers hope the strange aura of the hoof will teach them about the centaur who have long troubled Kalimdor's plains.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Cloven Hoof kept?",a="The Cloven Hoof rests in an ancient brazier at the back of Splithoof Hold, a cavern in Splithoof Crag north of Freewind Post. Elite Galak warriors guard it.",al={"cloven hoof location","where to find cloven hoof","splithoof hold relic"},it="place"},{q="Why does Rau Cliffrunner want the Cloven Hoof?",a="Rau Cliffrunner wants to study the Cloven Hoof to learn about centaur origins and magic. He senses strange energy from the relic and hopes it will reveal hidden truths about the hostile clans.",al={"why get cloven hoof","rau cliffrunner quest","who wants cloven hoof"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How is the Cloven Hoof retrieved from the brazier?",a="Magical fire surrounds the Cloven Hoof, so it cannot be taken directly. Pour a phial of special water into the ancient brazier to quench the sacred flame briefly, then take the hoof before the blaze returns.",al={"how to get cloven hoof","douse sacred flame","filled etched phial use"},gp=true},{q="Who are the Galak centaur guarding it?",a="The Galak are a centaur tribe that holds the northern reaches of Thousand Needles. Their stronghold is Splithoof Crag, where they fiercely guard their sacred fire from outsiders.",al={"galak centaur","splithoof crag centaur","who guards the flame"},it="people"},{q="What is the Cloven Hoof?",a="The Cloven Hoof is a mysterious, ancient relic revered by the Galak centaur of Thousand Needles. Encased within an eternal sacred flame deep inside Splithoof Hold, the object emanates a strange, unstudied energy that piques the intense curiosity of tauren researchers.",al={"what is cloven hoof","cloven hoof relic","what is the hoof"},it="identity",add="b52742f5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For generations, the nomadic tauren have endured relentless centaur aggression. Learning the origins and magic of relics like the Cloven Hoof could offer knowledge of their old adversaries.",["class:Shaman"]="Ritual elements can briefly quench magical flames and let the Cloven Hoof be retrieved. Such work calls for careful spiritual study in Kalimdor."},kw={"ancient brazier","cloven hoof","galak","rau cliffrunner","sacred flame","splithoof crag","splithoof hold"},rel={"quest:1195","npc:rau-cliffrunner","subzone:splithoof-hold","subzone:splithoof-crag","subzone:freewind-post","item:filled-etched-phial","topic:centaur"},src={"Cloven Hoof","The Sacred Flame (3)"}}
E["item:deadmire-s-tooth"] = {t="item",n="Deadmire's Tooth",z="thunderbluff",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, Deadmire stalks the murky waters, and his tooth marks an honorable hunt. Melor Stonehoof on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff receives it as proof that the ancient crocolisk's suffering has ended.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, Deadmire stalks the murky waters, and his tooth marks an honorable hunt.",sec={{t="A Trophy of Mercy",b="Tauren hunters on Hunter Rise see the hunt as a bond of balance, reverence, and mercy. Deadmire was once among the most magnificent crocolisks in Dustwallow Marsh. Great age turned his final years to torment, though he kept the fierce spirit of his prime. His massive bones and failing body had become a prison of pain. Deadmire's Tooth gives Melor Stonehoof proof that an honorable hunt has ended the beast's suffering.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Deadmire's Tooth used for?",a="Bring the tooth to Melor Stonehoof on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. It completes the hunt he assigns and proves Deadmire has been given a merciful release.",al={"deadmire tooth turn in","who wants deadmire tooth","what do i do with deadmire tooth"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Where does Deadmire's Tooth come from?",a="Deadmire's Tooth comes from Deadmire, an enormous ancient crocolisk in southern Dustwallow Marsh. He roams the waters east of Tabetha's Farm.",al={"where to get deadmire tooth","who drops deadmire tooth","deadmire location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Melor Stonehoof want Deadmire killed?",a="Melor Stonehoof sees Deadmire as a noble creature enduring terrible pain in old age. The hunt offers mercy, letting the crocolisk's flame pass peacefully instead of leaving him to waste away in torment.",al={"why kill deadmire","melor stonehoof reason","is deadmire evil"},it="motive"},{q="What is Deadmire's Tooth?",a="Deadmire's Tooth is a trophy taken from the jaw of Deadmire, a massive and ancient crocolisk lurking within the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. For hunters guided by the tauren traditions in Thunder Bluff, the tooth serves as physical proof that the mighty beast has been tracked down and granted a merciful end.",al={"deadmires tooth","what is the tooth of deadmire","deadmire tooth info"},it="identity",add="4f19a846"},{q="Why does anyone want Deadmire's Tooth?",a="Melor Stonehoof, a hunter trainer on the Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, asks for the tooth as proof of your hunt. Deadmire lives in constant, agonizing pain due to extreme age and grinding old bones. The tauren revere nature and view mercy as part of a hunter's sacred duty; presenting the tooth assures Melor that you have ended the noble beast's suffering.",al={"why bring deadmires tooth","who wants deadmire tooth","why does melor want the tooth"},it="why_wanted",add="200b2360"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter learning from the mentors of Hunter Rise, you learn that the hunt calls for respect and mercy as well as the pursuit of trophies.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Deadmire's hunt as part of the Earth Mother's cycle of balance. Elderly predators are guided toward peace instead of being left to suffer."},kw={"crocolisk","deadmire","dustwallow","hunter rise","melor stonehoof","thunder bluff","tooth"},rel={"quest:1205","npc:melor-stonehoof","zone:dustwallow","zone:thunderbluff","topic:hunter"},src={"Deadmire's Tooth","Deadmire (quest)"}}
E["item:filled-etched-phial"] = {t="item",n="Filled Etched Phial",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, the tauren seek a dryad phial filled with moonwell water. Its rare spiritual power can quench the eternal flame shielding a sacred centaur relic.",h="In Thunder Bluff, the tauren seek a dryad phial filled with moonwell water.",sec={{t="Moonwell Waters and Dryad Craft",b="To fill the phial, you must enter night elf territory deep in Ashenvale. Dryads around Raynewood Retreat carry the empty vessels, crafted to hold pure restorative draughts. A sacred moonwell near the western bank of the Falfarren River fills the phial with water rich in celestial and nature-bound power. Night elves regard taking it without leave as desecration. The tauren see the water as vital to meeting a threat farther south.",sp=0},{t="A Key to Centaur Sorcery",b="Zangen Stonehoof and Rau Cliffrunner sought this water for the deep ties between dryads and centaur. Both trace their ancestry to Cenarius, and their magic shares a primal resonance. In Thousand Needles, the Galak clan guards an ancient relic behind an unyielding protective flame said to date from the creation of the centaur race. The moonwell water in the dryad phial can pierce and extinguish that ward.",sp=1,bt={"q1195.3"}}},faq={{q="What is inside the Filled Etched Phial?",a="The Filled Etched Phial holds sacred water drawn from a night elf moonwell in Ashenvale, near the Falfarren River. The ornate glass vessel comes from dryads near Raynewood Retreat.",al={"what water is in the phial","what is etched phial filled with"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the tauren need moonwell water?",a="Rau Cliffrunner needs the sanctified water to pierce and extinguish the protective flame guarding the Galak centaur relic in Thousand Needles. Dryads and centaur share ancestry through Cenarius, giving the moonwell water power against the ancient ward.",al={"why moonwell water","why does rau need moonwell water"},sp=1,it="why_wanted",bt={"q1195.3"}},{q="Where does the empty phial come from?",a="Laughing Sisters, dryads who wander the woods around Raynewood Retreat in central Ashenvale, carry the empty phials.",al={"where do i find etched phial","how to get empty phial"},it="origin"},{q="Who do you deliver the Filled Etched Phial to?",a="After you collect the water, take it first to Zangen Stonehoof on the High Rise in Thunder Bluff. He directs you to bring it to Rau Cliffrunner at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",al={"who gets the phial","phial turn in"},it="next_step"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren, securing this water strikes at the Galak centaur, turning Cenarius's shared nature magic against their longtime tribal enemies.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you know the theft of a dryad's phial and the skimming of moonwell water by Horde agents violate Ashenvale's holiest sanctuaries."},kw={"ashenvale","dryad","etched phial","filled etched phial","galak","moonwell","rau cliffrunner","thousand needles","zangen stonehoof"},rel={"quest:1195","npc:zangen-stonehoof","npc:rau-cliffrunner","zone:ashenvale","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:freewind-post","topic:centaur"},src={"Filled Etched Phial","The Sacred Flame (quest)","The Sacred Flame (2)"}}
E["item:flatland-cougar-femur"] = {t="item",n="Flatland Cougar Femur",z="thunderbluff",s="Across Mulgore, cougars prowl the plains, and Maur Raincaller needs one of their bones. A Flatland Cougar Femur is part of the remedy he seeks for a venomous bite.",h="Across Mulgore, cougars prowl the plains, and Maur Raincaller needs one of their bones.",sec={{t="A Remedy for a Venomous Bite",b="Flatland cougars rank among Mulgore's most dangerous native stalkers. They blend into the dry brush, then spring upon unsuspecting prey. Hunters take their pelts and claws for leatherworking and trophies, while their heavy, marrow-rich bones have use in local medicine. Maur Raincaller of Bloodhoof Village suffered a venomous wound from Mazzranache, a monstrous pink strider. He urgently asked for a cougar femur and parts from other local beasts. Crushed or boiled, the bone yields properties for an antitoxin poultice meant to draw fever and necrotic venom from a festering bite.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Flatland Cougar Femur used for?",a="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village needs the femur to make an emergency remedy. The notorious plainstrider Mazzranache bit him, and he needs the marrow and bone to prepare an antitoxin before its virulent venom kills him.",al={"cougar femur use","what is this bone for","femur quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do you obtain a Flatland Cougar Femur?",a="You can gather a Flatland Cougar Femur from flatland cougars roaming Mulgore's central and southern plains. They prowl near the hillsides and through the tall grasses around Bloodhoof Village.",al={"where to find femur","cougar femur location","which mobs drop it"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why would Maur Raincaller need a cougar bone specifically?",a="Tauren herbalists and shamans use the dense bones and marrow of predatory animals in traditional salves and tinctures. They believe the strength and resilience of Mulgore's apex predators provide the restorative foundation needed to neutralize potent toxins.",al={"why cougar bone","why femur"}},{q="Who is Maur Raincaller?",a="Maur Raincaller lives in Bloodhoof Village. After wandering the plains, he ran afoul of Mazzranache, a legendary strider his grandfather once fought, and barely escaped with an infected, venomous bite to the shoulder.",al={"maur raincaller","who needs the bone"}},{q="What is a Flatland Cougar Femur?",a="It is a sturdy leg bone harvested from the predatory flatland cougars that roam the plains of Mulgore. Dense and resilient, bones like these are often sought by tribal healers and shamans to prepare traditional salves, poultices, and medicinal remedies.",al={"what is flatland cougar femur","flatland cougar femur item","cougar femur what is it"},it="identity",add="cc87b9fc"},{q="Where does a Flatland Cougar Femur come from?",a="It is obtained directly from flatland cougars, the lean predators native to the grasslands of Mulgore. Unlike crafted tools or brewed draughts, this is a raw natural trophy gathered by hunters tracking the wild beasts across the rolling plains.",al={"flatland cougar femur origin","where to get flatland cougar femur","who drops cougar femur"},it="origin",add="47eeaceb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the tauren of Mulgore, hunting flatland cougars tests vigilance and provides vital materials for traditional plains remedies.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you need sharp eyes to track flatland cougars through Mulgore's swaying brush, and the hunt tests your skill at bringing down a fellow predator cleanly."},kw={"bloodhoof village","femur","flatland cougar","maur raincaller","mazzranache","mulgore"},rel={"npc:maur-raincaller","quest:766","subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:mulgore","item:plainstrider-scale","item:prairie-wolf-heart","item:swoop-gizzard"},src={"Flatland Cougar Femur","Mazzranache (Classic)"}}
E["item:horn-of-arra-chea"] = {t="item",n="Horn of Arra'chea",z="thunderbluff",s="Across Mulgore, Arra'chea roams while Cairne Bloodhoof calls young hunters to prove their worth. The kodo's horn confirms a hunter can track prey and provide for the Shu'halo.",h="Across Mulgore, Arra'chea roams while Cairne Bloodhoof calls young hunters to prove their worth.",sec={{t="A Chieftain's Test",b="Passing the Rites of the Earthmother earns a youth a place atop Thunder Bluff, but High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof still expects his people to prove their worth. For the tauren, the hunt binds identity to lasting harmony with the land. Cairne sends young hunters to track Arra'chea, a massive, solitary kodo bull roaming the grasslands below. Taking the bull's horn shows mastery of tracking prey across vast distances.",sp=0},{t="Providing for the Tribe",b="Bringing Arra'chea's horn to Thunder Bluff does more than display strength; it helps sustain the community. Tauren use every part of a slain beast. The trophy tells the High Chieftain where Arra'chea fell, so gathering parties can go down into the plains and harvest the kodo's thick hide and rich meat for the fledgling capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Horn of Arra'chea?",a="The Horn of Arra'chea is taken from Arra'chea, a powerful, elusive kodo roaming Mulgore's plains. Hunters bring it to Cairne Bloodhoof as a rite of passage and proof of their tracking skill.",al={"horn of arrachea","arrachea horn","what is this horn"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Arra'chea?",a="Arra'chea is a renowned kodo bull that circles the grasslands northeast of Thunder Bluff. His strength and wide migratory route make him a formidable quarry for hunters proving their worth to the tribe.",al={"arrachea","who is arrachea","arrachea lore"}},{q="Why does Cairne Bloodhoof ask for this trophy?",a="Cairne Bloodhoof asks for the trophy because he expects his people to keep proving their worth. Tracking and felling Arra'chea shows a hunter's dedication to the traditions of the Earthmother and provides resources for the community.",al={"why cairne want horn","cairne arrachea","rites of the earthmother horn"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What happens to the rest of the beast after it is killed?",a="Tauren use every part of the hunted animal. Once the horn confirms the kill, Cairne sends a gathering party down into Mulgore to collect the hide and meat for Thunder Bluff.",al={"arrachea meat","tauren hunting tradition","arrachea carcass"}},{q="Where does the Horn of Arra'chea come from, and who made it?",a="The horn is not a crafted artifact, but a natural trophy taken from Arra'chea, a mighty kodo that roams the plains of Mulgore below Thunder Bluff. To claim it, a hunter must track down the great beast on the open grasslands and fell it in honorable combat.",al={"origin horn of arrachea","where did horn of arrachea come from","who made horn of arrachea"},it="origin",add="0ff92160"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, presenting Arra'chea's horn to High Chieftain Cairne marks a rite of passage and proves your readiness to sustain and defend your people atop Thunder Bluff.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking Arra'chea's circular path across Mulgore tests the stalking and wilderness survival skills valued in a hunter."},kw={"arra'chea","cairne bloodhoof","horn of arra'chea","kodo","mulgore","rites of the earthmother","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:cairne-bloodhoof","quest:763","zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","topic:hunter","quest:421"},src={"Horn of Arra'chea","Rites of the Earthmother (3)"}}
E["item:incendia-agave"] = {t="item",n="Incendia Agave",z="thunderbluff",s="Beneath Darkcloud Pinnacle, Incendia Agave grows in the Boiling Pool. A skilled shaman can enchant it to kindle the sacred fire of life.",h="Beneath Darkcloud Pinnacle, Incendia Agave grows in the Boiling Pool.",sec={{t="A Rare Desert Herb",b="In Thousand Needles, Incendia Agave grows in and around the waters of the Boiling Pool, beneath Darkcloud Pinnacle. Wandering steam elementals guard the scarce plant, making it difficult to harvest. Though it grows underwater, the plant holds natural elements suited to rituals of flame.",sp=0},{t="The Sacred Fire",b="Tauren ritualists cannot kindle the dormant sacred fire of life with ordinary sparks. Elder Magatha Grimtotem, on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, can enchant harvested bushels of Incendia Agave into a mystical powder. The powder lights the ceremonial brazier used to summon the vengeful wind serpent Arikara.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does Incendia Agave grow?",a="Incendia Agave grows in and around the lake at the Boiling Pool beneath Darkcloud Pinnacle in northern Thousand Needles. Much of it lies submerged along the lakebed.",al={"where find agave","incendia agave location","where is agave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Incendia Agave used for?",a="Ten bushels of Incendia Agave are gathered and made into ritual powder. Magatha Grimtotem enchants it in Thunder Bluff to light the sacred fire of life and summon Arikara.",al={"incendia agave purpose","why gather agave","what does agave do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who can enchant the Incendia Agave?",a="Magatha Grimtotem, an influential shaman on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, has the ritual knowledge to enchant Incendia Agave.",al={"who enchants agave","magatha agave","who turns agave into powder"},it="people"},{q="What threats surround the Incendia Agave?",a="Hostile steam elementals roam the waters and shores of the Boiling Pool. They are exceptionally resistant to frost and fire spells.",al={"agave hazards","what guards agave","boiling pool dangers"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="What is Incendia Agave?",a="Incendia Agave is an exceptionally rare, spiky herb found thriving only around and within the steaming waters of the Boiling Pool in Thousand Needles. Despite growing in the lakeside depths, it harbors potent latent fiery properties, making it an essential component for rituals requiring elemental power once properly refined by a skilled shaman.",al={"what is incendia agave","incendia agave plant","what kind of plant is incendia agave"},it="identity",add="d4005c78"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can use raw elemental craft to turn the aquatic plant into powder potent enough to kindle sacred ritual flames.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, your tracking sense helps you find Incendia Agave's spiky clumps along the murky floor of the Boiling Pool."},kw={"arikara","boiling pool","darkcloud pinnacle","incendia agave","magatha grimtotem","sacred fire","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:5062","quest:5088","npc:magatha-grimtotem","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","zone:thousandneedles","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:elder-rise","topic:shaman"},src={"Incendia Agave","Sacred Fire"}}
E["item:incendia-powder"] = {t="item",n="Incendia Powder",z="thunderbluff",s="On Thunder Bluff, Incendia Powder is prepared to call a sacred spirit into the open. Magatha Grimtotem enchants it for use at Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles.",h="On Thunder Bluff, Incendia Powder is prepared to call a sacred spirit into the open.",sec={{t="A Spark of Summoning",b="Incendia Powder carries shamanic magic to the sacred fire atop Darkcloud Pinnacle. Magatha Grimtotem entrusts it to travelers on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. Scattered across the consecrated brazier where the dead are laid to rest, the powder calls forth Arikara, a vengeful winged serpent.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Portents",b="Magatha Grimtotem shaped the rites behind Incendia Powder. She believed changes in tauren ways had stirred ancient spirits to hunt High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, so she enchanted the powder to draw the apparition into the open and destroy it. The powder brings forth the fierce serpent, but the encounter leaves questions about why Arikara was stirred.",sp=1,bt={"q4821.5"}}},faq={{q="What is Incendia Powder used for?",a="At Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles, Incendia Powder is scattered into the sacred fire of life. The flame then calls forth Arikara, the vengeful spirit serpent.",al={"incendia powder purpose","why do i need incendia powder","what does incendia powder do"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who prepared the enchantment on the powder?",a="Magatha Grimtotem enchanted the gathered Incendia agave into refined powder on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Motega Firemane of Whitereach Post had sent word of Arikara.",al={"who made incendia powder","who enchanted incendia powder"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the powder need to be used?",a="Scatter the powder into the sacred fire pit on a solitary burial-needle spire within Darkcloud Pinnacle, high above the salt canyons of Thousand Needles.",al={"incendia powder location","where to throw incendia powder","where to use incendia powder"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why was summoning Arikara necessary?",a="Magatha Grimtotem fears that changes in tauren lore have angered Arikara and that the serpent may be stalking Cairne Bloodhoof. She asks that Arikara be summoned and slain before Cairne is harmed.",al={"why summon arikara","why fight arikara"},it="motive"},{q="What is Incendia Powder?",a="Incendia Powder is a refined, purified reagent steeped in ritual magic. When scattered onto the sacred fire of life atop Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles, its woven enchantment acts as a beacon that draws out Arikara, the vengeful wind serpent spirit.",al={"what is incendia powder","incendia powder lore","what is the powder"},it="identity",add="53c7ed7b"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see how elemental flame and spiritual warding join to awaken slumbering ancestral beings.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know ritual powders can kindle burial fires, where sacred tradition and the defense of tribal leadership meet."},kw={"arikara","darkcloud pinnacle","incendia powder","motega firemane","sacred fire of life","thousand needles","whitereach post"},rel={"quest:5088","npc:motega-firemane","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:whitereach-post","item:arikara-serpent-skin","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren"},src={"Incendia Powder","Arikara (quest)"}}
E["item:lydon-s-toxin"] = {t="item",n="Lydon's Toxin",z="thunderbluff",s="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon has made a toxin to disrupt the Venture Company's logging in the Stonetalon Mountains. Horde adventurers carry it to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff, who must devise a way to spread it.",h="In Tarren Mill, Apothecary Lydon has made a toxin to disrupt the Venture Company's logging in the Stonetalon...",sec={{t="A Royal Apothecary Solution",b="Apothecary Lydon made the toxin in the Hillsbrad Foothills to fight the Venture Company loggers despoiling the Stonetalon Mountains. He says the compound is lethal on contact and may spread from one target to another. Before it can be used against the goblins near Windshear Crag, the mixture must cross continents to Thunder Bluff. Apothecary Zamah, the Royal Apothecary Society's representative there, needs the raw toxin to devise a wide-dispersal device called the Toxic Fogger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Lydon's Toxin used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon made the toxin to disrupt the Venture Company's work around Windshear Crag. It is lethal on contact and may spread among the goblin laborers.",al={"lydon toxin purpose","what does the toxin do","why make lydon's toxin"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Lydon is a Royal Apothecary Society member stationed in Tarren Mill, in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He makes virulent poisons and experimental compounds for Forsaken aims.",al={"who is lydon","apothecary lydon","lydon creator"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the toxin need to go to Thunder Bluff?",a="Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff needs the toxin because it has no practical way to be spread widely. She studies regional flora and coordinates Society efforts in Kalimdor, and adapts the mixture into a portable fogging device.",al={"why thunder bluff","why bring toxin to zamah","apothecary zamah purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What happens after Zamah receives the toxin?",a="Apothecary Zamah turns the toxin into a pressurized aerosol device called the Toxic Fogger. An operative can use it to spread the toxin through the Venture Company's encampment.",al={"toxic fogger creation","what does zamah do with the toxin"},it="next_step"},{q="What is Lydon's Toxin?",a="Lydon's Toxin is a virulent alchemical concoction formulated by Apothecary Lydon of the Royal Apothecary Society. Engineered specifically for use against the goblin-run Venture Company, the substance is designed to produce devastating and potentially contagious results when deployed against enemy ranks.",al={"what is lydons toxin","lydon toxin","about lydons toxin"},it="identity",add="73882111"},{q="Why does anyone want Lydon's Toxin?",a="The Forsaken apothecaries and their Horde allies want the toxin to eradicate the encroaching Venture Company operatives. Apothecary Zamah requires Lydon's brew so she can construct an effective delivery mechanism, allowing the Horde to disperse its lethal, contagious effects across enemy worksites.",al={"why want lydons toxin","why is the toxin needed","purpose of lydons toxin"},it="why_wanted",add="105322cc"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="The transport of Lydon's Toxin shows how far the Royal Apothecary Society's network reaches. It coordinates field research between Lordaeron and Kalimdor to show the Forsaken's usefulness to their allies.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren welcome help against the Venture Company's destruction of nature, but the Royal Apothecary Society's chemical methods test their shamanic sensibilities."},kw={"apothecary lydon","apothecary zamah","lydon's toxin","royal apothecary society","thunder bluff","toxic fogger","venture company"},rel={"quest:1067","quest:853","item:toxic-fogger","zone:thunderbluff","topic:venture-company"},src={"Lydon's Toxin","Return to Thunder Bluff (1)"}}
E["item:nightmare-shard"] = {t="item",n="Nightmare Shard",z="thunderbluff",s="In the Wailing Caverns, a glowing shard bears a taint Falla Sagewind cannot ignore. She binds its pure, disturbed essence of the Emerald Dream into the Nightmare Shard and sends it to senior druids for a warning kept from others.",h="In the Wailing Caverns, a glowing shard bears a taint Falla Sagewind cannot ignore.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Vision",b="Deep in the Wailing Caverns, Falla Sagewind examines a mysterious glowing shard and finds its energy darker than she expected. It reflects an unnatural affliction in the Emerald Dream, like a waking nightmare. Falla binds this tainted essence into the Nightmare Shard and orders it carried without delay to elder leaders of the Cenarion Circle.",sp=0},{t="Hushed Omens",b="When the Nightmare Shard reaches Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise or Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus, each looks into its depths with dismay. The vision unsettles them and confirms their quiet suspicions that something has gone terribly wrong within the Dream. Fearing panic among the public, the druids take the shard and warn the courier to speak no further of what they saw.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Nightmare Shard?",a="Falla Sagewind entrusts the Nightmare Shard to a courier after examining a glowing fragment brought from the Wailing Caverns. It holds the pure, disturbed essence of the Emerald Dream, with a dark, corruptive vision instead of peaceful nature energies.",al={"what is nightmare shard","nightmare shard lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who created the Nightmare Shard?",a="Falla Sagewind gives the Nightmare Shard to a courier after examining a glowing fragment brought from the Wailing Caverns. She recognizes its corruption and charges the courier to carry it directly to senior druids for study.",al={"who made the nightmare shard","where does the shard come from"},it="origin"},{q="Why are the druid leaders so alarmed by it?",a="Looking into the shard, Hamuul Runetotem and Mathrengyl Bearwalker see a nightmare twisting the Emerald Dream. Fearing danger and public panic, they silence further discussion and keep the matter among senior members of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"why is hamuul worried","why does mathrengyl hide the shard"},sp=1,it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the shard need to be delivered?",a="Horde adventurers are instructed to carry the shard to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Alliance travelers carry it to Mathrengyl Bearwalker within the Cenarion Circle in Darnassus.",al={"who do i bring the shard to","nightmare shard turn in"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, the shard reveals that the Emerald Dream is no longer untouched by corruption. It confirms their concerns over Naralex's fate in the Wailing Caverns.",["faction:Horde"]="For Horde travelers, the shard brings grave news to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, where Hamuul Runetotem works to anchor the tauren's place in the wider Cenarion brotherhood."},kw={"emerald dream","falla sagewind","glowing shard","hamuul runetotem","in nightmares","mathrengyl bearwalker","nightmare shard","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:3369","quest:6981","npc:falla-sagewind","npc:mathrengyl-bearwalker","quest:1489","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:emerald-dream","subzone:elder-rise"},src={"Nightmare Shard","In Nightmares (Horde)","In Nightmares (Alliance)"}}
E["item:pendant-of-the-sea-lion"] = {t="item",n="Pendant of the Sea Lion",z="thunderbluff",s="At the Shrine of Remulos, druids join the Pendant of the Sea Lion's two halves. The completed talisman marks an initiate's readiness to learn an aquatic form.",h="At the Shrine of Remulos, druids join the Pendant of the Sea Lion's two halves.",sec={{t="A Token of the Deep",b="A druid must master the water's dangers to claim the sea lion's aquatic aspect. The pendant has two halves, one embodying the agility to slip past aquatic predators, the other the endurance to withstand prolonged submersion. At the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade, the pieces are joined into one.",sp=0},{t="Proof of Mastery",b="After the pendant is forged, an initiate brings it to an elder mentor. Turak Runetotem waits on the rises of Thunder Bluff, while Mathrengyl Bearwalker is in Darnassus. The talisman proves the initiate has completed trials under Dendrite Starblaze, allowing the elder to teach the secrets of taking an aquatic form.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Pendant of the Sea Lion?",a="The pendant proves a druid initiate has completed trials of aquatic agility and endurance and is ready to learn an aquatic form.",al={"what does pendant of the sea lion do","sea lion pendant use","why get pendant of the sea lion"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the pendant assembled?",a="The pendant's two halves, one for agility and one for endurance, are joined at the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade.",al={"how to make sea lion pendant","where combine pendant halves"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who do I present the pendant to in Thunder Bluff?",a="In Thunder Bluff, you present the completed pendant to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.",al={"who takes pendant thunder bluff","turak runetotem pendant","horde aquatic form turn in"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Can night elves also earn this pendant?",a="Yes. Night elf druids undergo the same trial in Moonglade, then bring the assembled pendant to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus.",al={"alliance sea lion pendant","darnassus sea lion pendant"}},{q="What is the Pendant of the Sea Lion?",a="The Pendant of the Sea Lion is a sacred druidic talisman symbolizing mastery over the water. It embodies the agility required to evade dangerous aquatic predators alongside the deep endurance necessary to remain submerged without surfacing. Druids carry this joined relic as tangible evidence that they understand the wild balance of nature before adopting an aquatic aspect.",al={"what is pendant of the sea lion","pendant sea lion info","sea lion pendant lore"},it="identity",add="203d1c94"},{q="Where does the Pendant of the Sea Lion come from, and who made it?",a="The talisman is forged by young druids undergoing the Trial of the Sea Lion. It is created by retrieving two separate pieces—the Half Pendant of Aquatic Agility and the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance—from trial locations and bringing them together before the Shrine of Remulos in Moonglade, uniting the aspects into a single sacred emblem.",al={"who made pendant of the sea lion","origin of sea lion pendant","how is the pendant of the sea lion created"},it="origin",add="ad633d46"},{q="Why does anyone want the Pendant of the Sea Lion?",a="Druidic mentors demand to see the completed pendant as undeniable proof of your training. In Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem requires the medallion to verify that you met Moonglade's trials before he will impart the secrets of the aquatic form. Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade also inspects the joined relic to confirm the trial's completion.",al={"why want pendant of the sea lion","who wants the sea lion pendant","why show pendant of the sea lion"},it="why_wanted",add="384283bf"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, assembling the pendant marks a milestone in your training. It lets you breathe underwater and swim swiftly as a sea lion.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren walking the path of the Cenarion Circle, you honor your ancestors and Moonglade's teachings when you bring the pendant to Turak Runetotem."},kw={"aquatic form","dendrite starblaze","mathrengyl bearwalker","moonglade","pendant of the sea lion","remulos","turak runetotem"},rel={"quest:31","quest:5921","npc:turak-runetotem","npc:mathrengyl-bearwalker","npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:remulos","topic:druid","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Pendant of the Sea Lion","Aquatic Form (Horde)","Aquatic Form (Alliance)"}}
E["item:plainstrider-scale"] = {t="item",n="Plainstrider Scale",z="thunderbluff",s="Across Mulgore, Plainstrider Scale is sought for a remedy Maur Raincaller prepares in Bloodhoof Village. The tough scale helps counter a spreading infection.",h="Across Mulgore, Plainstrider Scale is sought for a remedy Maur Raincaller prepares in Bloodhoof Village.",sec={{t="A Rare Ingredient",b="Plainstriders roam Mulgore with tough scales covering their powerful legs. The scales protect them, though only some are firm enough to grind for folk remedies.",sp=0},{t="A Remedy for a Venomous Bite",b="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village was bitten in the shoulder by Mazzranache, a legendary strider with demonic red eyes and a venomous bite. The wound left Maur delirious with fever. To cleanse the spreading infection before it proves fatal, he needs a Plainstrider Scale, a wolf heart, a cougar femur, and a swoop gizzard.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Plainstrider Scale used for?",a="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village needs a Plainstrider Scale for a remedy. He combines it with parts from other Mulgore predators to treat the infected wound Mazzranache inflicted with its venomous bite.",al={"what does plainstrider scale do","plainstrider scale use","why need plainstrider scale"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do you find a Plainstrider Scale?",a="You find Plainstrider Scales on wild plainstriders roaming Mulgore's open grasslands.",al={"where to get plainstrider scale","how to get plainstrider scale","plainstrider scale location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why is Maur Raincaller infected?",a="Maur Raincaller was bitten in the shoulder by Mazzranache, a tallstrider with crimson eyes and a venomous bite. The wound left him with a worsening fever and delirium.",al={"how did maur get sick","why is maur sick","mazzranache bite"},it="motive"},{q="What other ingredients does Maur need for his remedy?",a="Maur needs a Plainstrider Scale, a Prairie Wolf Heart, a Flatland Cougar Femur, and a Swoop Gizzard for his remedy.",al={"maur raincaller ingredients","cure for mazzranache","mazzranache quest items"}},{q="What is a Plainstrider Scale?",a="It is a tough, specialized scale harvested from the tallstriders roaming the windswept grasslands of Mulgore. While birds and striders are known primarily for their plumage and sharp beaks, their rugged legs and feet bear coarse, hardened scales capable of withstanding the rough plains. Shamans and herbalists value these rare, dense scales for their protective traits when preparing specialized poultices and cures.",al={"what is plainstrider scale","plainstrider scale","plainstrider scales"},it="identity",add="95a4c3dd"},{q="Where does a Plainstrider Scale come from?",a="It is a natural animal part taken directly from the wild plainstriders that roam Mulgore. Nobody crafts it; hunters harvest it from the legs of fallen tallstriders across the plains, gathering only the sturdiest scales for use in medicinal preparations.",al={"plainstrider scale source","where does plainstrider scale come from","who made plainstrider scale"},it="origin",add="d7ded3c8"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you learn to gather remedies from the land and use the plains' wildlife to sustain your tribe."},kw={"bloodhoof village","maur raincaller","mazzranache","mulgore","plainstrider","remedy","scale","tallstrider"},rel={"quest:766","npc:maur-raincaller","subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:mulgore","item:prairie-wolf-heart","item:flatland-cougar-femur","item:swoop-gizzard"},src={"Plainstrider Scale","Mazzranache (Classic)"}}
E["item:prairie-wolf-heart"] = {t="item",n="Prairie Wolf Heart",z="thunderbluff",s="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village needs a Prairie Wolf Heart for a remedy against venom.",h="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village needs a Prairie Wolf Heart for a remedy against venom.",sec={{t="A Remedy for a Venomous Bite",b="Maur Raincaller lives in Bloodhoof Village and is suffering from the venom of Mazzranache, the legendary plainstrider. The bite brings fever and threatens to spread poison through him. Maur seeks the heart of a prairie wolf, along with cougar bone and bird gizzard, for a traditional plains remedy meant to stop the infection before delirium proves fatal.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a Prairie Wolf Heart used for?",a="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village needs a Prairie Wolf Heart for a folk remedy. He combines it with other animal parts to treat the venomous bite Mazzranache gave him.",al={"wolf heart use","why get wolf heart","prairie wolf heart purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does one obtain a Prairie Wolf Heart?",a="Prairie wolves, prairie wolf alphas, and prairie stalkers hunt across Mulgore’s plains, and their bodies provide the heart.",al={"wolf heart location","who drops wolf heart","how to find prairie wolf heart"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why does Maur Raincaller need animal organs to treat his wound?",a="Mazzranache’s infected bite brings fever and delirium. Maur relies on tauren plains remedies made with a wolf heart, cougar femur, plainstrider scale, and swoop gizzard to cleanse the infection before it proves lethal.",al={"why wolf heart for medicine","maur remedy"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Can any wolf heart be used for the remedy?",a="Maur asks for a wolf heart. The heart for his remedy comes from prairie wolves, prairie wolf alphas, or prairie stalkers on Mulgore’s plains.",al={"any wolf heart","which wolves drop it"},gp=true},{q="What is a Prairie Wolf Heart?",a="A Prairie Wolf Heart is the harvested organ of the predatory wolves that prowl the rolling plains of Mulgore. While it holds little common trade value, the vitality of a wild beast's heart makes it a prized ingredient in traditional tauren medicine. It serves as one of several potent reagents required to brew remedies capable of purging virulent natural poisons and deep infections.",al={"what is prairie wolf heart","prairie wolf heart","about prairie wolf heart"},it="identity",add="ee1c9772"},{q="Where does a Prairie Wolf Heart come from?",a="The heart is taken directly from the wild prairie wolves, prairie wolf alphas, and prairie stalkers native to the grassy plateaus of Mulgore. It is a natural biological organ harvested from a slain predator rather than an object crafted by mortal hands.",al={"where does prairie wolf heart come from","prairie wolf heart origin","who made prairie wolf heart"},it="origin",add="1392571f"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know that animal parts can help make practical cures for survival in Mulgore’s wilds.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you learn to track the wolf packs that hunt Mulgore’s plains and understand the beasts that live there."},kw={"bloodhoof village","maur raincaller","mazzranache","mulgore","prairie stalker","prairie wolf heart","wolf heart"},rel={"npc:maur-raincaller","quest:766","subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:mulgore","item:flatland-cougar-femur","item:plainstrider-scale","item:swoop-gizzard"},src={"Prairie Wolf Heart","Mazzranache (Classic)"}}
E["item:rendered-spores"] = {t="item",n="Rendered Spores",z="thunderbluff",s="Across the Barrens, Rendered Spores are being rushed from Apothecary Helbrim to Thunder Bluff before they decay. Apothecary Zamah must stabilize the emulsion beneath the city.",h="Across the Barrens, Rendered Spores are being rushed from Apothecary Helbrim to Thunder Bluff before they...",sec={{t="A Volatile Mixture",b="Apothecary Helbrim makes Rendered Spores from fungal spores gathered near the Barrens’ damp oases. He processes the strange spores into an active chemical emulsion, but it is unstable. After forty-five minutes, it breaks down and becomes useless for scientific study.",sp=0},{t="Delivery to the Pools of Vision",b="Apothecary Helbrim cannot finish refining the emulsion at his remote outpost. It must reach his Forsaken colleague, Apothecary Zamah, beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff. In the Pools of Vision, Zamah has the equipment and reagents to reseal and finish processing the spores for the Royal Apothecary Society.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Rendered Spores used for?",a="Apothecary Helbrim turns fungal matter into an emulsion for the Royal Apothecary Society to study. In Thunder Bluff, Apothecary Zamah uses it to continue investigating the strange growths spreading across the Barrens.",al={"purpose of rendered spores","what does zamah do with spores","why rendered spores"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does the emulsion have a time limit?",a="The emulsion Apothecary Helbrim makes is volatile and starts to decay as soon as it is mixed. Its active potency lasts only forty-five minutes, so it must be carried across the plains to Thunder Bluff before it becomes inert.",al={"why are rendered spores timed","why do spores expire","rendered spores duration"}},{q="Who created these spores?",a="Apothecary Helbrim, a Forsaken researcher at the Crossroads in the Barrens, turns raw fungal spores gathered near the oases into an unstable liquid compound.",al={"who made rendered spores","who renders the spores","helbrim spores"},it="origin"},{q="Where does the mixture need to go?",a="The mixture must reach Apothecary Zamah, who lives in the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital.",al={"where to bring rendered spores","zamah location","pools of vision location"},it="purpose"},{q="What are Rendered Spores?",a="Rendered Spores are the processed extract of strange fungal growths harvested across the Barrens. Apothecary Helbrim boiled and rendered the raw spores down into a volatile, unstable liquid emulsion, carefully preparing the mixture for further alchemical study by the Royal Apothecary Society.",al={"what is rendered spores","rendered spores info","what are the rendered spores"},it="identity",add="7897c588"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you are part of a people whose Royal Apothecary Society seeks biological compounds across Kalimdor to aid the Forsaken. Fast couriers link field researchers like Helbrim with specialists like Zamah.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Forsaken apothecaries experimenting on strange Barrens flora inside the sacred Pools of Vision. Their work reflects the uneasy, practical alliance forged within Thunder Bluff."},kw={"apothecary helbrim","apothecary zamah","barrens","crossroads","emulsion","pools of vision","rendered spores","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:apothecary-helbrim","quest:853","quest:848","subzone:pools-of-vision","subzone:spirit-rise","zone:thunderbluff","zone:barrens"},src={"Rendered Spores","Apothecary Zamah (quest)"}}
E["item:steelsnap-s-rib"] = {t="item",n="Steelsnap's Rib",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thousand Needles, Steelsnap's Rib marks the end of a feared hyena's reign. Melor Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff wants the bone brought to Hunter Rise as proof that Steelsnap has been slain.",h="In Thousand Needles, Steelsnap's Rib marks the end of a feared hyena's reign.",sec={{t="A Hunt Outside the Blessing",b="Tauren hunts often seek food, honor, or harmony with nature. Steelsnap is different. The alpha hyena roams the canyon floor south of Camp E'thok in Thousand Needles, terrorizing peaceful wildlife and rallying lesser predators to bloodshed. Hunt master Melor Stonehoof, on Hunter Rise, marks Steelsnap for death. He asks for the hyena's rib as proof the tyrant is slain and the canyon cleansed of its blight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Steelsnap's Rib used for?",a="Bring the rib to Melor Stonehoof on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. It proves Steelsnap has been defeated.",al={"steelsnap rib quest","who wants steelsnaps rib","what do i do with steelsnaps rib"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where can I find Steelsnap to get the rib?",a="Steelsnap roams the canyon floor in northwestern Thousand Needles, south of Camp E'thok. Loyal packmates often flank him.",al={"steelsnap location","where is steelsnap","find steelsnap"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Melor Stonehoof want Steelsnap killed?",a="Melor considers Steelsnap an unnatural tyrant outside the Earthmother's blessing. The hyena spreads bloodshed and fear among peaceful beasts, unlike predators that hunt for survival.",al={"why kill steelsnap","melor stonehoof motive","steelsnap lore"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Melor Stonehoof?",a="Melor Stonehoof is a veteran tauren hunter on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. He sends aspiring trackers after dangerous beasts across Kalimdor.",al={"who is melor","melor stonehoof location","hunter rise melor"},it="identity"},{q="What is Steelsnap's Rib?",a="It is a heavy bone taken from the carcass of Steelsnap, a notoriously savage hyena that terrorizes the canyons of Thousand Needles. Rather than useful crafting material or meat, it serves as undeniable physical proof that the vicious beast has been put down.",al={"steelsnaps rib what is it","what is steelsnap rib","steelsnap bone"},it="identity",add="27efcb35"},{q="Where does Steelsnap's Rib come from?",a="The rib comes directly from the remains of Steelsnap, an abnormally fierce hyena roaming the arid flats of Thousand Needles south of the Barrens. To claim it, a hunter must hunt down the beast and defeat both Steelsnap and his pack.",al={"where do you get steelsnaps rib","origin of steelsnaps rib","who drops steelsnap rib"},it="origin",add="57ae26da"},{q="Why does Melor Stonehoof want Steelsnap's Rib?",a="Melor Stonehoof asks for the rib as physical proof of Steelsnap's death. Unlike hunts undertaken for food or honor, Melor sends hunters to eradicate Steelsnap because the beast exists outside the Earthmother's blessing, spreading bloodshed and fear among more peaceful creatures. Returning with the bone confirms the canyon has been cleansed of that taint.",al={"why bring steelsnap rib to melor","why does melor need the rib","why collect steelsnaps rib"},it="why_wanted",add="4a69fb67"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, tracking down Steelsnap tests your skill against a dangerous pack leader and helps cull a threat to the wild's balance.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, bringing back Steelsnap's Rib fulfills your duty to the Earthmother by purging a cruel creature that taints the sacred balance."},kw={"camp e'thok","hunter rise","hyena","melor stonehoof","steelsnap","steelsnap's rib","thousand needles","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:1131","npc:melor-stonehoof","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:hunter-rise","subzone:camp-e-thok","zone:thunderbluff","quest:1130","topic:hunter"},src={"Steelsnap's Rib","Steelsnap (quest)"}}
E["item:swoop-gizzard"] = {t="item",n="Swoop Gizzard",z="thunderbluff",s="Across Mulgore, swoops soar as predatory birds, and their gizzards go into traditional remedies for deadly toxins.",h="Across Mulgore, swoops soar as predatory birds, and their gizzards go into traditional remedies for deadly...",sec={{t="A Rare Folk Ingredient",b="Swoops hunt across Mulgore’s plains and mesas, with keen eyes and a taste for scavenging. Tauren use their feathers and meat in daily life, while herbalists and healers prize their internal organs, especially the gizzard. Dense and muscular, it helps counter venomous bites and festering infections when combined with cougar bones and wolf hearts.",sp=0},{t="A Remedy for Mazzranache's Bite",b="In Bloodhoof Village, Maur Raincaller tends the wound Mazzranache left on his shoulder. The legendary plainstrider’s venom drives Maur into delirium as the poison creeps through him. To make a poultice that can expel the lethal venom, Maur needs a swoop gizzard, a prairie wolf heart, a flatland cougar femur, and a plainstrider scale.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a swoop gizzard used for?",a="Maur Raincaller in Bloodhoof Village needs a swoop gizzard as an essential ingredient in a remedy. Mixed with three other animal parts, it forms a cure for the venomous infection left by Mazzranache, the vicious plainstrider.",al={"swoop gizzard use","why do i need swoop gizzard","swoop organ purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where do swoop gizzards come from?",a="Swoop gizzards come from the swoops gliding over Mulgore’s plains, including standard swoops, wiry swoops, and taloned swoops.",al={"where to find swoop gizzard","what drops swoop gizzard","swoop hunting"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Maur Raincaller need this specific part?",a="Mazzranache bit Maur, and the unusually ferocious plainstrider’s venom brings raging fevers and nightmares. Tauren folk medicine uses potent animal parts, including a gizzard, to counter the toxins in Maur’s veins.",al={"maur remedy","why a gizzard","cure for mazzranache"},it="motive"},{q="Is the gizzard used for anything other than Maur's cure?",a="No. Beyond Maur Raincaller’s specialized folk remedy in Bloodhoof Village, swoop gizzards have no standard culinary, alchemical, or crafting use.",al={"other uses for swoop gizzard","cooking swoop gizzard","alchemy swoop gizzard"},it="purpose"},{q="What is a Swoop Gizzard?",a="A Swoop Gizzard is an internal organ harvested from the predatory birds known as swoops that glide above the plains of Mulgore. Like many avian digestive organs, it helps process tough prey. In traditional tauren medicine, such potent, specialized animal parts are valued for their raw natural qualities and used as ingredients in herbal remedies and restorative concoctions.",al={"what is swoop gizzard","swoop gizzard item","what is a swoop gizzard"},it="identity",add="8f6be1e3"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter or shaman, gathering these parts honors the tradition of using Mulgore’s wildlife to sustain and heal the tribe."},kw={"bloodhoof village","gizzard","maur raincaller","mazzranache","mulgore","remedy","swoop"},rel={"npc:maur-raincaller","quest:766","subzone:bloodhoof-village","item:plainstrider-scale","item:prairie-wolf-heart","item:flatland-cougar-femur"},src={"Swoop Gizzard","Mazzranache (Classic)"}}
E["item:vial-of-innocent-blood"] = {t="item",n="Vial of Innocent Blood",z="thunderbluff",s="Syndicate shadow mages gather Vial of Innocent Blood in the ruins of Durnholde Keep. The Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill seeks it as a catalyst for experimental toxins.",h="Syndicate shadow mages gather Vial of Innocent Blood in the ruins of Durnholde Keep.",sec={{t="A Gruesome Reagent",b="Syndicate shadow mages gather innocent blood in the ruins of Durnholde Keep. The Syndicate's fallen human nobles practice dark arts within the crumbled walls. Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill wants untainted blood for an experimental pacifying agent. He means to use it against the Venture Company in Stonetalon Mountains, and sees the Syndicate's stores as a convenient source.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Vial of Innocent Blood used for?",a="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill uses the blood to brew a toxin meant to suppress aggression among Venture Company operators troubling the Horde in Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"innocent blood use","what is vial of innocent blood for","blood of innocents use"},it="item"},{q="Who carries these vials?",a="Syndicate shadow mages carry the vials around the ruined fortress of Durnholde Keep in the southeastern Hillsbrad Foothills.",al={"who drops vial of innocent blood","where to get innocent blood","syndicate shadow mages"},it="origin"},{q="Why do Syndicate shadow mages have innocent blood?",a="The Syndicate's human brigands and fallen nobles employ shadow casters to harvest and preserve innocent blood for dark magical experiments.",al={"why do syndicate have blood","syndicate blood rituals"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need blood from innocents?",a="Lydon says innocent blood has rare properties needed to make a concoction that bleeds violence from its victims and renders them docile.",al={"why innocent blood","apothecary lydon blood"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Vial of Innocent Blood?",a="It is a small phial containing blood harvested from guiltless victims, prized as a potent reagent by dark spellcasters and alchemists alike. Rather than gathering it through honorable or ordinary means, it is seized specifically to fuel insidious rituals and powerful chemical concoctions.",al={"what is vial of innocent blood","vial of innocent blood lore","what is this blood"},it="identity",add="21111c2c"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you know the Royal Apothecary Society will use morally questionable ingredients, gathering from human outlaws to advance its alchemy.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, securing this reagent helps its efforts against Venture Company deforestation in Stonetalon."},kw={"apothecary lydon","durnholde keep","hillsbrad foothills","innocent blood","syndicate shadow mage","tarren mill","vial of innocent blood"},rel={"quest:1066","subzone:durnholde-keep","subzone:tarren-mill","topic:syndicate","zone:hillsbrad","topic:venture-company","topic:horde","topic:mage"},src={"Vial of Innocent Blood","Blood of Innocents (quest)"}}
E["item:zamah-s-note"] = {t="item",n="Zamah's Note",z="thunderbluff",s="Zamah's Note carries an urgent plea from Thunder Bluff to Tarren Mill. Zamah asks Apothecary Lydon for an alchemical way to drive the Venture Company from Stonetalon without direct bloodshed.",h="Zamah's Note carries an urgent plea from Thunder Bluff to Tarren Mill.",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Great Sea",b="The Venture Company has dug deep into the Stonetalon Mountains, felling trees and tearing up sacred land. Zamah wants a way to force the goblins out without slaughter. She turns to the Forsaken Royal Apothecary Society for help. Her note tells her colleague, Apothecary Lydon, about the danger in Stonetalon. Lydon is in Tarren Mill, far away in the Hillsbrad Foothills of Lordaeron.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Connections",b="The sealed note must cross continents to reach Lydon. Travelers from Kalimdor take a zeppelin to the Undercity, then travel south through Silverpine Forest into Hillsbrad. Lydon is intrigued by Zamah's specific request. Word has reached him from across the ocean, and he prepares an alchemical answer to the goblin problem.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Zamah's Note?",a="Zamah's Note is a sealed letter from Thunder Bluff to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill. It asks for an alchemical formula to remove the Venture Company from Stonetalon.",al={"what is this item","zamah note","letter to lydon"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Zamah need help from Tarren Mill?",a="Zamah wants to drive the goblins out of Stonetalon without bloodshed. She asks Apothecary Lydon because the Forsaken alchemists make specialized concoctions for subtle disruptions.",al={"why send to hillsbrad","why contact lydon","why tarren mill"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the note need to be delivered?",a="The note must reach Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, in the Hillsbrad Foothills of Lordaeron.",al={"who gets the note","zamah note turn in","where do i take the note"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Who is the Venture Company mentioned in the note?",a="The Venture Company is a goblin-run mining and logging syndicate. It clear-cuts forests, exploits natural resources, and pollutes lands across Kalimdor, including the sacred peaks of the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"venture company stonetalon","who are venture co","venture co"},it="threat"},{q="Where does Zamah's Note come from, and who wrote it?",a="The note was penned by Zamah, a Forsaken residing in Thunder Bluff. Concerned with the Venture Company's ongoing exploitation and destruction within the Stonetalon Mountains, she drafted the letter to reach out across the sea to a trusted colleague in Lordaeron.",al={"who wrote zamahs note","where did zamahs note come from","who made zamahs note"},it="origin",add="c24d4d7f"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want Zamah's Note?",a="Apothecary Lydon needs the note because it outlines Zamah's specific request for an alchemical solution against the Venture Company. Zamah seeks an extreme, bloodless method to drive the defilers out of Stonetalon, and the note details her precise requirements so Lydon can prepare the proper concoction.",al={"why does lydon want the note","why is zamahs note wanted","purpose of zamahs note"},it="why_wanted",add="6846e14b"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="The note's delivery shows how the Horde's distant capitals across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms share routes and resources.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you belong to a people whose Royal Apothecary Society offers specialized chemical expertise to allies facing difficult crises."},kw={"hillsbrad foothills","lydon","stonetalon mountains","tarren mill","thunder bluff","undercity","venture company","zamah"},rel={"quest:1065","subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","zone:undercity","topic:venture-company","topic:lordaeron","zone:tirisfal"},src={"Zamah's Note","Journey to Tarren Mill"}}
E["npc:ahanu"] = {t="npc",n="Ahanu",z="thunderbluff",s="Couriers arriving in Thunder Bluff can find Ahanu in Hewa's Armory. He crafts and trades leather armor for travelers and young braves setting out across Mulgore and the wider plains, and helps new couriers find their way across the bluffs.",h="Couriers arriving in Thunder Bluff can find Ahanu in Hewa's Armory.",sec={{t="Merchant of Hewa's Armory",b="Ahanu works the hides his friend Jahan Hawkwing sends from the Crossroads. In Hewa's Armory on Thunder Bluff's lower rise, he crafts durable leather gear for those who travel Kalimdor's grasslands. Travelers arriving by wind rider from the Crossroads can find him among the city's tradesfolk. He receives their deliveries and directs messengers toward the local flight roosts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ahanu?",a="Ahanu is a tauren merchant in Hewa's Armory on Thunder Bluff's lower rise. He sells leather armor and helps couriers arriving from the Crossroads.",al={"ahanu npc","ahanu lore","who is ahanu"},it="identity"},{q="What does Ahanu sell?",a="Ahanu sells basic leather armor, including jerkins, belts, boots, and bracers. The gear is made for hunters, rogues, and young adventurers.",al={"ahanu goods","ahanu wares","ahanu vendor"},gp=true},{q="Where in Thunder Bluff can I find him?",a="Ahanu works inside Hewa's Armory on Thunder Bluff's lower rise, near other armorers, leatherworkers, and weapon smiths.",al={"ahanu location","where is ahanu","ahanu map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests involve Ahanu?",a="Young tauren adventurers bring goods to Ahanu by wind rider in 'Ride to Thunder Bluff'. Afterward, he sends them back to Tal, the city's wind rider master.",al={"ahanu quests","ride to thunder bluff ahanu"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Ahanu on?",a="Ahanu is a loyal member of the Horde and a proud citizen of Thunder Bluff. He operates openly under the banner of High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof, outfitting tauren hunters, druids, and visiting Horde travelers who pass through the city.",al={"ahanu faction","is ahanu horde","who does ahanu serve"},it="side",add="f9ab69c3"},{q="Why is Ahanu here?",a="Ahanu tends shop inside Hewa's Armory on the lower rise of Thunder Bluff. He serves as a resident armorer, providing sturdy cured and tanned leather gear to hunters and wayfarers exploring the plains of Mulgore and the wider continent.",al={"why is ahanu in thunder bluff","ahanu purpose thunder bluff","what brought ahanu here"},it="why_here",add="b68e223b"},{q="What does Ahanu want?",a="Ahanu is content with his trade as a leather merchant, seeking little beyond fair business and companionship. He focuses on supplying travelers with durable armor while enjoying the company of fellow locals in the city.",al={"what does ahanu need","ahanu goal","ahanu motivation"},it="wants",add="c2a07e44"},{q="Who is Ahanu tied to?",a="Ahanu counts Jahan Hawkwing, a fellow tauren merchant at the Crossroads in the Barrens, among his friends. Jahan sends him fresh bundles of hides, which Ahanu works into leather goods in Thunder Bluff.",al={"ahanu friends","who does ahanu know","ahanu companions"},it="ties",add="b04a3d48"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a young tauren brave arriving from the Crossroads by wind rider, you can find familiar hospitality and essential hides for the road with Ahanu."},kw={"ahanu","hewa's armory","jahan hawkwing","leather armor","mulgore","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:6362","quest:6363","zone:thunderbluff","npc:jahan-hawkwing","topic:tauren"},src={"Ahanu"}}
E["npc:bashana-runetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Bashana Runetotem",z="thunderbluff",s="On the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, Bashana Runetotem studies plants and corruption. She is the daughter of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and aids the Cenarion Circle.",h="On the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, Bashana Runetotem studies plants and corruption.",sec={{t="A Daughter of the Circle",b="Bashana Runetotem carries her father Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem’s druidic legacy on Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise. While he guides tauren druids and advises Cairne Bloodhoof, Bashana studies unusual plants and regional threats. She gives travelers tools such as evergreen pouches to cultivate mysterious flora, including morrowgrain. She also coordinates Horde efforts against corruption spreading from places such as Blackfathom Deeps.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bashana Runetotem?",a="Bashana Runetotem is a tauren druid and researcher on Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise. The daughter of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, she studies unusual plants for the Cenarion Circle and organizes responses to natural threats across Kalimdor.",al={"who is bashana","bashana lore","who is bashana runetotem"},it="identity"},{q="What research does she conduct with morrowgrain?",a="Bashana asks Horde adventurers to cultivate and gather morrowgrain with seed packets and soil. The Cenarion Circle studies the herb’s unusual properties and its connection to other botanical mysteries across Kalimdor.",al={"morrowgrain research","what does bashana do with morrowgrain","why morrowgrain"},it="wants"},{q="What is her connection to Blackfathom Deeps?",a="Bashana receives a report and proof from adventurers sent by Argent Guard Thaelrid to confront the cultists of Blackfathom Deeps. She rewards their help against corruption threatening Ashenvale.",al={"bashana blackfathom deeps","blackfathom villainy quest","why bfd"},it="why_here"},{q="Where can she be found?",a="Bashana is on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, near the druidic pavilions. The mesa is dedicated to the city’s shamans, druids, and spiritual elders.",al={"where is bashana runetotem","bashana location","how to find bashana"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Bashana Runetotem on?",a="Bashana is devoted to both the Horde and the Cenarion Circle. As a tauren druid operating from Thunder Bluff, she works to aid her people and the broader Horde, while staying true to the nature-defending tenets of the Cenarion druids who study the mysteries and corruptions troubling Kalimdor.",al={"bashana runetotem faction","who does bashana serve","bashana horde or cenarion circle"},it="side",add="2d6e22c9"},{q="Who is Bashana Runetotem tied to?",a="Bashana is the daughter of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, the venerable leader of the tauren druids in Thunder Bluff. Under his guidance, she carries out important research on behalf of the Cenarion Circle and helps guide new champions who wish to aid the druids' work.",al={"bashana runetotem family","who is bashana related to","bashana hamuul daughter"},it="ties",add="10189cb7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid learning under Hamuul, Bashana shows the fieldwork needed to understand Kalimdor’s changing ecology.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Bashana to connect Thunder Bluff’s Cenarion Circle with champions fighting cultist threats."},kw={"bashana","blackfathom deeps","cenarion circle","elder rise","hamuul","morrowgrain","runetotem","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:1489","quest:1200","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:cenarion-circle","zone:blackfathom","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Bashana Runetotem"}}
E["npc:bluff-runner-windstrider"] = {t="npc",n="Bluff Runner Windstrider",z="thunderbluff",s="On Thunder Bluff's mesas, Bluff Runner Windstrider carries urgent messages across the city. He directs Horde travelers toward distant frontiers, including Ashenvale, Feralas, and the Plaguelands.",h="On Thunder Bluff's mesas, Bluff Runner Windstrider carries urgent messages across the city.",sec={{t="A Messenger on the Mesas",b="Bluff Runner Windstrider carries messages across Thunder Bluff's high plateaus. His swift runs keep the city's leaders and visitors informed. He jogs along the rope bridges and pathways, calling out news and carrying dispatches. When outposts across Kalimdor or the Eastern Kingdoms need reinforcements, Windstrider calls on passing champions to carry word and answer the call to arms.",sp=0},{t="Calls to the Frontier",b="Bluff Runner Windstrider's messages reach far beyond Mulgore. He sends adventurers north to join Senani Thunderheart's great hunt at Splintertree Post in Ashenvale. He points seasoned scouts south toward Camp Mojache in Feralas and carries grave warnings about the ongoing undead menace in the Western Plaguelands. His dispatches connect Mulgore's tribal heart to the wider conflicts of the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Bluff Runner Windstrider?",a="Bluff Runner Windstrider carries messages across Thunder Bluff. He shares news and calls on capable Horde travelers to help with urgent campaigns across Azeroth.",al={"windstrider npc","bluff runner","who is windstrider"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Bluff Runner Windstrider?",a="Bluff Runner Windstrider jogs along Thunder Bluff's bridges and terraces. He often circles between the central mesa and neighboring rises.",al={"windstrider location","where is bluff runner","find windstrider"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Windstrider offer?",a="Bluff Runner Windstrider directs travelers toward distant regions. His calls include the Ashenvale hunt, the establishment of Camp Mojache in Feralas, and calls to arms in the Plaguelands.",al={"windstrider quests","what does he give","bluff runner tasks"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is he called a 'Bluff Runner'?",a="Thunder Bluff's rugged mesas, cliffs, and suspended bridges can make mounted travel cumbersome or slow. Runners like Windstrider carry messages across the city on foot.",al={"what is a bluff runner","bluff runner title"},it="name"},{q="Whose side is Bluff Runner Windstrider on?",a="Bluff Runner Windstrider serves the tauren tribes and the Horde from high atop Thunder Bluff. As an official courier and messenger, he acts on behalf of the elders and chieftains to deliver critical news, rally warriors, and maintain communication with distant outposts across Kalimdor and beyond.",al={"windstrider faction","bluff runner windstrider allegiance","who does windstrider serve"},it="side",add="e05bd34a"},{q="Why is Bluff Runner Windstrider here?",a="Windstrider roams the rises of Thunder Bluff to circulate urgent word among travelers and defenders. A city built across sprawling mesas requires swift couriers on foot to relay announcements between leaders and adventurers, ensuring word reaches those ready to answer the call of distant settlements.",al={"why is windstrider in thunder bluff","windstrider purpose thunder bluff","what does windstrider do here"},it="why_here",add="b3137841"},{q="What does Bluff Runner Windstrider want?",a="Windstrider seeks capable adventurers willing to venture far beyond Mulgore. By delivering summons, news, and calls to arms, he hopes to guide rising heroes toward frontiers where the Horde needs aid, directing them toward vital hunting grounds and embattled outposts across Azeroth.",al={"what does windstrider need","bluff runner windstrider motives","windstrider quests why"},it="wants",add="7698149f"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can carry news from Mulgore to the fronts where the Horde fights for resources and survival.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can follow the tradition of runners who keep the tribes and central elders connected without machinery or foreign post networks."},kw={"ashenvale","bluff runner","camp mojache","messenger","mulgore","thunder bluff","windstrider"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","topic:tauren","topic:horde","quest:235","zone:ashenvale","subzone:camp-mojache"},src={"Bluff Runner Windstrider"}}
E["npc:dendrite-starblaze"] = {t="npc",n="Dendrite Starblaze",z="thunderbluff",s="In Nighthaven, Dendrite Starblaze guides druids who come to Moonglade. As a Cenarion Circle mentor, he welcomes night elf and tauren apprentices. Through him they are summoned to the holy grove to master its rites, from cleansing toxins to communing with nature's forms.",h="In Nighthaven, Dendrite Starblaze guides druids who come to Moonglade.",sec={{t="A Guide in the Sacred Haven",b="When novice druids learn Teleport: Moonglade, Dendrite is among the first to greet them in Nighthaven. He follows the Cenarion Circle's calling beyond the Alliance and Horde. Night elf and tauren druids alike find kinship beneath the haven's boughs, where Kaldorei tradition meets the tauren path.",sp=0},{t="Trials of the Wild",b="Dendrite guides apprentices into nature's deeper ways. He sends them to examine tainted waters and seek herbs that can cure poison and pestilence. Then he oversees the water trials, testing their patience and endurance beneath the surface before he grants them communion with aquatic forms.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is a night elf druid and Cenarion Circle mentor in Nighthaven, within Moonglade. He guides developing druids through essential rites and training.",al={"dendrite starblaze","who is dendrite","starblaze moonglade"},it="identity"},{q="Why does a night elf train Horde tauren?",a="The Cenarion Circle keeps beyond the Alliance and Horde's political divisions. In Moonglade, night elves and tauren practice druidic arts together under ancient oaths of brotherhood, leaving worldly conflicts beyond the mountain passes.",al={"why does dendrite train horde","dendrite tauren druid","cross faction druid mentor"},it="side"},{q="What quests does Dendrite Starblaze offer?",a="Dendrite guides druids through trials in curing venom and disease, then toward the communion required for aquatic form.",al={"dendrite quests","starblaze quest list"},gp=true},{q="Where can Dendrite Starblaze be found?",a="Dendrite can be found in Nighthaven, on the northern shores of Lake Elune'ara in Moonglade.",al={"dendrite location","where is starblaze","dendrite starblaze map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="How do young druids reach Dendrite for the first time?",a="Racial trainers teach novice druids Teleport: Moonglade around their tenth circle of training. The spell carries them straight to Moonglade, where Dendrite awaits.",al={"how to get to dendrite","teleport to moonglade quest"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Can non-druid adventurers interact with him?",a="Non-druids may visit Nighthaven and speak with Dendrite. He offers no training, trials or tasks to those outside the Cenarion Circle's druidic traditions.",al={"non druid dendrite","can warrior talk to starblaze"},gp=true},{q="What does Dendrite Starblaze want?",a="Dendrite guides novice druids along the path of nature and balance. Through trials honoring the spirits of the wild—such as communing with the Great Bear Spirit and mastering powers over poison and the waters—he works to ensure that all initiates, regardless of their heritage, learn the responsibilities and ancient disciplines of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"dendrite starblaze goal","what does dendrite want","dendrite starblaze motive"},it="wants",add="3038adca"},{q="Why is Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade?",a="Moonglade is sacred, neutral ground where the Cenarion Circle convenes away from worldly factional conflict. Stationed in Nighthaven, Dendrite serves as a welcoming mentor for fledgling druids summoned to the haven, administering foundational lessons and trials essential to their spiritual growth.",al={"why is dendrite here","dendrite starblaze location moonglade","why is dendrite in nighthaven"},it="why_here",add="ef589fff"},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze tied to?",a="Dendrite is an emissary and mentor within the Cenarion Circle. He works closely with fellow druids of both night elf and tauren lineage, answering the call of the wild spirits and the teachings of Cenarius rather than the political banners of Darnassus or the Horde.",al={"dendrite starblaze faction","dendrite starblaze cenarion circle","who does dendrite serve"},it="ties",add="7aee8496"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="When you first teleport to Moonglade, Dendrite guides you in curing sickness and seeking communion with aquatic forms.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Shu'halo druid from Mulgore, you can see in Dendrite how the Cenarion Circle's bond reaches beyond the feud between Horde and Alliance.",["race:NightElf"]="As a Kaldorei initiate, you meet Dendrite at Nighthaven, where he keeps the classical rites of nature stewardship and welcomes you into the Cenarion order."},kw={"aquatic form","cenarion circle","curing the sick","dendrite starblaze","druid","lessons anew","moonglade","night elf","nighthaven"},rel={"subzone:nighthaven","quest:5921","quest:6121","quest:6124","quest:6125","quest:31","quest:5932","quest:5931"},src={"Dendrite Starblaze"}}
E["npc:falla-sagewind"] = {t="npc",n="Falla Sagewind",z="thunderbluff",s="On a crag above the Barrens, Falla Sagewind watches the land for signs of trouble. Her camp lies between the Crossroads and the Lushwater Oasis, where she studies changes in nature and magic.",h="On a crag above the Barrens, Falla Sagewind watches the land for signs of trouble.",sec={{t="Watcher of the High Crag",b="Falla Sagewind keeps camp on a secluded summit southwest of the Crossroads, high above the Barrens trails. From there, she watches the savanna and the changes in its wildlife. She also studies corruption rising from fissures beneath the Wailing Caverns. Her vigil keeps her apart from the daily trade at the Crossroads, but her attention remains on the spirits and wounds of the land.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="Strange, pulsing shards taken from mutated beasts in the Wailing Caverns lead travelers to Falla Sagewind. She studies the twisted magic disrupting the oases and recognizes signs that the Emerald Dream has turned foul beneath the earth. For deeper answers about the nightmare taking root in the region, she sends travelers to the wise druids of the Cenarion Circle.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Falla Sagewind?",a="Falla Sagewind watches over the Barrens from her camp on a high cliff southwest of the Crossroads. She helps travelers understand the strange magical afflictions spreading across the region.",al={"who is falla sagewind","who is falla","falla sagewind lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Falla Sagewind?",a="Falla Sagewind camps atop a mountain peak southwest of the Crossroads and north of the Lushwater Oasis. Rocky paths wind up from the surrounding savanna to her camp.",al={"falla sagewind location","where is falla","how to reach falla sagewind"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Falla Sagewind interested in the Wailing Caverns?",a="Falla Sagewind studies strange magic in a glowing shard recovered from the Wailing Caverns. She directs travelers to experienced druids for further counsel.",al={"falla wailing caverns","why does falla care about the oasis","falla glowing shard"},it="motive"},{q="Is Falla Sagewind affiliated with any clan or family?",a="Falla Sagewind shares her surname with other tauren, but no family connection is confirmed.",al={"sagewind family","who are the sagewinds","is falla related to tahu"},it="ties"},{q="What quests involve Falla Sagewind?",a="Falla Sagewind helps investigate the Wailing Caverns through The Glowing Shard and In Nightmares, which concern the dark dream corrupting the local oases.",al={"falla sagewind quests","quests from falla","in nightmares quest"},gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players interact with Falla Sagewind?",a="Yes. Falla Sagewind helps travelers of both factions with the Glowing Shard. She sends Alliance adventurers to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus and Horde adventurers to Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.",al={"is falla sagewind hostile","falla alliance friendly"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Falla Sagewind on?",a="Falla Sagewind is a tauren who keeps to no faction's banner. Stationed in the rugged heights of the Barrens, she aids travelers of both the Horde and the Alliance who investigate the unnatural corruptions spreading out from the Wailing Caverns, and assists those working to cleanse the land.",al={"falla sagewind faction","is falla sagewind horde","who does falla sagewind serve"},it="side",add="53e3505a"},{q="What does Falla Sagewind want?",a="Falla Sagewind seeks to understand and confront the growing corruption seeping from the Wailing Caverns. When adventurers bring her curious relics, such as glowing shards pulled from the creatures within, she works to uncover the nightmare taking root inside the subterranean springs.",al={"falla sagewind goals","what does falla want","falla sagewind purpose"},it="wants",add="709098cb"},{q="Why is Falla Sagewind here?",a="Falla Sagewind keeps watch atop a mountain ridge southwest of the Crossroads, overlooking the Lushwater Oasis and the nearby entrance to the Wailing Caverns. From this elevated vantage, she monitors the land's corruption and guides travelers who uncover dark relics tied to the disturbed dreamers below.",al={"why is falla sagewind in the barrens","why is falla on the mountain"},it="why_here",add="26262d64"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may see Falla Sagewind's watch over the earth as quiet stewardship. From high places, she watches for spiritual rot while her brethren defend the roads below.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can follow Falla Sagewind's help in tracing the tragic descent of Naralex and the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can turn to Falla Sagewind to interpret strange omens and corrupted relics brought back by scouts from the contested Barrens savannas."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","falla","glowing shard","lushwater oasis","nightmares","sagewind","tauren","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:6981","quest:3369","subzone:lushwater-oasis","subzone:crossroads","topic:tauren"},src={"Falla Sagewind"}}
E["npc:holt-thunderhorn"] = {t="npc",n="Holt Thunderhorn",z="thunderbluff",s="On Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Holt Thunderhorn trains tauren hunters for the Horde. He teaches tracking and survival, and points hunters toward specialized trials across Mulgore and beyond.",h="On Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Holt Thunderhorn trains tauren hunters for the Horde.",sec={{t="Master of the Rise",b="Holt Thunderhorn trains hunters for the Horde on Hunter Rise, above the plains of Mulgore. He teaches ranged combat, tracking, and survival. Like other elders of his craft, he guides young tauren as they move from roaming hunters to disciplined defenders of their new capital.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can Holt Thunderhorn be found?",a="Holt Thunderhorn can be found on Hunter Rise, the southeastern plateau in Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital in Mulgore.",al={"holt thunderhorn location","where is holt","hunter trainer thunder bluff"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What does Holt Thunderhorn teach?",a="Holt Thunderhorn is a hunter trainer who teaches marksmanship, wilderness survival, and beast taming. He also directs novice hunters to specialized beast mastery trials.",al={"what does holt teach","holt thunderhorn trainer","what abilities holt"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What role do hunters hold in Thunder Bluff?",a="Hunters are the traditional backbone of tauren society. They provide food, patrol the borders against centaur raiding parties, and honor the Earth Mother through balanced, reverent tracking.",al={"hunter rise purpose","tauren hunter lore"}},{q="Who is Holt Thunderhorn?",a="Holt Thunderhorn is a respected tauren hunter trainer stationed on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. Dedicated to passing on the wilderness arts of the shu'halo, he instructs young hunters in marksmanship, survival, and the ancient bond between hunter and beast.",al={"who is holt","holt thunderhorn lore","who is holt thunderhorn"},it="identity",add="c3f17fe5"},{q="Whose side is Holt Thunderhorn on?",a="Holt serves the tauren tribes of Thunder Bluff and the greater Horde under the leadership of Cairne Bloodhoof. He aids any hunter loyal to the Horde who seeks to sharpen their instincts and honor the plains.",al={"holt thunderhorn faction","who does holt serve","is holt horde"},it="side",add="d59405da"},{q="Why is Holt Thunderhorn here?",a="Holt remains atop Hunter Rise to mentor new generations of trackers, marksmen, and beast masters. With the tauren now settled in Mulgore, skilled hunters are essential to sustain the city and protect the mesas from hostile wildlife and invaders.",al={"why is holt in thunder bluff","what is holt doing here","holt thunderhorn purpose"},it="why_here",add="03eb281d"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can look to Holt Thunderhorn as a central mentor in Thunder Bluff. He teaches weapon techniques and tracking, and refers hunters to beast taming.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you inherit a hunting culture that fed and protected the nomadic tribes long before they made a permanent home atop the bluffs. Holt Thunderhorn carries on that tradition on Hunter Rise."},kw={"holt thunderhorn","hunter rise","hunter trainer","mulgore","thunder bluff"},rel={"subzone:hunter-rise","zone:thunderbluff","quest:6081","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren"},src={"Holt Thunderhorn"}}
E["npc:innkeeper-pala"] = {t="npc",n="Innkeeper Pala",z="thunderbluff",s="On Thunder Bluff’s lower rise, travelers find Innkeeper Pala tending the Cat and the Shaman. She offers a place to rest, cold drinks, and a hearthstone binding for journeys across Mulgore and beyond.",h="On Thunder Bluff’s lower rise, travelers find Innkeeper Pala tending the Cat and the Shaman.",sec={{t="Hospitality on the Lower Rise",b="Innkeeper Pala tends the hearth at the Cat and the Shaman on Thunder Bluff’s lower rise. Travelers arrive from the central lifts or the plains of Mulgore. In the common room, weary warriors, wandering druids, and the Horde’s visiting allies can find shelter, a warm drink, and a familiar place to rest.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Innkeeper Pala?",a="Find Pala inside the Cat and the Shaman on Thunder Bluff’s lower rise, near the city’s main lifts.",al={"pala location","where is pala","innkeeper pala map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What services does she provide to travelers?",a="Pala can bind your hearthstone to the Cat and the Shaman, letting you return there instantly. She also sells simple food and drinks to restore health and mana.",al={"pala services","can i bind hearthstone thunder bluff","what does pala sell"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the name of her tavern?",a="Pala’s tavern is called the Cat and the Shaman. Horde travelers passing through the city’s lower tier gather there.",al={"cat and the shaman","thunder bluff lower inn name","pala inn name"},it="name"},{q="Who is Innkeeper Pala?",a="Innkeeper Pala is a tauren host who tends to travelers and weary wanderers at the Cat and the Shaman, located on the lower rise of Thunder Bluff. She maintains the hearth, sweeps the floors, and offers food, drink, and a restful place for those visiting the high mesas of the tauren capital.",al={"who is pala","innkeeper pala","who is innkeeper pala"},it="identity",add="18c94984"},{q="Whose side is Innkeeper Pala on?",a="Innkeeper Pala is loyal to the tauren tribes and the Horde under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Standing welcomingly in the heart of Thunder Bluff, she gladly caters to tauren kin, orcs, trolls, and the visiting Forsaken who seek hospitality within the city.",al={"innkeeper pala faction","innkeeper pala allegiance","is pala horde"},it="side",add="3afadd2e"},{q="What does Innkeeper Pala want?",a="Pala wants little more than to keep the Cat and the Shaman running smoothly. Her focus remains on offering warm hospitality, serving provisions, and providing a clean, peaceful sanctuary where weary travelers can bind their spirits and rest between arduous journeys across Kalimdor.",al={"what does pala want","pala goal","innkeeper pala purpose"},it="wants",add="0c2271e0"},{q="Why is Innkeeper Pala here?",a="Thunder Bluff's sprawling rises see steady traffic of hunters, shamans, and emissaries across the plains of Mulgore. Innkeeper Pala remains stationed at the lower rise to run the tavern, ensuring that arriving adventurers and traders always have a welcoming hearth and provisions close at hand.",al={"why is pala here","why is pala in thunder bluff","innkeeper pala role"},it="why_here",add="1c871847"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren returning from Kalimdor’s frontiers, you can find a familiar, welcoming face beneath the towering totems of Thunder Bluff’s central mesas.",["faction:Horde"]="As an orc, troll, or Forsaken visiting Mulgore, you can rest at Pala’s inn beside the lifts."},kw={"cat and the shaman","hearthstone","innkeeper","innkeeper pala","mulgore","pala","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren","topic:horde","quest:5923","quest:8357"},src={"Innkeeper Pala"}}
E["npc:lieutenant-lisande"] = {t="npc",n="Lieutenant Lisande",z="thunderbluff",s="On Thunder Bluff’s high mesas, Lieutenant Lisande watches for signs of the Scourge.",h="On Thunder Bluff’s high mesas, Lieutenant Lisande watches for signs of the Scourge.",sec={{t="An Unlikely Envoy",b="Lieutenant Lisande serves the Argent Dawn from Thunder Bluff, where human faces are rare. The holy order watches for signs of the Lich King's taint, even in remote Kalimdor. When undead forces stir on the plains below, Lisande calls on Horde champions to ride out and investigate before the Scourge can defile the sacred earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is a human standing in Thunder Bluff?",a="Lisande represents the Argent Dawn, an organization dedicated to destroying the Scourge. The Dawn welcomes both Alliance and Horde races, and its liaisons may enter capital cities to coordinate defenses against the undead.",al={"human in thunder bluff","why is Lisande here","is she hostile"},it="why_here"},{q="What is the Argent Dawn's interest in Mulgore?",a="The Lich King's reach threatens every corner of Azeroth, not only the Eastern Kingdoms. Lisande watches for necromantic activity or Scourge forces that threaten Mulgore, so local defenders know of the danger.",al={"scourge in mulgore","why thunder bluff","undead in tauren lands"},it="purpose"},{q="What tasks does Lieutenant Lisande give out?",a="Lisande sends adventurers down from the bluffs to investigate Scourge incursions around the territory and report back. The Dawn can then assess the scale of the threat.",al={"lisande quest","what does lisande do","investigate quest"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lieutenant Lisande?",a="Lieutenant Lisande is an officer serving the Argent Dawn. Despite being a human in the heart of Horde territory, she stands openly in Thunder Bluff to rally brave defenders against a menace threatening all living things.",al={"who is lisande","lieutenant lisande identity","who is lieutenant lisande"},it="identity",add="986453a4"},{q="Whose side is Lieutenant Lisande on?",a="Lisande is loyal to the Argent Dawn rather than the Alliance. The Dawn is a neutral coalition dedicated entirely to fighting the Scourge, which allows her to work directly alongside the tauren and Horde champions without factional hostility.",al={"lisande alliance or horde","who does lisande serve","is lisande alliance"},it="side",add="b5328b2a"},{q="What does Lieutenant Lisande want?",a="Lisande wants vigilant adventurers to investigate and confront the Scourge forces encroaching on the lands outside Thunder Bluff. Her aim is to stem the undead threat before it can overrun the plains of Mulgore.",al={"what does lisande want","lisande goals","why does lisande need help"},it="wants",add="9158bc2a"},{q="Who is Lieutenant Lisande tied to?",a="She is directly tied to the Argent Dawn, an independent order of holy warriors, magi, and scouts drawn from diverse races to combat the Scourge wherever the undead menace rears its head.",al={"lisande faction","who does lisande work with","lisande connections"},it="ties",add="0fde76ad"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Though Lisande is an outsider, the tauren respect the Argent Dawn's work to cleanse the land of the undead.",["faction:Horde"]="Lisande reminds the Horde that fighting the Scourge calls for pragmatism and occasional cooperation with neutral human orders."},kw={"argent dawn","lieutenant lisande","lisande","mulgore","scourge","scourge invasion","thunder bluff"},rel={"topic:argent-dawn","zone:thunderbluff","topic:scourge"},src={"Lieutenant Lisande"}}
E["npc:magatha-grimtotem"] = {t="npc",n="Magatha Grimtotem",z="thunderbluff",s="On Elder Rise, Magatha Grimtotem challenges Cairne Bloodhoof's vision for the tauren. The Grimtotem matriarch and Thunder Bluff's Elder Crone is a formidable shaman and political schemer.",h="On Elder Rise, Magatha Grimtotem challenges Cairne Bloodhoof's vision for the tauren.",sec={{t="The Matriarch of Elder Rise",b="Magatha Grimtotem leads the Grimtotem tribe from Elder Rise, with her own retinue and bodyguards. She gained authority through an arranged union, then her mate died suddenly in a climbing accident. Her reclusive tribe follows her as its political and spiritual leader. Magatha preaches tauren dominance, unlike Cairne Bloodhoof. She sees other mortal races as intruders on Kalimdor, to be eradicated or swept aside.",sp=0},{t="A Curious Alliance",b="Though Magatha openly disdains other races, she was among the first to advocate admitting the Forsaken to the Horde. She says the tauren can teach the undead spiritual balance and help them reclaim their humanity. Magatha also works directly with the Royal Apothecary Society beneath Thunder Bluff, consulting figures such as Apothecary Zamah about practical alchemy and arcane relics.",sp=0},{t="Political Machinations",b="Magatha Grimtotem counsels Cairne while working to weaken his authority and testing the defenses of potential threats. She sends adventurers into dangerous places, from Ragefire Chasm to face trogg forces to a hunt for the vengeful spirit Arikara. Each assignment builds Grimtotem influence or prepares her to supplant the Bloodhoof dynasty.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Magatha Grimtotem?",a="Magatha Grimtotem is the Elder Crone and matriarch of the Grimtotem tribe. A gifted shaman since childhood, she took total rule after her mate died in a climbing accident. She resides on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and is Cairne Bloodhoof's chief political rival.",al={"magatha backstory","who is the elder crone","elder crone thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Magatha support the Forsaken?",a="Magatha says tauren traditions and shamanic wisdom can guide the Forsaken back toward humanity. Many suspect her ties to the Royal Apothecary Society seek alchemical secrets and allies beyond Cairne's loyal inner circle.",al={"magatha and undead","why magatha likes forsaken","magatha apothecary zamah"}},{q="What is Magatha's relationship with Cairne Bloodhoof?",a="Magatha sees Cairne Bloodhoof as soft, naive, and unfit to lead the united tauren. Cairne favors coexistence in the Horde and peace across Kalimdor; Magatha believes the Grimtotem should reclaim ancestral lands by force and eliminate foreign intruders.",al={"magatha vs cairne","does magatha hate cairne","cairne and magatha"},it="conflict"},{q="What was the mission in Ragefire Chasm?",a="Magatha sent Maur into Ragefire Chasm beneath Orgrimmar to negotiate with its troggs. They killed him, so she sent Horde adventurers into the cavern to retrieve his satchel and butcher the troggs in retribution.",al={"magatha ragefire quest","why magatha sent maur","lost satchel magatha"}},{q="Who is Arikara?",a="Arikara is a vengeful wind serpent spirit said to seek retribution against the tauren. Magatha says Arikara seeks vengeance against Cairne Bloodhoof and sends capable champions to summon and slay the beast with enchanted agave.",al={"serpent of vengeance","arikara quest","magatha arikara"}},{q="Where can Magatha Grimtotem be found?",a="Magatha resides in the large main tent atop Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, attended by her servant Rahauro and two stoic Grimtotem guards.",al={"magatha location","where is magatha","magatha elder rise"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Magatha Grimtotem on?",a="Magatha serves herself and the Grimtotem tribe above all else. While she holds an honored seat on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise and formally belongs to the Horde, her allegiance is purely transactional. She openly challenges High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof's vision for their people, favoring ruthless tauren dominance over peace, and pursues private alliances—most notably with the Forsaken—to further her own faction's reach.",al={"magatha loyalties","who does magatha serve","is magatha loyal to the horde"},it="side",add="ebac2d3c"},{q="What does Magatha Grimtotem want?",a="Magatha believes that only she is fit to lead the tauren. She seeks to wrest authority away from Cairne Bloodhoof, drive all lesser races from Kalimdor, and reclaim the ancestral holdings of her people. To amass the power needed to achieve this, she constantly gathers ancient relics, tests potential enemies, and cultivates controversial relationships that Cairne and the other elders would never condone.",al={"magatha goals","what is magatha planning","magatha motivations"},it="wants",add="b26ae613"},{q="Why is Magatha Grimtotem here?",a="As the elder crone and matriarch of the Grimtotem, Magatha resides on the Elder Rise to represent her fierce tribe within the united tauren nation. From this lofty vantage, she advises travelers, counsels the city, and keeps a watchful eye on Cairne Bloodhoof's rule, ensuring her clan retains a powerful voice in the governance of Thunder Bluff.",al={"why is magatha in thunder bluff","why is magatha here"},it="why_here",add="0cc6173c"},{q="Who is Magatha Grimtotem tied to?",a="Magatha commands the fierce warriors of the Grimtotem tribe, flanked constantly by her personal guards and servants. Outside her clan, she maintains an unusually close, active partnership with the Forsaken—working alongside Royal Apothecary Society figures like Apothecary Zamah—and maintains private connections with seers and agents across Kalimdor who operate outside Cairne's inner circle.",al={"magatha allies","who does magatha associate with","magatha connections"},it="ties",add="4e6ef5c4"},{q="Why is Magatha Grimtotem famous or feared?",a="Magatha was blessed with immense shamanic talent from childhood and has spent a lifetime translating that power into absolute authority over the Grimtotem. Many within Thunder Bluff fear her ruthless ambition, whispering that she arranged her own marriage to win leadership of her clan. Her willingness to employ dark remedies, meddle with vengeful spirits, and defy Cairne makes her one of the most intimidating figures in Mulgore.",al={"why is magatha feared","is magatha powerful","magatha reputation"},it="fame",add="92d0808b"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the Grimtotem's dark reputation. Magatha's presence on Elder Rise reminds you of the ideological divide threatening the united tribes.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you find a surprisingly warm welcome from the Elder Crone, who consults the Royal Apothecary Society in the Pools of Vision.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you face one of Kalimdor's most powerful practitioners, whose command of the primal elements few living tauren can rival.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you may find Magatha's aid and counsel valuable against regional threats. Her fierce clan loyalty and open contempt for other races make her an untrustworthy comrade."},kw={"arikara","bloodhoof","cairne","elder crone","elder rise","grimtotem","magatha","ragefire","thunder bluff","zamah"},rel={"npc:cairne-bloodhoof","topic:grimtotem-tribe","subzone:elder-rise","quest:1063","quest:1064","quest:5088","quest:5722","quest:853"},src={"Magatha Grimtotem"}}
E["npc:maur-raincaller"] = {t="npc",n="Maur Raincaller",z="thunderbluff",s="In Bloodhoof Village, Maur Raincaller watches over Mulgore’s herds and wild beasts. He attends to concerns tied to the plains’ natural and spiritual life.",h="In Bloodhoof Village, Maur Raincaller watches over Mulgore’s herds and wild beasts.",sec={{t="A Resident of Bloodhoof Village",b="Maur Raincaller lives near the heart of Bloodhoof Village, on the shore of Lake Stonebull. He watches over matters involving Mulgore’s wildlife and the balance of the elements. After the strider Mazzranache bites him and infects his wound, Maur asks young travelers to gather animal parts for a remedy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Maur Raincaller?",a="Maur Raincaller is a tauren who lives in Bloodhoof Village in Mulgore. He asks travelers to deal with unruly wildlife nearby.",al={"maur raincaller role","who is maur","maur raincaller lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Maur Raincaller?",a="Maur Raincaller can be found outdoors in Bloodhoof Village, among its tepees and hearth fires. The village lies south of Thunder Bluff, on the eastern bank of Lake Stonebull.",al={"maur raincaller location","where is maur","maur coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What trouble is Maur dealing with?",a="Maur Raincaller’s wound is infected after Mazzranache bites him. He asks travelers to bring parts from Mulgore’s wolves, cougars, plainstriders and swoops so he can make a remedy.",al={"maur raincaller quest","mazzranache problem","what does maur want"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Maur Raincaller on?",a="Maur Raincaller is a loyal tauren of the Bloodhoof tribe and an adherent of the Horde. Living in Bloodhoof Village, his loyalty rests firmly with High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof and the safety of Mulgore's plains.",al={"maur raincaller faction","is maur raincaller horde","who does maur serve"},it="side",add="fd24c378"},{q="Why is Maur Raincaller here in Bloodhoof Village?",a="Maur lives in Bloodhoof Village, the Bloodhoof tribe's home on the plains of Mulgore. After the fearsome strider Mazzranache bit him and the wound became infected, he stays in the village and asks travelers to bring him the beast parts he needs for a remedy.",al={"why is maur in bloodhoof village","maur raincaller purpose mulgore","what does maur do here"},it="why_here",add="231da345"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a young tauren leaving Camp Narache, you can help protect your people’s ancestral lands from wandering predators and disruptive beasts.",["class:Hunter"]="Maur Raincaller sends you to hunt wolves, cougars, plainstriders and swoops across the plains for parts to treat the bite Mazzranache gave him."},kw={"bloodhoof village","maur raincaller","mazzranache","mulgore","plainstrider","tauren"},rel={"quest:766","subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:mulgore","topic:tauren"},src={"Maur Raincaller"}}
E["npc:melor-stonehoof"] = {t="npc",n="Melor Stonehoof",z="thunderbluff",s="On Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Melor Stonehoof sets hunters to difficult trials. He sends Horde hunters after dangerous beasts across the Barrens and Thousand Needles to test their tracking and mettle.",h="On Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Melor Stonehoof sets hunters to difficult trials.",sec={{t="A Mentor of the Wilds",b="Melor Stonehoof watches the plains from Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. For the tauren, hunting joins survival with spiritual balance and respect for nature's greatest predators. Melor teaches those who carry bow and blade for the Horde to honor that balance, sending promising stalkers to test their craft against legendary beasts.",sp=0},{t="Trials of the Hunt",b="Melor sends hunters after elusive beasts that threaten the wilds. In the Barrens, they aid the huntress Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads, then pursue Steelsnap, a cunning and vicious hyena in Thousand Needles. These trials test whether hunters can outsmart and outfight the deadliest creatures of central Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The Monsters of Distant Lands",b="Hunters who prove their skill in the Barrens face beasts in distant lands. Melor sends seasoned hunters after Deadmire, an ancient crocolisk in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh, and Frostmaw, a savage yeti in the Alterac Mountains. Each hunt tests whether a stalker has mastered the Hunter's Way.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Melor Stonehoof?",a="Melor Stonehoof is on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. The mesa lies south of the main bluff of the tauren capital, reached by rope bridges.",al={"melor stonehoof location","where is melor","melor stonehoof coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What quests does Melor Stonehoof offer?",a="Melor offers a series of hunting challenges for mid-level adventurers. He directs hunters to Sergra Darkthorn in the Barrens, sends them after the ferocious hyena Steelsnap, and points them toward Deadmire in Dustwallow Marsh and Frostmaw in the Alterac Mountains.",al={"melor quests","what does melor do","melor stonehoof questline"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why does Melor send hunters after Steelsnap?",a="Steelsnap is a vicious, cunning hyena that stalks Thousand Needles. Melor sends capable hunters to track and slay him, testing their skill, endurance, and courage in the wild.",al={"why kill steelsnap","steelsnap quest lore"},it="motive"},{q="What is Deadmire?",a="Deadmire is an unusually large, aggressive crocolisk in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. Melor challenges hunters to slay it as a test of prowess.",al={"who is deadmire","deadmire lore","deadmire beast"},it="target"},{q="Do you need to be a hunter class to take his quests?",a="No. Melor offers his hunting trials to any capable adventurer fighting for the Horde. They reflect the hunter's way and suit the hunter class.",al={"melor hunters only","can other classes do melor quests"},gp=true},{q="Who is Sergra Darkthorn, and why does Melor send you to her?",a="Sergra Darkthorn is an orc huntress at the Crossroads in the Barrens. Melor sends promising hunters to aid her in subduing the plains' unruly predators and learn from another veteran of the wild.",al={"melor sergra connection","sergra darkthorn quest"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Melor Stonehoof?",a="Melor Stonehoof is a respected tauren hunter stationed on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff. Dedicated to the traditions of the hunt and the preservation of balance, he guides promising trackers across Kalimdor, testing their strength and cunning against the land's fiercest predators.",al={"who is melor stonehoof","melor stonehoof lore","who is melor"},it="identity",add="c4d46d44"},{q="Whose side is Melor Stonehoof on?",a="Melor is loyal to the tauren tribes and the Horde. From his perch high atop Thunder Bluff, he serves his people by mentoring Horde hunters and coordinating efforts against perilous beasts that threaten travelers and settlements across the Barrens and beyond.",al={"melor stonehoof faction","is melor horde","melor stonehoof loyalty"},it="side",add="d59647ad"},{q="What does Melor Stonehoof want?",a="Melor seeks to instruct hunters in the ancient ways of stalking, tracking, and honoring their quarry. He wants skilled trackers to prove themselves by hunting notorious beasts such as Steelsnap, Deadmire, and Frostmaw, and he works with allies like Sergra Darkthorn to test their mettle.",al={"melor stonehoof goal","what does melor want","melor stonehoof purpose"},it="wants",add="2962cc83"},{q="Why is Melor Stonehoof here in Thunder Bluff?",a="Melor makes his home on Hunter Rise, the natural gathering ground for the marksmen, trappers, and trackers of the tauren. From this vantage, he can observe incoming hunters, offer council, and dispatch tested warriors into the wilds to safeguard the land.",al={"why is melor on hunter rise","why is melor in thunder bluff","melor stonehoof location purpose"},it="why_here",add="6e964c49"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you follow Melor's tracking trials along the sacred path of the hunt.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see in Melor a deep reverence for the hunt, a trial of strength held in balance with the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you face the wild beasts that endanger settlements from Mulgore to Thousand Needles. Melor hardens warriors and stalkers for that work."},kw={"deadmire","frostmaw","hunter rise","hunter's way","melor","sergra darkthorn","steelsnap","stonehoof","thunder bluff"},rel={"subzone:hunter-rise","zone:thunderbluff","quest:861","quest:1131","quest:1205","quest:860","quest:1130","topic:tauren"},src={"Melor Stonehoof"}}
E["npc:miles-welsh"] = {t="npc",n="Miles Welsh",z="thunderbluff",s="In the Pools of Vision, Miles Welsh teaches priests beneath Thunder Bluff. The Forsaken trainer offers spiritual instruction and shadow discipline in the tauren capital.",h="In the Pools of Vision, Miles Welsh teaches priests beneath Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Shadow in the Caverns",b="Miles Welsh teaches priests in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff. Far from Lordaeron's plague-scarred ruins, the Forsaken priest makes his home in the grotto beneath the city. He instructs travelers in divine and shadowy energies. His place in the heart of Mulgore reflects the tenuous ties between the Forsaken and the Horde. There, he shares sanctuary with tauren mystics and shamans while guiding acolytes in shadow and faith.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Miles Welsh?",a="Miles Welsh trains priests in the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff. He helps Horde priests with their training and specialized disciplines.",al={"miles welsh role","who is miles welsh","miles welsh priest trainer"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Miles Welsh?",a="Find Miles Welsh in the Pools of Vision, the caverns beneath the Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff. Enter through a cave entrance on the mesa.",al={"miles welsh location","where is miles welsh","how to find miles welsh"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is an undead priest trainer in Thunder Bluff?",a="The Forsaken and tauren are allies in the Horde. Magatha Grimtotem advocated for the Forsaken to join, allowing emissaries and trainers like Miles Welsh to serve in Mulgore.",al={"why forsaken in thunder bluff","undead priest in tauren city"},it="why_here"},{q="What abilities does he teach?",a="Miles Welsh teaches general priest spells. He also helps Forsaken and troll acolytes seeking specialized racial teachings such as Touch of Weakness or Shadowguard.",al={"priest spells thunder bluff","what does miles welsh teach"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Miles Welsh on?",a="Miles Welsh stands with the Forsaken and the broader Horde. Though the tauren follow an entirely different spiritual path rooted in the Earth Mother, Miles resides beneath their mesa among their allies to offer his knowledge of the priesthood to Horde travelers who seek it.",al={"miles welsh faction","miles welsh horde or alliance","who does miles welsh serve"},it="side",add="c3aae6f3"},{q="What does Miles Welsh want?",a="Miles Welsh serves as an instructor to fellow priests who visit Thunder Bluff. Down in the secluded Pools of Vision, he shares his discipline and dark arts with those treading the path of shadow and faith, ensuring the Horde's disciples have guidance even far from Lordaeron.",al={"what does miles welsh do","miles welsh purpose","miles welsh goals"},it="wants",add="9239b409"},{q="Who is Miles Welsh tied to?",a="Miles Welsh is bound to the Forsaken of the Undercity. His presence in Thunder Bluff places him alongside the Forsaken emissaries and travelers welcomed to the tauren capital through the fledgling pact between Cairne Bloodhoof's people and Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's followers.",al={"miles welsh allies","who does miles welsh work for","miles welsh connections"},it="ties",add="03472250"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a priest traveling through Kalimdor, you can study new spells and advance your spiritual training with Miles Welsh, one of the few such teachers in central Horde territory.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead traveler, you may find Miles Welsh a familiar, cold face in the earthy, sun-drenched tauren capital."},kw={"devouring plague","forsaken","miles welsh","pools of vision","priest trainer","spirit rise","thunder bluff"},rel={"subzone:pools-of-vision","zone:thunderbluff","topic:forsaken","quest:5644","quest:5643"},src={"Miles Welsh"}}
E["npc:rahauro"] = {t="npc",n="Rahauro",z="thunderbluff",s="On Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, Rahauro sends Horde fighters against threats beneath Orgrimmar. He serves Magatha Grimtotem, coordinating the response to troggs in Ragefire Chasm and the search for a fallen agent’s possessions.",h="On Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, Rahauro sends Horde fighters against threats beneath Orgrimmar.",sec={{t="Voice of the Elder Crone",b="Rahauro attends Magatha Grimtotem on the high terrace of Elder Rise. He speaks and acts for the elder crone, who relies on trusted servants to recruit others. When wild creatures swarm beneath the orcish capital, Rahauro handles the arrangements and sends Horde mercenaries to face them.",sp=0},{t="Trouble in Ragefire Chasm",b="Troggs in the caverns of Ragefire Chasm rejected Magatha’s attempt to make peace. Her envoys went below Orgrimmar to parley, but the troggs attacked and killed them. Magatha sees the creatures as a threat to the Horde, and Rahauro sends champions into the caverns to thin their numbers and learn their strength.",sp=0},{t="The Fallen Envoy's Satchel",b="Maur Grimtotem served Magatha and was among those killed by the troggs. Before he died in Ragefire Chasm, Maur found something he meant to show his mistress. Rahauro sends explorers through the volcanic paths to recover Maur’s lost satchel and whatever findings it holds.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Rahauro?",a="Rahauro attends Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. He directs travelers to act for his mistress and the Horde.",al={"who is rahauro","rahauro lore","who is this tauren"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Rahauro?",a="You can find Rahauro on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, near Magatha Grimtotem.",al={"rahauro location","where is rahauro","find rahauro"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Rahauro want adventurers to go to Ragefire Chasm?",a="Magatha sent envoys to negotiate with the troggs beneath Orgrimmar, but the troggs killed them. Rahauro sends adventurers into Ragefire Chasm to thin their numbers and counter the threat to the Horde.",al={"rahauro ragefire","why send to ragefire","rahauro trogg quest"},it="wants"},{q="Who was Maur Grimtotem?",a="Maur Grimtotem served Magatha and went into Ragefire Chasm as her envoy. He found something noteworthy in the caves, but troggs killed him before he could bring it to her.",al={"maur grimtotem","who is maur","lost satchel guy"}},{q="What is inside the lost satchel Rahauro seeks?",a="The lost satchel holds something Maur Grimtotem discovered before his death. Rahauro wants it recovered from the trogg-infested caves and brought safely to Thunder Bluff.",al={"lost satchel contents","what is in the satchel","maur's satchel"}},{q="Does Rahauro belong to the Grimtotem tribe?",a="Rahauro attends Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise and oversees matters involving agents such as Maur. His service places him within Magatha’s retinue in Thunder Bluff.",al={"is rahauro grimtotem","rahauro tribe","rahauro faction"},it="side"},{q="Why is Rahauro on the Elder Rise?",a="Rahauro remains upon the heights of Elder Rise to attend directly to his mistress, Magatha Grimtotem. From this vantage in Thunder Bluff, he oversees her local interests and recruits capable Horde adventurers to deal with distant perils, such as the emerging trogg menace deep beneath Orgrimmar in Ragefire Chasm.",al={"why is rahauro here","rahauro purpose elder rise","what is rahauro doing in thunder bluff"},it="why_here",add="7ce6993c"},{q="Who is Rahauro tied to?",a="Rahauro is an attendant serving Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. He handles her affairs, coordinates efforts regarding her fallen servants such as Maur Grimtotem, and represents her interests within the broader Horde by dispatching champions to handle threats to their collective security.",al={"rahauro allegiance","who does rahauro work for","rahauro connections"},it="ties",add="ba00cb60"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can take on Rahauro’s early dungeon assignments in Thunder Bluff. They serve the tauren leadership and defend Orgrimmar, the orcish capital.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren on Thunder Bluff’s terraces, you can see how Magatha’s influence reaches beyond Elder Rise. Rahauro works within her inner circle."},kw={"elder rise","grimtotem","magatha","maur","ragefire chasm","rahauro","satchel","thunder bluff","troggs"},rel={"npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:maur-grimtotem","quest:5723","quest:5722","quest:5724","zone:ragefire","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Rahauro"}}
E["npc:tal"] = {t="npc",n="Tal",z="thunderbluff",s="At Thunder Bluff, Tal tends the Horde's chief wind rider roost above the plains of Mulgore. He sends seasoned wyverns carrying travelers across Kalimdor.",h="At Thunder Bluff, Tal tends the Horde's chief wind rider roost above the plains of Mulgore.",sec={{t="Keeper of the High Roost",b="Tal tends the wind rider roost on Thunder Bluff's central mesa, linking the tauren capital with the rest of the Horde. He cares for the loyal wind riders, or wyverns, keeping them healthy and well-fed for long journeys across Kalimdor. From the roost, he sends messengers to Camp Taurajo and scouts across the Barrens to Orgrimmar. The flights keep the towering mesa city in touch with its allies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What role does Tal play in Thunder Bluff?",a="Tal is Thunder Bluff's wind rider master. He oversees the roost atop the bluffs, cares for the winged beasts, and arranges flights across Kalimdor for members of the Horde.",al={"who is tal","tal flight master","what does tal do"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Tal send travelers?",a="Tal sends travelers from Thunder Bluff to places across central and southern Kalimdor, including Camp Taurajo, the Crossroads, Orgrimmar, and distant wilderness outposts.",al={"where can tal fly","tal destinations","thunder bluff flight paths"},gp=true},{q="Why are wind riders used instead of traditional mounts?",a="Wind riders are flying mounts that provide swift, direct travel into and out of Thunder Bluff. The city's sheer cliffs and great height make ground routes slow and winding, while the flyers avoid the need to use the elevators.",al={"why wyverns","thunder bluff flying beasts"}},{q="Who is Tal?",a="Tal is the tauren wind rider master stationed high upon the central roost of Thunder Bluff. As a flight master, he oversees the care, breeding, and dispatching of the city's winged wyverns, providing vital aerial transit for travelers journeying across Kalimdor.",al={"who is tal","tal identity","tal npc"},it="identity",add="704cf2c5"},{q="Whose side is Tal on?",a="Tal is steadfastly loyal to Thunder Bluff and the Horde. He offers his wind riders exclusively to members of the Horde and their allies, ensuring swift passage between Mulgore, the Barrens, and outposts across Kalimdor while denying access to the Alliance.",al={"tal faction","is tal horde","tal allegiances"},it="side",add="a57be0bc"},{q="What does Tal want?",a="Tal seeks to maintain Thunder Bluff's vital aerial lifelines. His priority is keeping his wind riders well-fed, calm, and ready for flight, while ensuring Horde couriers, scouts, and adventurers can traverse the rugged expanses of Kalimdor swiftly and safely.",al={"what does tal want","tal motive","tal goal"},it="wants",add="e868146f"},{q="Why is Tal here?",a="Tal tends the roost perched atop Thunder Bluff because the city's towering mesas are naturally suited for aerial departures and landings. From this central summit, his wind riders can catch the high updrafts and carry passengers across the plains of Mulgore and beyond.",al={"why is tal in thunder bluff","tal roost location","why here"},it="why_here",add="dfa35811"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren venturing beyond your ancestral pastures, you can rely on Tal for the quickest and safest passage from the high bluffs into the broader world.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use Tal's roost to travel between the tauren capital, the Crossroads, and Orgrimmar."},kw={"flight master","mulgore","roost","tal","thunder bluff","wind rider master","wyvern"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","quest:6363","quest:6364","subzone:bloodhoof-village","zone:orgrimmar","subzone:crossroads","topic:tauren"},src={"Tal"}}
E["npc:turak-runetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Turak Runetotem",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem guides young tauren toward nature and balance. From the Hall of Elders on Elder Rise, he assists Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and leads novices through trials to commune with spirits and master animal forms.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem guides young tauren toward nature and balance.",sec={{t="Voice of the Earthmother",b="In the Hall of Elders atop Thunder Bluff’s Elder Rise, Turak Runetotem guides those who seek the druid’s path. He assists Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem in bringing the ancient druidic arts back among the tauren. Turak teaches that a druid honors the Earthmother’s will. Strength of body must rest upon spiritual respect and harmony with nature.",sp=0},{t="The Path of the Claw",b="When fledgling druids are ready for animal forms, Turak sends them into the wider world. He teaches them to join the Cenarion Circle and travel by teleportation across Kalimdor to Moonglade. Turak remembers his own first communion with the Great Bear Spirit as bewildering and intense. To test his students’ courage, he sends them to face Lunaclaw and win the strength of body and heart required for the Path of the Claw.",sp=0},{t="Guardians of Balance",b="Turak teaches more than the primal forms of combat. He sends his disciples to Dendrite Starblaze to study poison, and Dendrite sends them to help animals poisoned near the Crossroads. Even Turak is surprised by the rash of poisonings.\n\nTurak also guides novices through arduous rites beneath the tides, where they awaken their aquatic form. These trials shape them into protectors able to heal Azeroth’s deepest wounds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Turak Runetotem?",a="Find Turak Runetotem in the Hall of Elders on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, alongside Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem.",al={"turak location","where is turak runetotem","turak runetotem thunder bluff"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What role does Turak play for new druids?",a="Turak teaches young tauren druids to reach Moonglade and guides them through trials for their Bear and Aquatic forms. He also teaches them to cure natural poisons.",al={"what does turak teach","turak druid trainer","turak role"},it="purpose"},{q="What is Turak's connection to Moonglade?",a="Turak teaches novice druids to teleport to Moonglade. There, Dendrite Starblaze offers advanced spiritual guidance through the Cenarion Circle.",al={"turak moonglade","how does turak know dendrite","teleport moonglade turak"},it="ties"},{q="How is Turak related to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Turak belongs to the Runetotem tribe and serves Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem as a trusted assistant and teacher in the Hall of Elders.",al={"is turak related to hamuul","hamuul and turak"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Turak send druids to the Crossroads?",a="Turak sends students to Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade to study poison. Dendrite sends them to help with animal poisonings near the Crossroads. When they return, Turak grants them the power to cure poison permanently.",al={"turak crossroads","turak poison quest","power over poison"},it="motive"},{q="What was Turak's personal experience with the Great Bear Spirit?",a="Turak recalls that his first communion with the Great Bear Spirit, on the path to becoming a Druid of the Claw, was bewildering and profoundly intense. The experience deepened his reverence for the form.",al={"turak bear spirit","turak path of the claw"},it="history"},{q="Who is Turak Runetotem?",a="Turak Runetotem is a wise and patient tauren druid trainer residing in the Hall of Elders on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. Serving as a trusted assistant to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem, he walks with profound balance in nature's presence. Turak devotes himself to guiding young Horde druids through their initial trials, helping them attune to the wild spirits and master the ancient teachings of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who is turak","turak runetotem lore","turak identity"},it="identity",add="fcca94f0"},{q="Whose side is Turak Runetotem on?",a="Turak is devoted both to the tauren of Thunder Bluff within the Horde and to the Cenarion Circle. He represents the growing druidic bond between the tauren and night elves, bridging the traditional loyalties of the Horde with the sacred, nonpartisan duty to heal and protect Azeroth's natural balance.",al={"turak faction","who does turak serve","turak loyalty"},it="side",add="d36f6346"},{q="What does Turak Runetotem want?",a="Turak seeks to nurture the next generation of tauren druids and safeguard the land from corruption. He wants initiates to understand the true essence of nature's power—urging them to commune with spirits like the Great Bear, overcome trials of body and heart, and use their gifts to cleanse poisons and restore harmony across Kalimdor.",al={"turak goals","what is turak's purpose","turak motive"},it="wants",add="b696f0bb"},{q="Why is Turak Runetotem here?",a="Turak is stationed in the Hall of Elders on Elder Rise to serve alongside Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. While Hamuul oversees the druidic communion for all tauren, Turak acts as his primary instructor on the high bluffs, personally preparing novice druids before sending them onward to Moonglade and wider duties across the Barrens.",al={"why is turak in thunder bluff","why is turak on elder rise","turak thunder bluff purpose"},it="why_here",add="83600788"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a tauren druid, you can learn from Turak Runetotem. He teaches the path to Moonglade and tests aspirants for their Bear and Aquatic forms.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share in the revival of druidic customs after the Third War. Turak Runetotem helps your people reclaim their ancient harmony with the Earthmother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can look to Turak Runetotem, who trains nature’s guardians to face blights, environmental corruption, and the lingering scars across Kalimdor."},kw={"aquatic form","bear form","dendrite starblaze","druid","elder rise","hall of elders","hamuul","lunaclaw","moonglade","runetotem","thunder bluff","turak"},rel={"subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","npc:dendrite-starblaze","quest:6001","quest:5921","quest:6125","quest:31","topic:druid"},src={"Turak Runetotem"}}
E["npc:zangen-stonehoof"] = {t="npc",n="Zangen Stonehoof",z="thunderbluff",s="At the High Rise bonfire, Zangen Stonehoof tends the flames and aids tauren kin across Kalimdor. Each evening, he keeps the central fire burning in Thunder Bluff.",h="At the High Rise bonfire, Zangen Stonehoof tends the flames and aids tauren kin across Kalimdor.",sec={{t="Keeper of the High Rise Flame",b="Zangen Stonehoof tends the communal bonfire atop Thunder Bluff's High Rise. Each evening, as twilight falls over Mulgore, he lights the fire above the city's highest bluffs. The flames give warmth to the tribes gathered beneath High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Zangen also keeps ties with allies beyond Mulgore's mesa, helping with spiritual and ritual work across the continent.",sp=0},{t="Aiding the Cliffrunners",b="Zangen helps Rau Cliffrunner, who is stationed south in Thousand Needles. When Rau needed water from a night elf moonwell for sacred rituals, Zangen enlisted dependable Horde adventurers to cross the contested forests of Ashenvale. They secured a filled phial from the ancient groves and sent it south to Freewind Post. Zangen helps preserve ancient rites and support scattered tauren posts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Zangen Stonehoof?",a="Zangen Stonehoof tends the central bonfire on Thunder Bluff's High Rise. Each evening, he keeps it burning and organizes aid and deliveries for distant kin across Kalimdor.",al={"who is zangen","zangen stonehoof","what does zangen do"},it="identity"},{q="What does Zangen do with the bonfire?",a="Each evening around nightfall, Zangen lights the great bonfire beside him on the High Rise. Its flames give light and warmth to the upper terrace.",al={"why is zangen near the fire","zangen bonfire","lighting the fire"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Zangen need moonwell water from Ashenvale?",a="Zangen acts for Rau Cliffrunner, stationed at Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Rau needs water from an Ashenvale moonwell for a sacred ritual, so Zangen sends travelers to retrieve it and carry it south.",al={"zangen moonwell quest","the sacred flame","why moonwell water"},it="wants"},{q="Where can Zangen Stonehoof be found?",a="Zangen Stonehoof stands beside the communal fire pit at the center of Thunder Bluff's High Rise, on the upper mesa.",al={"zangen location","find zangen stonehoof","where is zangen"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Zangen Stonehoof on?",a="Zangen Stonehoof is fully devoted to the Horde and his fellow tauren. From his post on the High Rise in Thunder Bluff, he aids his people by coordinating with allies like Rau Cliffrunner and enlisting capable Horde travelers to assist in sacred tasks across Kalimdor.",al={"zangen stonehoof faction","is zangen horde","who does zangen serve"},it="side",add="44db2024"},{q="Who is Zangen Stonehoof tied to?",a="Zangen works closely with Rau Cliffrunner, an associate stationed out in the harsh expanse of Thousand Needles. When Rau requires sacred materials—such as potent moonwell water from the forests of Ashenvale—Zangen acts as his liaison in the capital, finding travelers willing to undertake the journey.",al={"zangen stonehoof associates","who works with zangen stonehoof","rau cliffrunner zangen"},it="ties",add="edd8b42e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, Zangen links Mulgore's civic center with distant kin, including the Cliffrunners in Thousand Needles.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler in Thunder Bluff, you can turn to Zangen for help reaching contested regions such as Ashenvale."},kw={"bonfire","high rise","moonwell water","rau cliffrunner","the sacred flame","thunder bluff","zangen stonehoof"},rel={"subzone:high-rise","zone:thunderbluff","npc:rau-cliffrunner","quest:1195","zone:ashenvale","zone:thousandneedles","topic:tauren","topic:horde"},src={"Zangen Stonehoof"}}
E["quest:1063"] = {t="quest",n="The Elder Crone",z="thunderbluff",s="Seereth Stonebreak sends word from Stonetalon to Thunder Bluff. Enraged by goblin deforestation and mining, the mountain's elements need spiritual guidance, so Seereth sends emissaries to seek counsel from Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise.",h="Seereth Stonebreak sends word from Stonetalon to Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="Cry from Stonetalon",b="Goblin deforestation and mining have enraged the elemental spirits of Stonetalon Mountains. Seereth Stonebreak sees that force alone cannot ease the land's spiritual anguish and turns to elder shamans for wisdom. Seereth knows few tribal leaders by name, but knows of Magatha Grimtotem, an elder famed for her knowledge and commanding presence.",sp=0},{t="Audience on Elder Rise",b="Magatha Grimtotem holds court atop Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, where shamanic and spiritual affairs gather. The Grimtotem tribe's relationship with Cairne Bloodhoof's leadership is tense and often confrontational. Even so, Magatha is a formidable elder whose counsel carries great weight across the Horde. You bring Stonetalon's troubles to her, seeking her guidance.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Alliance",b="Magatha Grimtotem sends word of the elemental turmoil to the Forsaken alchemists living in the city rather than relying only on traditional tauren rites. She draws the Horde's newest and most cynical allies into Kalimdor's spiritual affairs, showing a cunning and unconventional way of handling power and problems.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who sends me to find Magatha?",a="Seereth Stonebreak, in Stonetalon Mountains, sends you after you fight the Venture Company goblins cutting through the mountain forests.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","seereth stonebreak"}},{q="Where is Magatha Grimtotem located?",a="Magatha Grimtotem lives atop Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, on the northeastern bluff linked to the central mesa by wooden bridges.",al={"magatha location","where is magatha","elder rise"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Seereth asking an elder tauren for help?",a="Goblin industry has disturbed Stonetalon's spirits. Seereth sees that force alone cannot heal the land and seeks spiritual guidance to calm the elements.",al={"why elder crone","why consult magatha"},it="motive"},{q="Who is Magatha Grimtotem?",a="Magatha Grimtotem is the elder crone and matriarch of the Grimtotem tribe. Her tribe is fiercely aggressive and skeptical of the united Horde, while Magatha holds great political and spiritual influence atop Thunder Bluff.",al={"elder crone lore","who is the elder crone","magatha background"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after speaking with Magatha?",a="Magatha hears your report on Stonetalon and sends you to Apothecary Zamah, a Forsaken emissary in the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise, for help.",al={"what next","quest follow up"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is this quest called 'The Elder Crone'?",a="The title refers to Magatha Grimtotem. Her own clan and the wider tauren people know her as the Elder Crone for her great age, shamanic knowledge, and authority as matriarch.",al={"why crone","elder crone title"},it="name"},{q="Why does Seereth Stonebreak send an adventurer to Thunder Bluff instead of going herself?",a="Seereth Stonebreak remains stationed in Stonetalon Mountains overseeing the immediate defense and spiritual restoration of the land against Venture Company logging. As an orc shaman tied to the frontier, she cannot abandon her post to make the long journey across the Barrens to Thunder Bluff. She relies on traveling champions of the Horde to carry word of Stonetalon's peril directly to the tauren elders on her behalf.",al={"why send me","why can't seereth go","why seereth need player"},it="why_me",add="9e600b44"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see how fragile the balance is between Cairne's united tribes and the aloof, fiercely traditional Grimtotem, who dwell in Thunder Bluff.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you know the weight of Stonetalon's elemental unrest. Seeking Magatha's counsel on Elder Rise reflects the spiritual crisis in Kalimdor's peaks.",["faction:Horde"]="You see the Horde's ties at work as Stonetalon's frontier troubles reach the high halls of Thunder Bluff's leadership."},kw={"elder crone","elder rise","grimtotem","magatha","seereth stonebreak","spirits","stonetalon","tauren","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:seereth-stonebreak","quest:1062","quest:1064","quest:1061","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","zone:stonetalon"},m={start="Seereth Stonebreak",["end"]="Magatha Grimtotem",level="18",faction="Horde",id=1063},src={"The Elder Crone"}}
E["quest:1064"] = {t="quest",n="Forsaken Aid",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, Magatha Grimtotem sends you to seek help for Stonetalon's blighted spirits. She turns to Apothecary Zamah, the Forsaken emissary in the Pools of Vision, to bring tauren and undead knowledge together.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Magatha Grimtotem sends you to seek help for Stonetalon's blighted spirits.",sec={{t="A Pragmatic Partnership",b="Magatha Grimtotem sees practical value in the Forsaken alliance. When word reaches Thunder Bluff of corrupted elemental spirits and suffering land in the Stonetalon Mountains, she turns to the undead for help. She believes those who understand disease can help cure it, so she sends you to the Royal Apothecary Society instead of seeking traditional druidic remedies.",sp=0},{t="Beneath the Spirit Rise",b="Apothecary Zamah represents Undercity interests on Kalimdor from the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise. Tauren shamans, priests, and seers use the cavern as a sacred retreat, and Zamah's presence brings Forsaken work into their midst. Magatha sends a serpent messenger ahead of you to alert Zamah, opening a direct line to the Forsaken's alchemical researchers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Magatha Grimtotem consulting the Forsaken about Stonetalon?",a="Magatha believes the Forsaken's knowledge of plagues and disease can help diagnose and treat the sickness in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"why forsaken aid","magatha and the undead","why ask forsaken"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Apothecary Zamah be found?",a="Apothecary Zamah lives in the Pools of Vision, an underground cavern beneath Spirit Rise on Thunder Bluff's northwestern bluff. A cave tunnel near the pool on the mesa above leads inside.",al={"apothecary zamah location","where is zamah","pools of vision entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens when you accept the quest from Magatha?",a="When you accept Magatha's request, she summons a Serpent Messenger. It slithers and flies across Thunder Bluff toward Apothecary Zamah to announce your arrival.",al={"serpent messenger","magatha snake"},gp=true},{q="How do the Forsaken feel about helping the tauren in Stonetalon?",a="Apothecary Zamah expresses sympathy for Stonetalon's troubled spirits. She says the Forsaken are eager to help and strengthen their bond with the Horde.",al={"forsaken motives stonetalon","why zamah helps"},it="allies"},{q="What quest line follows after speaking with Zamah?",a="After you meet Zamah, the investigation turns to Forsaken alchemy and eventually leads to Journey to Tarren Mill in the Eastern Kingdoms, where you consult higher-ranking apothecaries.",al={"what comes next","next quest after forsaken aid"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken stationed inside the sacred Pools of Vision?",a="The Pools of Vision host Horde scholars, mages, and seers. Apothecary Zamah works there as an official emissary and researcher, keeping her controversial experiments away from the main thoroughfares.",al={"why are undead in pools of vision","spirit rise undead"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Magatha send you instead of consulting Apothecary Zamah herself?",a="As an Elder Crone of the Grimtotem tribe and a prominent leader atop the Elder Rise, Magatha Grimtotem relies on independent adventurers to carry out sensitive, ground-level business across Thunder Bluff. Dispatching an able courier not only tests your reliability in tribal matters, but it also establishes direct contact between an active Horde operative and Apothecary Zamah beneath the Spirit Rise.",al={"why me forsaken aid","why magatha send adventurer zamah","why does magatha need me"},it="why_me",add="5f2f83c5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Tauren often look to druidism and the Earth Mother to heal the land. Magatha's turn to undead alchemists shows her unconventional approach to tribal diplomacy.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, offering alchemical aid to the tauren is a chance to prove their worth and earn trust within a wary Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde's aid to the tauren links Kalimdor and Lordaeron in an alliance shaped since the Third War."},kw={"apothecary zamah","forsaken aid","magatha grimtotem","pools of vision","serpent messenger","spirit rise","stonetalon mountains","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:magatha-grimtotem","quest:853","subzone:pools-of-vision","quest:1063","quest:1065","quest:1061","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:spirit-rise"},m={start="Magatha Grimtotem",["end"]="Apothecary Zamah",level="18",faction="Horde",id=1064},src={"Forsaken Aid"}}
E["quest:1065"] = {t="quest",n="Journey to Tarren Mill",z="thunderbluff",s="Apothecary Zamah seeks a way to drive the Venture Company from Stonetalon Mountains without open war. She sends you across the sea to Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill, where the Royal Apothecary Society works in Lordaeron.",h="Apothecary Zamah seeks a way to drive the Venture Company from Stonetalon Mountains without open war.",sec={{t="A Plea Across the Great Sea",b="In Thunder Bluff, Apothecary Zamah is a link between the Forsaken and the Earth Mother's children. The Venture Company is logging and mining the sacred lands of Stonetalon Mountains, and the tauren have found that ordinary methods will not stop them. Zamah turns to her peers in the Royal Apothecary Society for a chemical deterrent. She hopes their alchemy can drive the company out without a drawn-out war.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Hillsbrad",b="You cross the sea from Kalimdor by zeppelin toward Lordaeron and the Undercity. From Tirisfal Glades, the road leads south through Silverpine Forest and into the contested Hillsbrad Foothills. Tarren Mill lies near human farmsteads and ruins. Once a human hamlet, it is now a Forsaken stronghold and a place where the Royal Apothecary Society carries out its research.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Lydon's Craft",b="Apothecary Lydon works in Tarren Mill with volatile chemistry and biological agents. Lydon sometimes tests mixtures on living subjects. Zamah's note explains the problem with the Venture Company, and Lydon eagerly takes it up. The Society welcomes a chance to test its compounds in a new place, and Lydon begins preparing reagents for the goblins.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah send me all the way to Tarren Mill?",a="Apothecary Zamah needs a concoction to drive the Venture Company from Stonetalon Mountains without open war. Her colleague Apothecary Lydon works with the Royal Apothecary Society in Tarren Mill and can prepare the alchemical compounds she needs.",al={"why go to tarren mill","why send to lydon","journey to tarren mill purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Tarren Mill located?",a="Tarren Mill is in the northern Hillsbrad Foothills on Lordaeron. From Kalimdor, take a zeppelin from Durotar to the Undercity in Tirisfal Glades, then travel south through Silverpine Forest and east into Hillsbrad.",al={"where is tarren mill","tarren mill location","how do i get to tarren mill"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are Apothecary Zamah and Apothecary Lydon?",a="Apothecary Zamah and Apothecary Lydon belong to the Forsaken Royal Apothecary Society. Zamah works in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff, studying local plants and helping the tauren, while Lydon conducts alchemical and plague experiments in Tarren Mill.",al={"who is zamah","who is lydon","who are the apothecaries"},it="people"},{q="Why are the Forsaken helping with the Venture Company in Stonetalon?",a="The Forsaken joined the Horde for survival and convenience, and the tauren spoke up to secure their place in the faction. Helping the tauren against the Venture Company strengthens that alliance and gives Forsaken alchemists a place to test their work.",al={"why do forsaken care about stonetalon","undead helping tauren stonetalon"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society is an order of Forsaken alchemists and scientists based beneath the ruins of Lordaeron in the Undercity. Under Lady Sylvanas Windrunner's direction, they develop elixirs, poisons, and blight strains to defend the Forsaken and destroy their enemies.",al={"what is the royal apothecary society","forsaken apothecaries lore"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after delivering the note to Lydon?",a="After receiving Zamah's request, Apothecary Lydon begins preparing a solution. To make a suitable mixture, you need to collect vials of innocent blood from the Syndicate shadow mages at Durnholde Keep.",al={"next quest after journey to tarren mill","what does lydon need"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah need an adventurer to deliver the note?",a="Apothecary Zamah is stationed on the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff as an emissary of the Royal Apothecary Society. Her work requires maintaining her presence among the suspicious tauren and managing her ongoing alchemical duties in Kalimdor. Sending an independent courier across the sea to Tarren Mill is far more practical than abandoning her delicate diplomatic and research post.",al={"why send me","why cant zamah go","why does zamah need me"},it="why_me",add="f7a71381"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, the defilement of Stonetalon cuts deep. Accepting Forsaken alchemy means making uneasy compromises to protect your sacred lands.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you see how the Royal Apothecary Society carries its chemical knowledge across the sea to help distant Horde allies.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you travel between Thunder Bluff and Tarren Mill, joining young defenders to allies across the sea."},kw={"apothecary lydon","apothecary zamah","hillsbrad","journey to tarren mill","stonetalon","tarren mill","thunder bluff","undercity","venture company"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","zone:hillsbrad","quest:1064","quest:853","topic:venture-company","zone:undercity","zone:tirisfal","topic:lordaeron"},m={start="Apothecary Zamah",["end"]="Apothecary Lydon",level="18",faction="Horde",id=1065},src={"Journey to Tarren Mill"}}
E["quest:1066"] = {t="quest",n="Blood of Innocents",z="thunderbluff",s="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks blood for a plan against the Venture Company in Stonetalon Mountains. The Royal Apothecary Society uses dark ingredients gathered from local bandits to pacify the encroaching company.",h="Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill seeks blood for a plan against the Venture Company in Stonetalon Mountains.",sec={{t="A Chemical Solution",b="The Horde faces a steady struggle in the Stonetalon Mountains, where the Venture Company ravages the wilderness and its people. Apothecary Lydon proposes an alchemical remedy instead of sending armies to blunt their axes. He plans to brew an agent that paralyzes and pacifies the mercenaries, leaving them weak and docile.",sp=0},{t="Stolen from the Wicked",b="Apothecary Lydon needs a rare and troubling ingredient: the blood of innocents. He avoids sending Horde agents to kill innocents himself and instead turns to the crimes of the Syndicate. Fallen nobles and cutthroats occupy Durnholde Keep, where rogue shadow mages harvest innocent blood for profane rituals. Lydon makes those mages his target for alchemical supplies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon need innocent blood?",a="Apothecary Lydon needs innocent blood as a key ingredient in an experimental brew. He hopes to make a toxin that drains the Venture Company's violent drive in Stonetalon Mountains, leaving its members subdued and easier to handle.",al={"what is innocent blood for","why blood of innocents","lydon blood quest"},it="motive"},{q="Who has the vials of innocent blood?",a="Syndicate shadow mages carry the vials of innocent blood. They lurk among the ruins of Durnholde Keep, southeast of Tarren Mill, and keep the blood for their own spellwork.",al={"who drops the blood","where to get blood of innocents","innocent blood location"},it="target"},{q="Why does a Hillsbrad quest involve the Stonetalon Mountains?",a="Horde leaders in Kalimdor sought scientific aid from the Royal Apothecary Society in the Eastern Kingdoms. The Venture Company conflict is in Stonetalon, while Apothecary Lydon in Tarren Mill has the dark craft needed to brew a specialized remedy.",al={"connection to stonetalon","why tarren mill stonetalon"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Syndicate?",a="The Syndicate is made up of former human nobles from the ruined kingdom of Alterac, now brigands, assassins, and cutthroats. Hoping to reclaim their lost lands, they use extortion and dark magic, and prey on travelers in Hillsbrad and Alterac.",al={"who are the syndicate","syndicate lore"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Durnholde Keep located?",a="Durnholde Keep lies southeast of Tarren Mill in the Hillsbrad Foothills. Once a human fortress and orc internment camp, it is now half in ruins and a major stronghold for the Syndicate.",al={"find durnholde keep","where is durnholde"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the Horde committing murder to get this blood?",a="No. The Royal Apothecary Society accepts gruesome methods, but Lydon directs agents to gather blood already harvested by Syndicate shadow mages from their victims.",al={"did horde kill innocents","innocent blood source"},it="threat"},{q="What is the Vial of Innocent Blood for?",a="Apothecary Lydon needs the vials of innocent blood to brew a specialized concoction for the Royal Apothecary Society. Rather than killing outright, his planned toxin is formulated to pacify the aggressive Venture Company operating in the Stonetalon Mountains, draining their will to fight and leaving them docile.",al={"vial of innocent blood use","what does innocent blood do","innocent blood purpose"},it="item",add="b5439bfd"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, efficiency comes before moral qualms. Lydon's calculated approach shows how the Royal Apothecary Society uses cold logic to solve problems for their living allies.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you may find the taking of innocent blood unsettling. The goal is to end the Venture Company's destruction of the wilderness in Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see its far-reaching ties at work: Forsaken alchemy in Lordaeron helps protect Horde lands in Kalimdor."},kw={"apothecary lydon","blood of innocents","durnholde keep","shadow mages","stonetalon mountains","syndicate","tarren mill","venture company"},rel={"subzone:tarren-mill","subzone:durnholde-keep","quest:1065","topic:syndicate","topic:venture-company","topic:horde"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1066,ri={"Vial of Innocent Blood"}},src={"Blood of Innocents (quest)"}}
E["quest:1067"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Thunder Bluff",z="thunderbluff",s="Apothecary Lydon’s toxin is bound for Thunder Bluff, where Zamah awaits it. She needs the formula to make a device that can spread it against the Venture Company.",h="Apothecary Lydon’s toxin is bound for Thunder Bluff, where Zamah awaits it.",sec={{t="A Transcontinental Delivery",b="Apothecary Lydon has made the toxin from the ingredients gathered in the Hillsbrad Foothills. He wants to see it tested on living subjects, but the liquid needs a way to spread it. You carry the vial across the Great Sea to Mulgore, where Apothecary Zamah waits for it.",sp=0},{t="Zamah's Apparatus",b="Apothecary Zamah works beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff as an ambassador and researcher for the Royal Apothecary Society. With Lydon's formula, she makes an aerosol device called the Toxic Fogger. She intends to use it against the Venture Company goblins.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of bringing the toxin to Thunder Bluff?",a="Lydon made the liquid toxin, but it needs a way to spread across a broad area. Zamah can turn the formula into an aerosol device called the Toxic Fogger.",al={"why thunder bluff","what does zamah do with toxin","lydons toxin use"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is the target of this concoction?",a="The toxin is meant for the Venture Company, a goblin mining syndicate whose operations reach the Stonetalon Mountains and beyond.",al={"who gets poisoned","target of lydon toxin","who are we fighting"},it="target"},{q="Where is Apothecary Zamah located?",a="Apothecary Zamah is in the Pools of Vision, beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"find zamah","where is apothecary zamah","zamah location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are Undercity apothecaries working in a Tauren city?",a="The Tauren gave the Forsaken asylum and helped them join the Horde, hoping they might find a cure for their affliction. Zamah represents the Royal Apothecary Society, whose work here turns toward pestilence and weapons rather than healing.",al={"forsaken in thunder bluff","why are undead in thunder bluff","apothecaries in mulgore"},it="why_here"},{q="What happens after turning in the toxin?",a="After Zamah receives the vial, she makes the Toxic Fogger. She then sends you to use it at a Venture Company facility in the Stonetalon Mountains.",al={"next quest","what after return to thunder bluff","fogger quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who created the original formula?",a="Apothecary Lydon, a Royal Apothecary Society researcher in Tarren Mill, made the poison.",al={"who made the poison","who is lydon","apothecary lydon lore"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Apothecary Lydon want this done?",a="Apothecary Lydon is eager to see his concoctions put to practical use in the field. His toxin is meant to bleed the violence from the Venture Company, leaving them weak and docile, but it cannot be deployed effectively on its own. Sending it back to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff allows her to create a proper delivery method that maximizes its effect, with favorable, perhaps even contagious, results.",al={"why does lydon want this","lydon motive","apothecary lydon reason"},it="motive",add="4bd277bc"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, you can see how the Royal Apothecary Society links research in Lordaeron with outposts on Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you know Magatha Grimtotem and the elders welcomed the Forsaken to Thunder Bluff, hoping they would find redemption or healing. The apothecaries beneath Spirit Rise instead make contagious weapons.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see Forsaken alchemists working together against the Venture Company's destructive operations."},kw={"apothecary lydon","apothecary zamah","lydon's toxin","pools of vision","return to thunder bluff","royal apothecary society","tarren mill","toxic fogger","venture company"},rel={"quest:853","quest:1086","zone:thunderbluff","topic:venture-company"},m={start="Apothecary Lydon",["end"]="Apothecary Zamah",level="23",faction="Horde",id=1067},src={"Return to Thunder Bluff (1)"}}
E["quest:1130"] = {t="quest",n="Melor Sends Word",z="thunderbluff",s="Jorn Skyseer brings word from Melor Stonehoof to promising hunters in the Barrens. Those who have proved their grit across Kalimdor are called to Hunter's Rise in Thunder Bluff for a harder trial.",h="Jorn Skyseer brings word from Melor Stonehoof to promising hunters in the Barrens.",sec={{t="A Summons to Thunder Bluff",b="Across the Barrens, Jorn Skyseer watches the crossings and encampments. He carries word from the elders of Hunter's Rise to hunters and warriors who have shown promise in the surrounding lands. Melor Stonehoof, a revered tauren mentor, has marked out a path for them.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Hunt",b="At Hunter's Rise in Thunder Bluff, you meet Melor Stonehoof. The elder hunter asks if you have the resolve to venture into distant, perilous wilderness. His summons opens trials far beyond the safety of Mulgore, where hunters face the continent's fiercest predators.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Melor Stonehoof?",a="Melor Stonehoof is a veteran tauren hunter on Hunter's Rise in Thunder Bluff. He judges rising trackers and warriors of the Horde, then sends worthy candidates across Kalimdor to track and hunt notorious beasts.",al={"melor","who is melor","melor stonehoof lore"},it="identity"},{q="Who delivers this summons?",a="Jorn Skyseer, a tauren beastmaster at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens, carries the message. He watches over travelers and sends those who have shown courage to Thunder Bluff to speak with Melor.",al={"who starts quest","jorn skyseer","who sent for me"}},{q="Where can I find Melor Stonehoof?",a="Melor is on Hunter's Rise, the southern mesa of Thunder Bluff devoted to tauren hunters, trackers, and beastmasters.",al={"melor location","where is melor","hunters rise thunder bluff"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What path is Melor planning for me?",a="Melor tests your endurance and hunting instincts with difficult tracking expeditions. The first sends you across Thousand Needles to hunt Steelsnap, a vicious hyena tyrant.",al={"what does melor want","next quest after melor sends word","melor chain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Melor recruit adventurers from the Barrens?",a="Surviving the Barrens' harsh predators, quilboar, and centaur shows that you have the instincts for elite hunts. Melor seeks those who can track elusive, deadly prey in unfamiliar lands.",al={"why me","why does melor care"},it="motive"},{q="Is this trial restricted to hunters?",a="Melor's trial is open to any Horde adventurer who has proved strength and resourcefulness in the wild. It begins on Hunter's Rise and tests the virtues of a tracker.",al={"is this a hunter quest","can other classes do this"},gp=true},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer send you to Melor Stonehoof?",a="Jorn Skyseer acts as a messenger and mentor in the Barrens, keeping an eye out for capable adventurers who prove their strength. Having witnessed your deeds across the plains, he recognizes that you have outgrown local tasks and directs you to Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, where Melor Stonehoof prepares worthy hunters for far greater trials across Kalimdor.",al={"why jorn sends word","why does jorn want me to see melor","jorn skyseer motive"},it="motive",add="2189d60f"},{q="Why does Jorn Skyseer choose you specifically?",a="Word of your accomplishments in the Barrens has reached the elders. Melor Stonehoof does not summon ordinary scouts or city guards; he seeks out tested wanderers who have demonstrated the skill and endurance necessary to track down the fiercest beasts in distant lands. Jorn singles you out because your reputation proves you are ready for Melor's path.",al={"why me melor sends word","why pick me jorn skyseer","why is melor calling me"},it="why_me",add="e1bd22c0"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, answering Melor's call is a traditional rite of adulthood and standing. You prove your mastery of the Hunt and bring honor to Hunter's Rise.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you see tauren beastcraft in Melor Stonehoof. He demands precision, patience, and respect for dangerous quarry.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you know Camp Taurajo and Thunder Bluff rely on skilled field operatives to manage dangerous predators near supply routes and outposts."},kw={"barrens","camp taurajo","hunter's rise","jorn skyseer","melor sends word","melor stonehoof","steelsnap","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:melor-stonehoof","quest:1131","quest:3261","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Jorn Skyseer",["end"]="Melor Stonehoof",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1130},src={"Melor Sends Word"}}
E["quest:1131"] = {t="quest",n="Steelsnap",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thousand Needles, Melor Stonehoof sends you after a hyena whose pack terrorizes the wildlife. Steelsnap's hunt breaks with the usual reasons tauren take a life.",h="In Thousand Needles, Melor Stonehoof sends you after a hyena whose pack terrorizes the wildlife.",sec={{t="A Hunt Outside the Blessing",b="Tauren hunters take life for sustenance, honor, or wisdom from the Earthmother. Melor Stonehoof asks you to hunt Steelsnap for another reason. The hyena is seen as a threat to nature's balance, bringing senseless violence and fear instead of keeping the cycle of life.",sp=0},{t="The Scourge of the Needles",b="Steelsnap roams the canyons of northern Thousand Needles, south of the centaur enclave at Camp E'thok. Fierce hyenas follow him, and together they attack the gentler wildlife on the canyon floor. Slaying Steelsnap and bringing back his rib will end his hold over the needles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Melor Stonehoof want Steelsnap killed?",a="Melor Stonehoof wants Steelsnap killed because he threatens the natural balance with senseless violence. Tauren hunts usually serve sustenance, honor, or wisdom from the Earthmother; this one aims to stop his attacks on the wildlife.",al={"why kill steelsnap","melor stonehoof reason","steelsnap motive"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Steelsnap be found?",a="Steelsnap roams northern Thousand Needles, south of Camp E'thok, the centaur enclave.",al={"steelsnap location","where is steelsnap","find steelsnap"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What proof must be brought back to Thunder Bluff?",a="Bring Steelsnap's Rib to Melor Stonehoof on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"steelsnap trophy","steelsnap objective","what do i loot"},it="item"},{q="Does Steelsnap fight alone?",a="No. Other hyenas follow Steelsnap and fight at his side.",al={"is steelsnap solo","steelsnap pack","steelsnap adds"},gp=true},{q="How does this hunt differ from traditional tauren hunts?",a="Tauren hunts usually serve sustenance, honor, or wisdom from the Earthmother. This hunt aims to stop a predator that disrupts the natural balance.",al={"tauren hunting philosophy","earthmother hunting","hunt lesson"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does Melor Stonehoof dwell?",a="Melor Stonehoof lives on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, where he instructs hunters and tests seasoned trackers.",al={"melor stonehoof location","where is melor","melor coords"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What kind of beast is Steelsnap?",a="Steelsnap is a vicious, tyrannical hyena prowling the canyon floor of Thousand Needles. Unlike ordinary beasts of the wild, he leads a pack of scavengers in senseless bloodshed, terrorizing gentler creatures and disrupting the natural balance. Melor Stonehoof considers him a foul creature cast entirely outside the Earthmother's blessing.",al={"who is steelsnap","what is steelsnap","steelsnap hyena"},it="target",add="1c130f9f"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For the Shu'halo, taking a beast's life carries spiritual weight. Hunting Steelsnap teaches you to cull a creature whose cruelty falls outside the Earthmother's grace.",["class:Hunter"]="Hunting Steelsnap tests your skill at tracking down a savage pack leader among the hyenas roaming the canyon floor.",["faction:Horde"]="Clearing a safer path through Thousand Needles protects supply lines and travelers heading from the Barrens toward Shimmering Flats."},kw={"camp e'thok","earthmother","hunter rise","hyena","melor stonehoof","steelsnap","thousand needles","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:melor-stonehoof","quest:1130","zone:thousandneedles","subzone:hunter-rise","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:camp-e-thok","zone:barrens"},m={start="Melor Stonehoof",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1131,ri={"Steelsnap's Rib"}},src={"Steelsnap (quest)"}}
E["quest:1195"] = {t="quest",n="The Sacred Flame",z="thunderbluff",s="Zangen Stonehoof sends the Horde after a sacred flame and an ancient relic. To aid Rau Cliffrunner in Thousand Needles, you seek a moonwell phial in Ashenvale.",h="Zangen Stonehoof sends the Horde after a sacred flame and an ancient relic.",sec={{t="Centaur Relics and Elven Waters",b="The Galak centaur guard an ancient relic in Thousand Needles. Their artifact dates to the creation of their race, and they protect it with sacred flames. Zangen Stonehoof needs water touched by lunar divinity to extinguish those flames. He sends you north to Ashenvale, where the ancestral forests hold the moonwell water he seeks.",sp=0},{t="Trespassing in Ashenvale",b="Pure moonwell water needs a vessel that will not corrupt it. You seek an etched phial from the Laughing Sisters, dryads near Raynewood Retreat. Then you submerge the phial in a moonwell along the western banks of the Falfarren River and carry it back to Mulgore.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Zangen Stonehoof need moonwell water?",a="Zangen needs moonwell water for his associate Rau Cliffrunner in Thousand Needles. Rau plans to use its potent magic to extinguish the sacred flame guarded by the hostile Galak centaur, so the Horde can recover an ancient relic.",al={"why moonwell water","purpose of moonwell water","why get water from ashenvale"},it="motive"},{q="Where can the etched phial be found?",a="The etched phial is carried by the Laughing Sisters, dryads who wander the woods around Raynewood Retreat in central Ashenvale, just off the northern road leading west from Splintertree Post.",al={"where is etched phial","how to get etched phial","phial location"},gp=true},{q="Which moonwell should be used to fill the phial?",a="The moonwell lies near the western bank of the Falfarren River, south of the main road across central Ashenvale.",al={"which moonwell","moonwell location","where to fill phial"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who are the Galak centaur?",a="The Galak are an aggressive centaur clan in the dusty expanses of Thousand Needles. They guard an ancient relic from the founding era of their kind, ringed by a sacred bonfire that Zangen and Rau intend to douse.",al={"galak tribe","galak centaur","who are galak"},it="history"},{q="Who receives the filled phial after Zangen?",a="After Zangen inspects the filled phial in Thunder Bluff, he sends you south to Thousand Needles to deliver it to Rau Cliffrunner, who requested it.",al={"who is rau","where does the water go next","next step after zangen"},it="next_step"},{q="Why kill dryads for their phials?",a="Dryad vessels are specially made to hold pure, enchanted liquids without tainting them. Ordinary bottles cannot safely carry water imbued with the celestial energies of a night elf moonwell.",al={"why attack dryads","why laughing sisters","dryad vessels"},it="hostile"},{q="What is the Filled Etched Phial for?",a="The phial holds sacred water drawn from a night elf moonwell in Ashenvale, contained within a vessel taken from the dryads. Zangen Stonehoof's associate, Rau Cliffrunner in the Thousand Needles, needs this consecrated water to extinguish the sacred flame of the Galak centaur, allowing the Horde to recover an ancient relic from the dawn of the centaur race.",al={"filled etched phial use","why filled etched phial","what does the phial do"},it="item",add="47d9b30a"},{q="Who are the Laughing Sisters?",a="The Laughing Sisters are dryads, daughters of the demigod Cenarius, who guard the enchanted groves around Raynewood Retreat in Ashenvale. Bound deeply to nature and the night elves, they dwell near sacred sites and carry specialized etched phials suitable for holding pure moonwell water. Because they are fiercely hostile to outsiders and the Horde, you must wrest a phial from them by force.",al={"why kill dryads","who are dryads raynewood","laughing sisters ashenvale"},it="target",add="9c32d271"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Centaur hostility has plagued the tauren for generations. A relic from the centaur race's genesis can give Mulgore's tribes insight into their foes and leverage against them.",["class:Druid"]="Tauren druids face an uneasy choice: slay nature's daughters, the dryads, to gather sanctified waters for a strike against the centaur's sacred flames.",["faction:Horde"]="Trouble around Raynewood Retreat risks inflaming night elf tensions in Ashenvale. Centaur relics in Thousand Needles bolster the Horde's southern frontiers."},kw={"ashenvale","etched phial","falfarren river","galak centaur","laughing sisters","moonwell","rau cliffrunner","raynewood retreat","the sacred flame","thousand needles","zangen stonehoof"},rel={"npc:zangen-stonehoof","subzone:raynewood-retreat","subzone:falfarren-river","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","zone:thousandneedles","zone:ashenvale","zone:thunderbluff","topic:centaur"},m={start="Zangen Stonehoof",level="25",faction="Horde",id=1195,ri={"Filled Etched Phial"}},src={"The Sacred Flame (quest)"}}
E["quest:1196"] = {t="quest",n="The Sacred Flame",z="thunderbluff",s="From Ashenvale, a phial of moonwell water travels south to Freewind Post. Rau Cliffrunner needs it to break the eternal flame guarding an ancient centaur relic in Thousand Needles.",h="From Ashenvale, a phial of moonwell water travels south to Freewind Post.",sec={{t="A Long Journey South",b="Zangen Stonehoof sends you south across central Kalimdor with an etched phial filled with purified moonwell water. You cross the sun-baked expanse of the Barrens, descend the towering Great Lift, and make for Freewind Post. Rau Cliffrunner waits on the high mesa above the canyon floor, watching the centaur clans below.",sp=0},{t="Shared Blood and Ancient Wards",b="Rau Cliffrunner explains why the moonwell water matters to his fight against the centaur. Dryads and centaur share ancestry through Cenarius, whose son Zaetar fathered the centaur. That kinship gives sacred moonwell water an arcane resonance, the one power that can pierce the eternal flame shielding a guarded centaur artifact.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is Rau Cliffrunner located?",a="Rau Cliffrunner lives atop Freewind Post in Thousand Needles. Travel south through the Barrens, descend the Great Lift to the canyon floor, then follow the southeastern trail to the elevator high on the sheer mesa needle.",al={"where is rau","rau cliffrunner location","find rau cliffrunner","freewind post turn in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Rau need moonwell water to combat centaur?",a="Centaur and dryads share a lineage through Cenarius. Their kinship gives night elf moonwell water the magical harmony needed to break the eternal flame protecting the centaur relic.",al={"why moonwell water","moonwell and centaur connection","dryad centaur relationship"},it="power"},{q="Who sent me with the phial?",a="Zangen Stonehoof sent you with the Filled Etched Phial after you gathered water from the guarded moonwell in Ashenvale.",al={"who gave this quest","zangen stonehoof","quest giver sacred flame 2"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after giving the phial to Rau?",a="After Rau confirms the waters are intact, he asks you to use the phial to quench the flame and retrieve the centaur relic from the nearby canyon.",al={"next quest","what after rau","sacred flame part 3"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="How do I get down into Thousand Needles?",a="Follow the main southern road through the Barrens to the cliff edge. The Great Lift waits there: two wooden elevators operated by tauren pulleys that carry travelers down to the canyon floor.",al={"how to reach thousand needles","getting past the barrens cliff","great lift directions"},it="arrival",gp=true},{q="Why are the tauren seeking a centaur relic?",a="The tauren and centaur have fought a brutal war across Kalimdor for generations. The tauren disrupt centaur rites and seize sacred artifacts to weaken the warlike clans entrenched across the Thousand Needles canyon.",al={"tauren centaur war","why steal centaur relic"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Zangen Stonehoof want this done?",a="Zangen Stonehoof is coordinating efforts to aid Rau Cliffrunner and the tauren in Thousand Needles. By securing the blessed moonwell water and ensuring it reaches Freewind Post, he provides Rau with the means to counteract the magical flame protecting a vital centaur relic.",al={"why send phial","zangen motive","zangen purpose"},it="motive",add="070b3297"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Every blow against the centaur helps protect Mulgore and the newly secured borders of your homeland.",["class:Druid"]="Rau Cliffrunner draws on deep knowledge of Cenarion bloodlines to understand the magical resonance between dryads and centaur.",["faction:Horde"]="Delivering this phial strengthens Freewind Post, the Horde's high outpost among the perilous passes of Thousand Needles."},kw={"centaur relic","etched phial","freewind post","great lift","rau cliffrunner","sacred flame","thousand needles","zangen stonehoof"},rel={"npc:rau-cliffrunner","npc:zangen-stonehoof","subzone:freewind-post","subzone:great-lift","zone:thousandneedles","topic:centaur","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","zone:barrens"},m={start="Zangen Stonehoof",["end"]="Rau Cliffrunner",level="29",faction="Horde",id=1196},src={"The Sacred Flame (2)"}}
E["quest:1197"] = {t="quest",n="The Sacred Flame",z="thunderbluff",s="At Splithoof Hold, Rau Cliffrunner seeks to silence the Galak centaur's sacred fire. With blessed water, you enter their stronghold, quench the brazier, and take the Cloven Hoof.",h="At Splithoof Hold, Rau Cliffrunner seeks to silence the Galak centaur's sacred fire.",sec={{t="Striking the Hearth",b="North of Freewind Post, Splithoof Crag marks the heart of Galak territory in Thousand Needles. Deep in its cavern, Splithoof Hold, a fire burns that the centaur hold sacred. Rau Cliffrunner prepares an etched phial of purified water for his allies. You enter the hold, use the water to quench the flame for a moment, and take the Cloven Hoof relic guarded within.",sp=0},{t="Secrets of the Hoof",b="When Rau Cliffrunner sees the Cloven Hoof, its strange power stirs his mystical senses. Tauren scholars have long fought the marauding centaur tribes across Kalimdor. The relic hints at deeper forces, still poorly understood, that feed the centaur's zeal and tribal unity.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where is the sacred flame located?",a="The flame burns deep inside Splithoof Hold, a cavern in the centaur camp at Splithoof Crag, north of Freewind Post in Thousand Needles.",al={"splithoof hold location","where is sacred flame","flame cave thousand needles"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who asks you to douse the flame?",a="Rau Cliffrunner, an elder stationed high atop Freewind Post, asks you to douse the flame after investigating the Galak centaur.",al={"quest giver sacred flame","rau cliffrunner location","who gives the quest"},it="identity"},{q="How do you put out the flame?",a="Use the Filled Etched Phial Rau Cliffrunner provides. It holds water gathered earlier in the chain, and briefly quenches the brazier.",al={"how to get cloven hoof","dousing flame item","quench sacred flame"},gp=true},{q="What is the Cloven Hoof?",a="The Cloven Hoof is a revered tribal relic kept inside the flame by the Galak centaur. Rau Cliffrunner senses unusual magical energy from it and hopes to learn about centaur culture and power.",al={"cloven hoof lore","centaur relic","what did we steal"},it="item"},{q="Why do the tauren want this relic?",a="Centaur tribes have driven tauren from their ancestral hunting grounds for generations. Taking a sacred heirloom disrupts Galak operations while the tauren seek to understand the arcane or spiritual forces behind their enemies' savagery.",al={"why steal cloven hoof","tauren centaur war"},it="motive"},{q="Which centaur clan guards Splithoof Hold?",a="The Galak tribe controls Splithoof Crag and its cavern hold. They are the chief centaur clan on the floor of Thousand Needles canyon.",al={"thousand needles centaur tribe","galak centaur"},it="target"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, striking into a centaur den and taking its sacred icon answers generations of raids. The relic is also a valuable prize for the scholars at Freewind Post.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can sense the strange energies radiating from the Cloven Hoof. They show that the centaur draw on mystical forces beyond brute savagery."},kw={"centaur","cloven hoof","freewind post","galak","rau cliffrunner","sacred flame","splithoof crag","splithoof hold","thousand needles"},rel={"npc:rau-cliffrunner","subzone:splithoof-hold","subzone:splithoof-crag","subzone:freewind-post","topic:centaur","quest:1195"},m={start="Rau Cliffrunner",["end"]="Rau Cliffrunner",level="29",faction="horde",id=1197,ri={"Cloven Hoof"}},src={"The Sacred Flame (3)"}}
E["quest:1205"] = {t="quest",n="Deadmire",z="thunderbluff",s="In Dustwallow Marsh, Deadmire suffers in the waterways north of the Stonemaul Ruins. Melor Stonehoof sends hunters from Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff to track the ancient crocolisk and bring back a tooth as proof. The hunt teaches tracking and mercy.",h="In Dustwallow Marsh, Deadmire suffers in the waterways north of the Stonemaul Ruins.",sec={{t="A Hunt of Mercy",b="On Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff, Melor Stonehoof teaches promising trackers the spiritual traditions of the hunt. Tauren hunters seek reverence and a bond with the natural world, not slaughter or trophies. Melor sends you east to Dustwallow Marsh to find Deadmire, an ancient crocolisk whose long life has become a burden.",sp=0},{t="The Ancient of the Marsh",b="North of the Stonemaul Ruins, Deadmire prowls the waterways as a massive, pale crocolisk. His strength and fury still come in sudden bursts, but age has worn down his body with grinding bones and unrelenting pain. Melor asks you to grant him a swift, honorable end and bring back one tooth as a token of his release.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Deadmire?",a="Deadmire is a massive, ancient white crocolisk in the swamps of Dustwallow Marsh. Though still dangerous, he suffers from the pain of his failing, aged body.",al={"what is deadmire","deadmire lore","who is the crocolisk"},it="target"},{q="Why does Melor Stonehoof want Deadmire killed?",a="Melor Stonehoof asks you to kill Deadmire as an act of mercy. The crocolisk's aging bones cause him maddening pain, and Melor believes releasing his spirit is a sacred duty.",al={"why kill deadmire","melor stonehoof motive","purpose of deadmire hunt"},it="motive"},{q="Where can Deadmire be found?",a="Deadmire prowls the waterways north of the Stonemaul Ruins in Dustwallow Marsh.",al={"where is deadmire","deadmire location","finding deadmire"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What proof does Melor require from the hunt?",a="Melor asks you to bring back one of Deadmire's teeth as proof of the hunt.",al={"deadmire quest item","what does melor want","deadmire proof"},it="item"},{q="What does this hunt teach aspiring hunters?",a="The hunt teaches you that a hunter's calling is more than killing. It means honoring nature and recognizing when a creature's life has become suffering.",al={"hunter philosophy","tauren hunting lesson","meaning of the hunt"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Melor Stonehoof, a tauren hunter, offers the hunt on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"deadmire quest giver","who starts deadmire","melor stonehoof location"},it="origin"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you balance skill in the hunt with spiritual responsibility. An honorable kill can be an act of mercy.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you honor the Earth Mother's creatures and respect the natural cycles of life and death.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde traveler, you take part in hunts for Thunder Bluff's elders and learn the land and traditions of your tauren allies."},kw={"crocolisk","deadmire","dustwallow marsh","hunter rise","melor stonehoof","stonemaul ruins","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:melor-stonehoof","zone:thunderbluff","zone:dustwallow","subzone:stonemaul-ruins"},m={start="Melor Stonehoof",faction="Horde",id=1205,ri={"Deadmire's Tooth"}},src={"Deadmire (quest)"}}
E["quest:1529"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Water",z="thunderbluff",s="Your path to the Call of Water begins in Thunder Bluff, where a shaman is ready to seek the element of water. To meet Islen Waterseer, you travel east across the Barrens to its eastern shore. The meeting begins a spiritual journey toward the Water Totem.",h="Your path to the Call of Water begins in Thunder Bluff, where a shaman is ready to seek the element of water.",sec={{t="A Summons from the Bluff",b="You have mastered earth and fire, and now your trainers judge you ready to study water. In Thunder Bluff, Xanis Flameweaver recognizes when you have shown the discipline to approach this cleansing element. Your path leads away from Mulgore's mesas and east across the dry plains of the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="The Hermit of the Coast",b="You find Islen Waterseer in a fishing shack on the eastern coast, south of Ratchet and the mouth of the Southfury River. She lives apart from the settlements, beside the open ocean. Islen reads your readiness in the elements around you. Earth, wind, and fire already touch your spirit, and she prepares you for trials that will teach you the purity of water.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this journey?",a="A shaman trainer in Thunder Bluff, such as Xanis Flameweaver, sends you once your training has brought you to the rites of water.",al={"quest giver","who starts call of water","where to get call of water tb"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Islen Waterseer located?",a="Islen Waterseer lives in a fishing hut on the eastern coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet and the Southfury River's mouth.",al={"where is islen waterseer","islen location","find islen"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of the Call of Water trial?",a="The trial begins a shaman's communion with water, testing your understanding of its purity and leading toward the Water Totem.",al={"why do call of water","call of water purpose","shaman water totem quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Do other Horde races receive this same instruction?",a="Tauren shaman receive the summons in Thunder Bluff. Orc and troll shaman in Orgrimmar and Durotar receive similar calls to find Islen Waterseer on the Barrens coast.",al={"is this only for tauren","orc call of water","troll call of water"},it="people"},{q="What elements must a shaman master before water?",a="Before seeking water, you commune with earth and fire. Islen also sees earth, wind, and fire touching your spirit before water reveals its purity.",al={"prerequisites","which totems first","elemental order"},it="history"},{q="What happens after finding Islen Waterseer?",a="Finding Islen completes your journey from Thunder Bluff. She then sets further tasks across Kalimdor to help you understand and purify water.",al={"what next","after finding islen","call of water part 2"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Xanis Flameweaver send me on this quest?",a="Xanis Flameweaver serves as a guide on your path as a shaman. Having observed your patience and your mastery over the initial elements, he recognizes that your spirit has progressed far enough to face the trials of water. His role is not to lead you every step of the way, but to recognize your readiness and direct you to Islen Waterseer, who holds the deeper wisdom necessary to test your understanding of water's purity.",al={"why does xanis send me","xanis flameweaver motive","why seek islen waterseer"},it="motive",add="6892158c"},{q="Why must I undertake this journey myself?",a="The path of a shaman is intensely personal. Communing with the elements demands individual spiritual discipline and proof of devotion, which cannot be delegated to guards or undertaken by your mentors on your behalf. As Islen Waterseer observes, you must take each step under your own power to show the spirits that you possess the inner fortitude to commune with water.",al={"why must i go myself","why me call of water","can someone else go to islen"},it="why_me",add="22e527b8"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you move from early elemental trials toward the cleansing, restorative powers of water and tide.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you leave Mulgore's sheltered plains from Thunder Bluff and travel into the wider reaches of Kalimdor.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share shamanic traditions that link orc, troll, and tauren spiritualists."},kw={"barrens","call of water","islen waterseer","ratchet","shaman","southfury river","thunder bluff","water totem","xanis flameweaver"},rel={"npc:islen-waterseer","zone:barrens","subzone:ratchet","subzone:southfury-river"},m={start="Xanis Flameweaver",["end"]="Islen Waterseer",level="20",faction="Horde",id=1529},src={"Call of Water (Thunder Bluff)"}}
E["quest:1532"] = {t="quest",n="Call of Air",z="thunderbluff",s="Xanis Flameweaver sends seasoned Horde shamans from Thunder Bluff south to seek Prate Cloudseer in Thousand Needles. There they seek communion with the wind and the Air Totem, needed to channel its swift forces.",h="Xanis Flameweaver sends seasoned Horde shamans from Thunder Bluff south to seek Prate Cloudseer in Thousand...",sec={{t="The Whispering Winds",b="A shaman who has attuned to earth, fire, and water now faces air, the final element. From Thunder Bluff, Xanis Flameweaver guides initiates through a trial of humility, focus, and respect for the sky. The winds are fickle and harder to control than the elements they have already learned.",sp=0},{t="A Pilgrimage South",b="The path leads south, past the Barrens and into the canyons of Thousand Needles. Far to the east, Prate Cloudseer dwells in a secluded cave on the cliffs, where canyon drafts howl day and night. She tests each initiate's preparedness before giving them the Air Totem, which channels gusts, lightning, and swift wind spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me on this quest?",a="Xanis Flameweaver, a shaman trainer in Thunder Bluff, sends you to attune to air after you have gained enough experience.",al={"quest giver","who starts call of air","xanis flameweaver"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Prate Cloudseer located?",a="Prate Cloudseer lives in a sheltered cave far to the east in Thousand Needles, just south of the Barrens.",al={"prate cloudseer location","where is prate","find prate cloudseer"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the element of air sought last?",a="Shamans seek air last because its currents are erratic and elusive. Tradition calls for mastering earth, fire, and water before attempting to attune to the wild winds.",al={"why air last","shaman air totem lore","elemental order"},it="history"},{q="What do I receive upon finding Prate Cloudseer?",a="Prate Cloudseer gives you the Air Totem, a conduit for focusing your elemental magic and calling on air spirits for support.",al={"air totem reward","what does prate give","quest reward call of air"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is this quest exclusive to Tauren?",a="Any Horde shaman who has attuned to earth, fire, and water can travel from Thunder Bluff to Thousand Needles to claim an Air Totem.",al={"can orcs do this","is this tauren only","horde shaman air quest"},it="people",gp=true},{q="What happens after finishing this quest?",a="When you arrive, Prate Cloudseer gives you the Air Totem, letting you invoke wind-based totems immediately. She also offers further training and trials to hone your connection with the sky.",al={"what comes next","after call of air","prate cloudseer quests"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Xanis Flameweaver send me on this quest?",a="Xanis Flameweaver sees that you have grown strong enough in your shamanic path to pursue mastery over the most volatile element: air. As your mentor in Thunder Bluff, he recognizes that the rushing winds of Kalimdor are calling to you. The element of air is notoriously difficult to bind and commune with, and Xanis cannot impart that final understanding himself from the high bluffs. Instead, he directs you south into Thousand Needles so Prate Cloudseer can initiate you into communion with the air spirits.",al={"why xanis sends me","xanis flameweaver motive","call of air purpose"},it="motive",add="52df4f2b"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, completing your elemental set marks a turning point. The Air Totem opens the way to swift currents and lightning-wreathed powers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde shaman, binding Kalimdor's wild winds in a sacred totem strengthens your faction's spiritual backbone.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you revere the winds as sacred messengers. They carry the Earth Mother's whispers across the plains from Mulgore's towering bluffs."},kw={"air totem","call of air","prate cloudseer","shaman","thousand needles","thunder bluff","xanis flameweaver"},rel={"zone:thousandneedles","zone:barrens"},m={start="Xanis Flameweaver",["end"]="Prate Cloudseer",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1532},src={"Call of Air (Thunder Bluff)"}}
E["quest:1718"] = {t="quest",n="The Islander",z="thunderbluff",s="Warrior trainers across Azeroth send proven fighters to Fray Island for a test among their peers. The island lies off the Merchant Coast, where chief warrior Klannoc Macleod awaits those who seek the next step in their training.",h="Warrior trainers across Azeroth send proven fighters to Fray Island for a test among their peers.",sec={{t="A Gathering of Blades",b="Warrior trainers in Alliance and Horde capitals send students who have outgrown basic drills to test themselves against their peers. A fighter's progress comes through combat, not rank or loyalty. The journey leads away from civilized sparring yards to a rugged isle in the Great Sea.",sp=0},{t="Fray Island and the Merchant Coast",b="Fray Island lies east of the Merchant Coast, just south of Ratchet in the Barrens. You can reach it by swimming across waters that pass over submerged sandbar shallows. Political ties matter little on the island, where fighters gather before Klannoc Macleod, its chief warrior, and await the trial he chooses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Fray Island?",a="Fray Island is a rocky outcrop off the Merchant Coast of the Barrens, south of Ratchet. Warriors from across Azeroth gather there to hone their craft, spar, and face combat trials away from civil authority.",al={"where is fray island","fray island lore","fray isle"},it="place"},{q="Who is Klannoc Macleod?",a="Klannoc Macleod is the chief warrior on Fray Island. He assesses those who make the journey and decides whether their spirit and skill merit further guidance along the warrior's path.",al={"who is klannoc","klannoc macleod role","macleod warrior"},it="identity"},{q="Why do trainers from both Horde and Alliance send warriors here?",a="Trainers from both the Horde and Alliance send warriors to test their martial skill in combat. Trainers in Orgrimmar, Stormwind, Thunder Bluff, and Ironforge recognize Fray Island as a proving ground for warriors able to survive its challenges.",al={"why do both factions go here","is fray island neutral","horde and alliance fray island"},it="purpose"},{q="How do you reach Fray Island from the mainland?",a="Travel south along the Merchant Coast from Ratchet in the Barrens. From shore, swim east across the sandbar shallows toward Fray Island.",al={"how to get to fray island","fray island directions","finding fray island"},gp=true},{q="What happens after meeting Klannoc Macleod?",a="After Klannoc Macleod confirms your journey and weighs your resolve, he invites you into The Affray, a gauntlet that tests your stamina against waves of challengers.",al={"what comes after the islander","klannoc macleod next quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why do the warrior trainers send you to Fray Island?",a="Your training in the cities has carried you as far as standard drills can take you. As your renown grows, your mentors know that true martial mastery cannot be learned from practice dummies or friendly sparring. They send you to Klannoc Macleod so you can measure your strength against real peers from across the world, testing whether you are truly worthy of advancing along the warrior's path.",al={"why send to fray island","trainer motive islander","why does trainer want me to go"},it="motive",add="b7452d18"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you take this rite of passage from basic maneuvers toward the full ferocity and tactical versatility of veteran stances.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior, you travel from Thunder Bluff or Orgrimmar to the Barrens to prove your strength beyond your chieftains' watchful eyes.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance warrior, you cross the sea or Kalimdor's wilderness to reach Fray Island, showing your martial devotion in a rugged frontier far from human and dwarven strongholds."},kw={"fray island","klannoc macleod","merchant coast","ratchet","the affray","the barrens","the islander","warrior"},rel={"subzone:fray-island","npc:klannoc-macleod","quest:1719","subzone:merchant-coast","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","quest:92532"},m={start="Wu Shen, Kelv Sternhammer  Baltus Fowler, Torm Ragetotem, Sorek",["end"]="Klannoc Macleod",level="30",id=1718},src={"The Islander"}}
E["quest:1840"] = {t="quest",n="Orm Stonehoof and the Brutal Helm",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, Orm Stonehoof has the skill to forge the Brutal Helm. Thun'grim Firegaze sends warriors to him for that work.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Orm Stonehoof has the skill to forge the Brutal Helm.",sec={{t="A Recommendation in Iron",b="Warriors who prove their mettle and assemble pieces of the Brutal Armor in the Barrens are sent up to Thunder Bluff. Thun'grim Firegaze is an accomplished armorsmith, but he knows the work has reached beyond his own skill. He refers the warriors to Orm Stonehoof, whose craft is renowned across Kalimdor. Orm can shape resilient battlefield helms from rare, savage trophies.",sp=0},{t="The Artisan by the Pool",b="Orm Stonehoof lives and works on the high bluffs of Mulgore, near the tranquil pool beneath Thunder Bluff's towering central totem. When a warrior arrives with Thun'grim Firegaze's word, Orm leaves his routine work to discuss the demanding components needed for a helm worthy of the Horde's front lines.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orm Stonehoof?",a="Orm Stonehoof is a skilled tauren armorsmith who lives in Thunder Bluff. Thun'grim Firegaze sends warriors to him for his skill in crafting battle helms.",al={"orm stonehoof","who is orm"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Orm Stonehoof be found?",a="Orm Stonehoof works near the pool beneath Thunder Bluff's massive central totem.",al={"where is orm","orm stonehoof location","find orm"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze send you to Thunder Bluff?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze can craft the chestpiece and other parts of the Brutal set, but Orm Stonehoof has the skill needed to forge the Brutal Helm.",al={"why thunder bluff","why see orm"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the Brutal Helm?",a="The Brutal Helm is headgear forged for Horde warriors who have reached veteran standing. It requires dangerous materials from beasts across Kalimdor.",al={"brutal helm quest","what is brutal helm"},it="item"},{q="What does Orm ask for next?",a="Orm Stonehoof asks you to gather beast trophies for the helm, starting with a Chimaeric Horn from a chimaera in the wild.",al={"next quest","after orm stonehoof","chimaeric horn quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Can any class take this quest?",a="No. This line is for warriors who have advanced far enough in their martial training and completed Thun'grim's initial armor work.",al={"is this warrior only","who can do this quest"},gp=true},{q="Why does Thun'grim Firegaze want you to see Orm Stonehoof?",a="Thun'grim Firegaze has helped guide your training as a warrior, but crafting a brutal helm requires a master artisan whose talent outmatches ordinary smithing. Recognizing Orm Stonehoof's unmatched skill at working metal and bone, Thun'grim sends you to the tauren craftsman in Thunder Bluff so you can earn a piece of armor worthy of your growing strength and service to the Horde.",al={"thungrim firegaze motive","why send to orm stonehoof","thungrim brutal helm reason"},it="motive",add="528c5ae8"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you are sent to one of the Horde's finest master smiths for heavyweight head protection.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you see orcish weaponmasters in the Barrens work with tauren craftsmen high atop Thunder Bluff."},kw={"armor quest","brutal helm","orm stonehoof","thun'grim firegaze","thunder bluff","warrior"},rel={"quest:1838","quest:1845","quest:1844","quest:1502","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Thun'grim Firegaze",["end"]="Orm Stonehoof",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1840},src={"Orm Stonehoof and the Brutal Helm"}}
E["quest:1844"] = {t="quest",n="Chimaeric Horn",z="thunderbluff",s="Orm Stonehoof sends a Horde warrior into the Charred Vale to face a suffering chimaera matriarch. Her horn is needed for the Brutal Helm, and the hunt tests the warrior’s strength and mercy.",h="Orm Stonehoof sends a Horde warrior into the Charred Vale to face a suffering chimaera matriarch.",sec={{t="A Test of Resolve",b="Orm Stonehoof will forge the Brutal Helm for Horde warriors, but tradition calls for proof before he begins. He asks for more than metal or coin: the warrior must show martial skill and face the scars left by devastating conflict.",sp=0},{t="The Scars of the Charred Vale",b="In the southwestern Stonetalon Mountains, the Charred Vale lies in ash. Once lush and green, the valley was burned into a smoking wasteland. Beasts still wander its soot-covered craters, twisted by pain and fury. Mighty chimaeras nest among dead trees and searing steam vents.",sp=0},{t="Mercy in Combat",b="For the tauren smith, the chimaera matriarch’s horn is both a needed piece for the helm and proof of strength. The hunt also ends the matriarch’s torment. By felling her, the warrior brings mercy to a wild spirit driven mad by the destruction of its home.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Orm Stonehoof?",a="Orm Stonehoof is a skilled tauren blacksmith in Thunder Bluff who helps veteran Horde warriors craft their class armor, including the Brutal Helm.",al={"orm stonehoof lore","who is orm stonehoof","thunder bluff blacksmith orm"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Orm want the galvanized horn?",a="The galvanized horn is a durable part of the Brutal Helm and proof that the warrior had the courage to track and defeat a dangerous alpha predator in hazardous terrain.",al={"galvanized horn use","why get galvanized horn","brutal helm horn"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What are chimaeras in Stonetalon?",a="Chimaeras are large, two-headed winged beasts native to Kalimdor. Fire and destruction in the Charred Vale have driven its surviving chimaeras violently mad.",al={"stonetalon chimaeras","chimaera lore","what are chimaeras"},it="threat"},{q="How does this quest fit into warrior training?",a="Around their thirtieth season, Horde warriors go to specialists such as Orm Stonehoof for dangerous trials. Completing these trials earns them the right to wear the heavy, spiked Brutal armor set made for battlefield champions.",al={"warrior brutal helm chain","level 30 warrior quest thunder bluff","brutal armor questline"},it="purpose"},{q="Why does Orm frame the hunt as an act of mercy?",a="Tauren culture honors harmony with the earth and its creatures. The Charred Vale’s inhabitants suffer from the devastation of their land, so slaying the matriarch is seen as ending her unrelenting pain, not as mindless slaughter.",al={"why mercy for the matriarch","free her of her misery"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Galvanized Horn for?",a="The galvanized horn serves a dual purpose for Orm Stonehoof. Materially, it provides the formidable, hardened horn needed to forge your Brutal Helm. Ritualistically, it acts as physical proof that you braved the ashen wastes of the Charred Vale, confronted a maddened chimaera matriarch, and demonstrated both martial strength and the mercy of granting her release.",al={"galvanized horn use","why do i need galvanized horn","galvanized horn brutal helm"},it="item",add="3a1b9e89"},{q="Who are you sent to hunt in the Charred Vale?",a="You are sent to hunt a chimaera matriarch dwelling amidst the ruins of the Charred Vale. Once a lush highland valley, the vale was thoroughly defiled by fiery destruction, driving the surviving beasts insane with agony and despair. The matriarch is one of these majestic predators, now suffering endlessly in the blighted ashes until you grant her an honorable end.",al={"chimaera matriarch target","who do i kill in charred vale","chimaeric horn target"},it="target",add="241e9666"},{q="Why does Orm send you instead of going himself?",a="Orm Stonehoof is testing your spirit, not asking for a routine errand. The Brutal Helm is a traditional, powerful piece of armor reserved only for warriors who have proved their resolve, martial prowess, and capacity for honorable mercy. By hunting the beast yourself in the hostile wastes of the Charred Vale, you prove to Orm that you are worthy of wearing his craft.",al={"why send me orm","why cant orm hunt the matriarch","why does orm need an adventurer"},it="why_me",add="c3120874"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a warrior, you prove your skill by hunting a solitary alpha beast in a brutal place, earning the right to wear the Brutal Helm.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you hear Orm Stonehoof’s reverence in his words: even in battle, ending a tormented beast’s suffering honors the Earth Mother.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you push from Sun Rock Retreat into Stonetalon’s contested wilds to forge the arms needed for Kalimdor’s defense."},kw={"brutal helm","charred vale","chimaera matriarch","chimaeric horn","galvanized horn","orm stonehoof","stonetalon","thunder bluff","warrior quest"},rel={"quest:1840","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:charred-vale","zone:stonetalon","subzone:sun-rock-retreat"},m={start="Orm Stonehoof",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1844,ri={"Galvanized Horn"}},src={"Chimaeric Horn"}}
E["quest:1845"] = {t="quest",n="Brutal Helm",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, Orm Stonehoof brings the warrior’s trial to its end with Brutal Helm. After gathering rare beast trophies across Kalimdor, an aspiring warrior earns recognition with a horned helm that honors their strength.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Orm Stonehoof brings the warrior’s trial to its end with Brutal Helm.",sec={{t="A Warrior's Rite",b="Orm Stonehoof is a stern smith in Thunder Bluff who guides Horde warriors through hard rites of passage. The trials test their skill in battle. Initiates hunt dangerous creatures in treacherous lands and claim rare trophies. Only those who meet Orm’s high standards may come before him to complete their armor.",sp=0},{t="The Gift of the Earthmother",b="The warrior proves their resolve in the wild by bringing Orm Stonehoof a rare chimaeric horn. In return, Orm presents Brutal Helm, heavy mail crafted to honor the beast and strengthen its wearer in the front line. As he gives the helm, Orm calls on the Earthmother’s blessing. He looks to the greater deeds the warrior is bound to undertake across Azeroth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the Brutal Helm?",a="Orm Stonehoof, a tauren blacksmith in Thunder Bluff, presents Brutal Helm to Horde warriors who complete his trials.",al={"who gives brutal helm","brutal helm npc","orm stonehoof quest"},it="identity"},{q="What task must be finished before receiving the helm?",a="Before receiving the helm, you complete the trial named Chimaeric Horn. You hunt fierce beasts in the wilderness and bring their horn to Orm Stonehoof in Thunder Bluff.",al={"prereq for brutal helm","chimaeric horn quest"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is Orm Stonehoof located?",a="Orm Stonehoof is near the pool beside the great central totem in Thunder Bluff’s high mesa city.",al={"orm stonehoof location","where is orm stonehoof"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Orm Stonehoof invoke the Earthmother?",a="As a tauren, Orm honors the Earthmother as the world’s creator and spiritual guardian. Her blessing on a warrior’s finished helm reflects the tauren belief that battle strength must be balanced with spiritual reverence.",al={"why mention earthmother","earthmother lore"},it="origin"},{q="Is this trial open to any adventurer?",a="No. The trial and its Brutal Armor rewards are for Horde warriors who prove their mettle through dedicated class trials.",al={"can anyone get brutal helm","brutal helm class"},it="why_me",gp=true},{q="What is the significance of the Brutal Armor set?",a="The Brutal Armor pieces mark a warrior’s progress from novice soldier to elite champion of the Horde. They are made from materials gathered from Kalimdor’s fiercest predators.",al={"brutal armor lore","why is it called brutal helm"},it="power"},{q="Why does Orm Stonehoof reward you with the Brutal Helm?",a="Orm Stonehoof bestows the helm not out of a desperate need or sudden crisis, but as ceremonial recognition of your martial growth. By gathering rare materials from across Kalimdor and proving your strength through the warrior trials, you have demonstrated that you are ready to bear the mantle of seasoned champions. Orm honors that perseverance, invoking the Earthmother's blessing so your armor may protect you in the even greater battles awaiting you.",al={"why does orm give you the helm","orm stonehoof brutal helm motive","why brutal helm"},it="motive",add="3a1185bd"}},ang={["class:Warrior"]="As a Horde warrior, you pass a key rite and take up heavy armor forged from ferocious beasts and blessed by veteran trainers.",["race:Tauren"]="In Thunder Bluff, your helm reflects the tauren tradition of turning hunting trophies into protective wargear under the Earthmother’s grace.",["faction:Horde"]="Beneath the Horde banner, you prove the physical endurance and hunting skill your leaders demand."},kw={"brutal helm","chimaeric horn","earthmother","hunter rise","orm stonehoof","thunder bluff","warrior"},rel={"quest:1844"},m={start="Orm Stonehoof",level="30",faction="Horde",id=1845},src={"Brutal Helm (quest)"}}
E["quest:1959"] = {t="quest",n="Report to Anastasia",z="thunderbluff",s="Horde mages from across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms are called to the Undercity. Anastasia Hartwell has sensed an unknown magical disturbance there and needs capable spellcasters to investigate.",h="Horde mages from across Kalimdor and the Eastern Kingdoms are called to the Undercity.",sec={{t="A Call to the Arcane",b="Horde mages hear of trouble in the Undercity. Those studying atop the bluffs of Thunder Bluff, in the dusty heat of Durotar, or among the ruins of Lordaeron receive the same call if they have enough skill. The Undercity's mages have sensed an unexplained disturbance within their domain and need help investigating it.",sp=0},{t="The Mage of the Undercity",b="Anastasia Hartwell oversees arcane matters in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. She confirms that mages have detected strange energies within the city. No one knows whether the magic is harmless or hostile. Anastasia needs a capable mage to investigate quietly, beginning in the Apothecarium.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Anastasia Hartwell?",a="Anastasia Hartwell is a Forsaken mage and arcane mentor in the Undercity's Magic Quarter. She guides new practitioners and watches for arcane disturbances in the Forsaken capital.",al={"anastasia hartwell lore","who is anastasia","hartwell undercity"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Anastasia Hartwell located?",a="Anastasia Hartwell is in the Magic Quarter, in the northern arc of the Undercity. She is among the spellcasting trainers and arcane researchers.",al={"where is anastasia","hartwell location","anastasia undercity map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are mages from Thunder Bluff or the Barrens being summoned to the Undercity?",a="The Undercity's mages have detected an unusual disturbance, and Horde interests in Lordaeron may be at risk. Mentors in Kalimdor send promising pupils there to help and gain experience with complex magical phenomena.",al={"why travel to undercity","why report to anastasia","thunder bluff mage quest"},it="motive"},{q="What kind of disturbance is Anastasia investigating?",a="Mages have detected unexplained magical fluctuations within the Undercity. Anastasia Hartwell does not yet know whether the energy is hostile, accidental, or harmless, so she begins a careful inquiry.",al={"what disturbance","magical disturbance undercity","what is wrong in undercity"},it="danger"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Horde mage trainers can send you to Anastasia once you have enough experience. They include Uthel'nay in Orgrimmar, Thurston Xane in Thunder Bluff, Cain Firesong in Brill, and Un'Thuwa in Sen'jin Village.",al={"who starts report to anastasia","quest starters report to anastasia"},it="people"},{q="What happens after reporting to Anastasia?",a="After you speak with Anastasia and receive her briefing, she directs you to investigate the disturbance in the city's Apothecarium, beginning with Investigate the Alchemist Shop.",al={"next quest after report to anastasia","report to anastasia follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why do the mage trainers send you to Anastasia Hartwell instead of handling it themselves?",a="Your trainers are needed to instruct fledgling spellcasters and maintain mystical oversight across Kalimdor's settlements. When word arrived that the Forsaken mages required assistance to investigate an arcane anomaly within the Undercity, the trainers sought out capable, rising practitioners ready for field duties rather than abandoning their teaching posts.",al={"why send me to anastasia","why cant the trainers go to undercity","why me report to anastasia"},it="why_me",add="22ef3f4a"}},ang={["class:Mage"]="As a Horde mage, you leave your regional training outpost for the Undercity, where deeper arcane mysteries and hazards lie beneath the ruins of Lordaeron.",["faction:Horde"]="The call brings Forsaken and other Horde mages together to protect their shared interests.",["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, you are called to the Undercity's Magic Quarter to help guard your young kingdom against arcane threats within its walls."},kw={"anastasia hartwell","cain firesong","investigate the alchemist shop","mage","magic quarter","report to anastasia","thurston xane","un'thuwa","undercity","uthel'nay"},rel={"npc:anastasia-hartwell","quest:1960","subzone:magic-quarter","zone:undercity","quest:1881","topic:horde"},m={start="Uthel'nay, Cain Firesong, Thurston Xane, or Un'Thuwa",["end"]="Anastasia Hartwell",level="15",faction="Horde",id=1959},src={"Report to Anastasia"}}
E["quest:27"] = {t="quest",n="A Lesson to Learn",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem sends young tauren druids north to study the waters. Their road leads to Nighthaven in Moonglade, where the Cenarion Circle guides their training.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem sends young tauren druids north to study the waters.",sec={{t="Mastery of the Depths",b="After learning the bear form and its physical might, your studies turn to adaptability. Azeroth's waterways bring hazards that landbound travelers cannot face easily. Turak Runetotem watches his students and sends those devoted to nature north to learn the aquatic form.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Nighthaven",b="Turak Runetotem sends you beyond Mulgore for guidance in shaping yourself for the waters. You travel to Moonglade, the sanctuary beneath Mount Hyjal, and reach Nighthaven. There, night elf mentors of the Cenarion Circle welcome tauren students. They set factional strife aside to preserve the shared teachings of Cenarius.",sp=0},{t="The Dual Trials",b="Dendrite Starblaze waits for you in Nighthaven, where your training begins. The night elf elder says mastery over the waters must be earned. Two trials await: one tests your endurance and composure under water, and the other calls for deep spiritual understanding of the aquatic aspect.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest A Lesson to Learn?",a="Turak Runetotem gives it from the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, where he trains druids. When you have enough experience, he sends you for advanced training.",al={"who starts a lesson to learn","where do i get a lesson to learn","turak runetotem quest"},gp=true},{q="Where must I go to complete this quest?",a="You travel to Nighthaven in Moonglade and speak with Dendrite Starblaze of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"where do i turn in a lesson to learn","dendrite starblaze location","where is nighthaven"},gp=true},{q="What ability does this quest chain lead to?",a="This path leads to Aquatic Form, which lets you swim swiftly underwater and breathe beneath the surface without end.",al={"what form does this give","aquatic form quest","why do this quest"},it="power"},{q="Why do tauren druids go to a night elf for training?",a="The Cenarion Circle is a neutral brotherhood devoted to Cenarius and the preservation of nature. In Moonglade, night elves and tauren set Horde and Alliance tensions aside to learn the sacred arts together.",al={"why moonglade","why dendrite starblaze","cenarion circle tauren"},it="ties"},{q="What trials does Dendrite Starblaze speak of?",a="Dendrite Starblaze tells you of two trials. One tests your composure under pressure underwater, and the other tests your spiritual resolve to understand the aquatic aspect.",al={"what are the two trials","dendrite tests","aquatic trials"}},{q="How does a druid reach Moonglade at this stage?",a="Druids can use Teleport: Moonglade, a spell born of their spiritual bond, to travel directly from anywhere in Azeroth to Nighthaven.",al={"how to get to moonglade","teleport to moonglade","getting to nighthaven"},gp=true},{q="Why does Turak Runetotem send me to Moonglade?",a="Turak Runetotem has watched your growth as a protector of nature and believes you are ready to advance your druidic path. He sends you to Moonglade so you can commune with the Cenarion Circle and learn the animal aspect granted by Cenarius that commands mastery over the water.",al={"why does turak send me","turak runetotem motive","why a lesson to learn"},it="motive",add="b1c6f6a1"},{q="Why do I have to undergo this training myself?",a="Shapeshifting is not a mantle that can be bestowed or carried out by another. Each druid must prove their own spirit and physical endurance directly before the Cenarion Circle to attune themselves to Cenarius's blessing and earn the aquatic aspect.",al={"why must i do the trials","why send me moonglade","why me a lesson to learn"},it="why_me",add="055244fc"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you leave terrestrial survival behind and begin learning to breathe and move underwater.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you join the druids of Thunder Bluff in the wider Cenarion brotherhood of Moonglade.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you honor Moonglade's sacred neutrality and walk beside night elves beneath Cenarius's shared canopy."},kw={"aquatic form","cenarion circle","dendrite starblaze","elder rise","lesson to learn","moonglade","nighthaven","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:dendrite-starblaze","npc:turak-runetotem","quest:31","subzone:nighthaven","quest:5922","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:cenarius"},m={start="Turak Runetotem",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="16",faction="Horde",id=27},src={"A Lesson to Learn (Horde)"}}
E["quest:31"] = {t="quest",n="Aquatic Form",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, a young Horde druid returns to master the waters. After proving worthy in Moonglade and attuning to the sea lion aspect, the druid comes home for formal recognition and Aquatic Form.",h="In Thunder Bluff, a young Horde druid returns to master the waters.",sec={{t="Return of the Sea Lion",b="Dendrite Starblaze sends the aspiring tauren druid back to Mulgore after the trials in Moonglade. The Pendant of the Sea Lion bears proof of balance and dedication through Kalimdor's waters. Carrying it shows the initiate has honored the ancient traditions needed to take an aquatic aspect.",sp=0},{t="Communion with the Waters",b="At Thunder Bluff's heights, the traveler presents the pendant to Turak Runetotem, their mentor. Pleased that the initiate has honored their ancestors and kept the balance of nature, Turak teaches the secret of the aquatic form. The druid can then move beneath rivers and oceans, breathe freely, and navigate the depths as a sea creature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="This rite brings a young Horde druid's passage to its end. In Thunder Bluff, the druid presents the Pendant of the Sea Lion and learns Aquatic Form.",al={"why do this quest","aquatic form purpose","what does this quest do"},it="purpose"},{q="Who do I bring the Pendant of the Sea Lion to?",a="Bring the Pendant of the Sea Lion to Turak Runetotem, the druid trainer on Thunder Bluff's upper rises in Mulgore.",al={"who turns this in","where to turn in aquatic form","turak runetotem location"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who sends you back to Thunder Bluff?",a="Dendrite Starblaze sends you back after your aquatic trials in Moonglade are complete.",al={"who gives aquatic form quest","dendrite starblaze quest"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Can non-druids complete this quest?",a="No. Only druids can complete this rite, which advances their spiritual and magical path toward animal forms.",al={"is this druid only","can other classes do aquatic form"},gp=true},{q="Why does a night elf in Moonglade help a Horde druid?",a="Moonglade is a neutral sanctuary overseen by the Cenarion Circle. Night elf mentors guide tauren druids in the ancient Cenarion arts, seeking nature's balance without political hostility.",al={"why does dendrite help horde","moonglade horde alliance","druid neutrality"},it="why_here"},{q="What ability does completing this quest grant?",a="Turak Runetotem teaches you Aquatic Form. While shapeshifted, you swim faster and breathe underwater.",al={"what form do i get","aquatic form spell","water form"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze send you back to Thunder Bluff?",a="Dendrite Starblaze oversees your trials in Moonglade on behalf of the Cenarion Circle, but Moonglade is a sanctuary of instruction rather than your personal home. Having tested your endurance and reverence for the water, Dendrite's duty is complete. He directs you back to your local mentor, Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff, to present proof of your rites and receive the final blessing that grants you the aquatic form.",al={"why send to turak","dendrite starblaze motive","why return to thunder bluff"},it="motive",add="269933c9"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Aquatic Form lets you cross bodies of water with ease and escape predators in the deep.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, mastering the beasts of the sea honors your ancestors and strengthens your people's return to druidic ways.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you share the tauren druids' spiritual link to the Cenarion Circle, walking between neutral sanctuaries and tribal capitals."},kw={"aquatic form","dendrite starblaze","druid","moonglade","pendant of the sea lion","sea lion","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:turak-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","topic:druid","zone:thunderbluff","quest:5921","quest:1067"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Turak Runetotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=31},src={"Aquatic Form (Horde)"}}
E["quest:3369"] = {t="quest",n="In Nightmares",z="thunderbluff",s="A shard from the Wailing Caverns brings a troubling vision to Thunder Bluff. Recovered as a glowing fragment, the Nightmare Shard is carried to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise, where it reveals corruption within the Emerald Dream.",h="A shard from the Wailing Caverns brings a troubling vision to Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="Falla Sagewind sees the pure essence of the Emerald Dream in the strange crystal from the Wailing Caverns. A dark, chaotic vision dwells inside it, more waking nightmare than peaceful slumber. Unwilling to speak openly of such an omen, she entrusts the shard to you. She sends you to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem, Thunder Bluff's most venerated elder druid.",sp=0},{t="A Secret in the Dream",b="On Elder Rise, Hamuul Runetotem peers into the Nightmare Shard, and his composure falters. The shard gives him tangible evidence that the Emerald Dream is unraveling into nightmare. He urges discretion, warning that ordinary travelers cannot understand such delicate matters, and quietly resolves to investigate the affliction threatening the slumbering realm.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Nightmare Shard?",a="The Nightmare Shard is the glowing fragment recovered in the Wailing Caverns. Falla Sagewind entrusts it to you after examining it. Made from the pure spiritual essence of the Emerald Dream, it holds a foul, twisted vision that shows something has gone terribly wrong in the Dream.",al={"what is nightmare shard","glowing shard nightmare","what did falla find"},it="item"},{q="Who is Falla Sagewind?",a="Falla Sagewind is a knowledgeable tauren druid on the mountainside overlooking the Wailing Caverns in the Barrens. She studies strange phenomena from the corrupted oasis caverns and sends Horde couriers to Hamuul Runetotem when dangerous relics are found.",al={"falla sagewind","who gave me this quest","quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem resides on Elder Rise, one of Thunder Bluff's elevated mesas. He stands within the druidic circle with his fellow Cenarion Circle practitioners.",al={"where is hamuul","hamuul runetotem location","elder rise hamuul"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Hamuul want to keep the shard a secret?",a="The Emerald Dream is the sacred sanctuary of nature and the slumbering druids. Proof that it is being twisted into nightmare could cause panic among the Cenarion Circle and weaken fragile spiritual restoration efforts across Kalimdor, so Hamuul urges silence.",al={"why keep it quiet","hamuul secret","why does hamuul hide the shard"},it="motive"},{q="Does the Alliance have a version of this quest?",a="Yes. Horde champions carry the Nightmare Shard to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff. Alliance investigators from the Wailing Caverns take their shard across the sea to Darnassus and present it to Mathrengyl Bearwalker of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"alliance version","in nightmares alliance","can alliance do this"},gp=true},{q="How does this relate to the Wailing Caverns?",a="The shard comes from the Wailing Caverns, where the druid Naralex entered a deep trance to channel underground springs into the Barrens. His slumber turned into a waking nightmare instead of healing the land, mutating cavern fauna and spreading into crystal shards like this one.",al={"wailing caverns connection","naralex connection","how does this relate to naralex"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Falla Sagewind want the Nightmare Shard delivered to Hamuul Runetotem?",a="When Falla Sagewind examines the shard, she recognizes it as pure essence of the Emerald Dream, but tainted by visions of a waking nightmare. Disturbed by what she sees, she realizes the discovery is far too dangerous and significant for her to handle alone. She refuses to speak of it further and insists you carry it immediately to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem in Thunder Bluff, trusting only one of the highest-ranking and wisest druids of the Cenarion Circle to understand and manage such a dire omen.",al={"why send shard to hamuul","why does falla want this done","falla sagewind motive"},it="motive",add="d74ecb00"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, the shard is alarming proof that the Emerald Dream's pristine sanctity is compromised. It confirms whispers of corruption creeping through Cenarion circles.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your return to Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem reflects the growing prominence of tauren druids in the Cenarion Circle. They face ancient cosmological threats alongside their night elven teachers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, delivering the shard helps safeguard central Kalimdor's spiritual well-being. It shows the Horde's crucial role in containing the fungal and dream-born corruption spilling from the Barrens."},kw={"elder rise","emerald dream","falla sagewind","glowing shard","hamuul runetotem","in nightmares","nightmare shard","thunder bluff","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:6981","quest:1489","npc:falla-sagewind","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:emerald-dream","topic:druid","topic:horde"},m={start="Falla Sagewind",["end"]="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem",level="25",faction="Horde",id=3369},src={"In Nightmares (Horde)"}}
E["quest:5062"] = {t="quest",n="Sacred Fire",z="thunderbluff",s="Hunters seek Incendia Agave at the Boiling Pool to prepare a sacred fire that can call Arikara from the canyons of Thousand Needles.",h="Hunters seek Incendia Agave at the Boiling Pool to prepare a sacred fire that can call Arikara from the...",sec={{t="Kindling the Spirit",b="Motega Firemane instructs hunters to prepare the sacred fire of life, an ancient flame that calls the spirit beast Arikara. The monstrous wind serpent cannot simply be tracked across the canyon floor; she must be drawn to the fire. The flame needs more than ordinary kindling. Rare Incendia Agave, which grows around the scalding waters of Thousand Needles, feeds it.",sp=0},{t="The Boiling Pool",b="Incendia Agave grows near the Boiling Pool, below Darkcloud Pinnacle. To gather the spiky plants, you brave blistering waters and steam elementals drifting through the mists. Many bushels grow beneath the surface, where the hot lake water tests every hunter sent to collect them.",sp=0},{t="The Elder's Blessing",b="Raw agave cannot ignite the ritual brazier. You carry the harvested plants from the plains to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. There, Magatha Grimtotem grinds and enchants the leaves into potent ritual powder, eager to see the vengeful beast challenged.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the sacred fire of life?",a="The sacred fire of life is a ritual flame used to summon the vengeful spirit serpent Arikara. Without it, the beast remains hidden and beyond reach.",al={"sacred fire","what does the fire do","why light the sacred fire"}},{q="Where does Incendia Agave grow?",a="Incendia Agave grows in and around the Boiling Pool in Thousand Needles, near Darkcloud Pinnacle. Many of the spiky plants lie beneath the hot lake water.",al={"where to find agave","incendia agave location","boiling pool agave"},gp=true},{q="Why must Magatha Grimtotem enchant the agave?",a="Raw Incendia Agave lacks the power to ignite the sacred fire. Magatha Grimtotem uses her shamanic craft to enchant the leaves into powder that can awaken the dormant flame.",al={"why magatha","who enchants the agave","what does magatha do"}},{q="Who is Arikara?",a="Arikara is a wind serpent born to deliver vengeance against those who commit terrible crimes. Motega Firemane sees her presence as an imminent peril that hunters must confront swiftly.",al={"what is arikara","arikara lore","wind serpent boss"},it="target"},{q="Who gives the quest Sacred Fire?",a="Motega Firemane gives it in Thousand Needles after you help him with his initial tasks concerning the local serpent threat.",al={"quest giver sacred fire","where to start sacred fire"},gp=true},{q="Why does Magatha smile when she hears of Arikara?",a="No explanation is given for Magatha Grimtotem's smile. She smiles after describing Arikara as a creature born to punish heinous acts, leaving you to wonder what she thinks.",al={"magatha smiling","magatha reaction","why does magatha smile"}},{q="Why does Motega Firemane send you to gather Incendia Agave?",a="Motega Firemane recognizes Arikara as a deadly threat that must be eliminated without delay. Summoning the vengeful wind serpent to hunt her down requires lighting the sacred fire of life, but doing so demands an enchanted powder made from rare Incendia Agave. Because Motega cannot perform the enchantment himself, he sends you to gather the herb and take it to Magatha Grimtotem in Thunder Bluff so the ritual can proceed.",al={"why does motega want this","motega firemane motive","why get incendia agave"},it="motive",add="74be6845"},{q="What is the Incendia Agave used for?",a="Incendia Agave is a rare plant found in the Boiling Pool of Thousand Needles. Once harvested, Magatha Grimtotem enchants the agave to produce a sacred powder. This powder is necessary to kindle the dormant sacred fire of life, the ceremonial flames required to summon the spirit serpent Arikara from hiding.",al={"incendia agave purpose","what is incendia agave for","incendia agave use"},it="item",add="64ef07c3"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, you honor the spirits through ritual hunting and face the elders' politics on Elder Rise as part of a rite of adulthood.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see elemental power infused into natural plants like Incendia Agave.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As an herbalist, you can track the submerged spiky bushels of Incendia Agave across the Boiling Pool.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you carry out trials for the elders and strengthen ties across Kalimdor's arid flatlands."},kw={"arikara","boiling pool","darkcloud pinnacle","elder rise","incendia agave","magatha grimtotem","motega firemane","sacred fire","thousand needles"},rel={"quest:4865","quest:5088","npc:motega-firemane","npc:magatha-grimtotem","zone:thousandneedles","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:elder-rise","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle"},m={start="Motega Firemane",["end"]="Magatha Grimtotem",level="27",faction="Horde",id=5062,ri={"Incendia Agave"}},src={"Sacred Fire"}}
E["quest:5088"] = {t="quest",n="Arikara",z="thunderbluff",s="Magatha Grimtotem sends a warning from Thunder Bluff: Arikara may be hunting High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. She sends Horde adventurers to summon and slay the ancient wind serpent on the burial spires of Thousand Needles.",h="Magatha Grimtotem sends a warning from Thunder Bluff: Arikara may be hunting High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof.",sec={{t="A Beast in the Smoke",b="Magatha Grimtotem enchants the refined Incendia powder, a reagent, to call Arikara. She warns that ancient tauren traditions have changed too quickly under the new Horde alliance, stirring the vengeance of the ferocious wind serpent spirit. Magatha sends you south to the canyon of Thousand Needles. She tells you to cast the powder onto a ritual pyre among the elevated burial sites of Darkcloud Pinnacle.",sp=0},{t="Doubt at Whitereach Post",b="After you slay Arikara on the burial needle and claim its skin, you bring the remains to Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post. Motega is bewildered, finding it hard to believe that a primal spirit would bear malice toward Cairne Bloodhoof. He sets his doubts aside rather than openly question Magatha, the tribe's most powerful shaman, and rewards you for protecting the chieftain.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Arikara?",a="Arikara is a powerful wind serpent summoned atop Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles. Magatha says modern departures from traditional tauren lore stirred the beast to vengeance.",al={"what is arikara","arikara lore","who is the serpent"},it="target"},{q="Why does Magatha Grimtotem want Arikara dead?",a="Magatha says Arikara is hunting Cairne Bloodhoof, the High Chieftain of the tauren. She sends you to destroy the serpent with enchanted Incendia powder before it can threaten Thunder Bluff's leader.",al={"magatha motivation","why kill arikara","why summon arikara"},it="motive"},{q="Where is the sacred fire located to summon her?",a="The unlit sacred fire of life stands atop an isolated spire within Darkcloud Pinnacle in Thousand Needles, where local tauren bury their dead.",al={"arikara location","where to summon arikara","sacred fire of life location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is Motega Firemane skeptical of the hunt?",a="Magatha fears Arikara may be stalking Cairne and asks you to bring proof of the hunt to Motega. Motega's response comes when you deliver the remains.",al={"motega reaction","why is motega confused","cairne arikara make sense"},sp=1,it="conflict"},{q="Is Cairne actually in danger from Arikara?",a="Magatha says she fears Arikara may be stalking Cairne. Her warning calls for action, but does not establish the danger independently.",al={"was cairne really hunted","did arikara want cairne","magatha lying"},sp=1,it="danger"},{q="What is the previous quest in this chain?",a="This story follows \"Sacred Fire,\" when adventurers gather Incendia Agave from the Boiling Pool in Thousand Needles for Magatha Grimtotem to enchant into Incendia powder.",al={"arikara prereq","quest before arikara","sacred fire quest"},it="history",gp=true},{q="What is the Arikara Serpent Skin for?",a="The serpent skin serves as irrefutable physical proof that the vengeful spirit has been summoned and slain. Magatha Grimtotem sends you to deliver her remains directly to Motega Firemane at Whitereach Post, demonstrating that the supposed threat stalking High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof has been extinguished.",al={"arikara serpent skin","serpent skin arikara","why skin arikara"},it="item",add="4b4aa583"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For you as a tauren, the story touches on tension between ancestral rites and political shifts under Cairne Bloodhoof's leadership, with the Grimtotem caught in the matter.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can see the friction between elemental ritual and political intrigue, and Motega's reluctance to challenge Magatha's spiritual authority.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you march into Thousand Needles to neutralize any threat to Cairne Bloodhoof, the venerable High Chieftain you are sworn to protect."},kw={"arikara","cairne bloodhoof","darkcloud pinnacle","incendia powder","magatha grimtotem","motega firemane","thousand needles","whitereach post","wind serpent"},rel={"npc:magatha-grimtotem","npc:motega-firemane","quest:5062","subzone:darkcloud-pinnacle","subzone:whitereach-post","zone:thousandneedles","npc:cairne-bloodhoof","topic:tauren"},m={start="Magatha Grimtotem",["end"]="Motega Firemane",level="28",faction="Horde",id=5088,ri={"Arikara Serpent Skin"}},src={"Arikara (quest)"}}
E["quest:5644"] = {t="quest",n="Devouring Plague",z="thunderbluff",s="Across the sea, Devouring Plague awaits Forsaken priests who travel far from Lordaeron. Miles Welsh in Thunder Bluff sends the adept to Aelthalyste in the Ruins of Lordaeron, where a signature form of Shadow magic awaits.",h="Across the sea, Devouring Plague awaits Forsaken priests who travel far from Lordaeron.",sec={{t="A Summons Home",b="In Thunder Bluff, Miles Welsh judges Forsaken priests who have honed their divine and shadowy disciplines. Posted among the tauren, he recognizes when an acolyte has grown strong enough for higher mysteries. Miles directs them back to the Ruins of Lordaeron rather than attempt to impart those teachings himself in Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="The Secrets of Aelthalyste",b="Beneath the city ruins, Aelthalyste waits in the Undercity's War Quarter. One of the foremost mentors of the Forsaken priesthood, she watches over acolytes who weave shadow. The Devouring Plague drains its victim and carries a corruptive force. Aelthalyste entrusts it only to those able to wield that force without succumbing to it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends you on this quest?",a="Miles Welsh sends you from the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff once your abilities have developed enough. He is a Forsaken priest trainer stationed among the tauren.",al={"who starts devouring plague quest","quest giver devouring plague","miles welsh role"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Aelthalyste located?",a="Aelthalyste is in the Undercity's War Quarter, among the training rings and dark conduits where Forsaken priests gather.",al={"aelthalyste location","where is aelthalyste","devouring plague turn in"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why can't Miles Welsh teach the spell himself?",a="Every priest learns Devouring Plague from a priest trainer at level twenty. Miles honors the Forsaken priesthood's hierarchy by sending worthy adepts home to the Undercity, where Aelthalyste can test them.",al={"why travel to undercity","why see aelthalyste","undercity priest trainer"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Devouring Plague from a lore perspective?",a="Devouring Plague is a devastating curse practiced by Forsaken priests. Its virulent magical affliction consumes a victim's vitality to restore the caster.",al={"what is devouring plague","lore of devouring plague","forsaken disease spell"},it="power"},{q="Is this quest available to other races?",a="No. This summons is for Forsaken priests, though priests of every race learn Devouring Plague from a priest trainer at level twenty.",al={"can trolls do devouring plague quest","can orcs do devouring plague","is this quest undead only"},gp=true},{q="Why is a Forsaken trainer in Thunder Bluff in the first place?",a="After the Forsaken joined the Horde, diplomats and mentors were exchanged across its capitals. Miles Welsh represents the Undercity's spiritual traditions and guides Forsaken traveling through Kalimdor.",al={"why are undead in thunder bluff","forsaken in thunder bluff lore","miles welsh thunder bluff"},it="why_here"},{q="Why does Miles Welsh send you to Undercity?",a="Miles Welsh recognizes that your grasp of the priesthood has outgrown what basic instruction abroad can offer. As a representative stationed among the tauren, his duty is to recognize when a promising Forsaken priest is ready for deeper mysteries. Rather than hold you back, he sends you home to Aelthalyste so you can be initiated into the darker teachings of the Forsaken priesthood.",al={"why does miles welsh want this done","miles welsh motive","why go to undercity"},it="motive",rc="Undead",add="ec2983f6"},{q="Why does Miles Welsh need you to go instead of delivering a message himself?",a="Miles Welsh serves as an emissary and mentor to Forsaken visitors on the high mesas of Thunder Bluff; his post requires him to remain on the bluff to instruct and represent his people. More importantly, the journey is about your personal ascension. The high priestess in the Undercity requires you to present yourself in person so she can judge your spiritual growth firsthand before sharing her lethal teachings.",al={"why me","why send me","why does miles need me"},it="why_me",rc="Undead",add="988f0d1b"}},ang={["class:Priest"]="As a Forsaken priest, you pass an important milestone in your education, moving from basic tenets into the dread Shadow traditions unique to the undead.",["race:Undead"]="As a Forsaken, you embrace harsh afflictions and Shadow magic such as Devouring Plague, unlike the Light practiced in life.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you are linked to distant outposts in Mulgore by spiritual and practical bonds that reach back to the Undercity."},kw={"aelthalyste","devouring plague","forsaken","miles welsh","shadow priest","thunder bluff","undercity","war quarter"},rel={"npc:aelthalyste","npc:miles-welsh","zone:undercity","subzone:war-quarter"},m={start="Miles Welsh",["end"]="Aelthalyste",level="20",faction="Horde",id=5644},src={"Devouring Plague (Thunder Bluff)"}}
E["quest:5922"] = {t="quest",n="Moonglade",z="thunderbluff",s="In Moonglade, a young tauren druid learns to reach nature’s ancient keepers. Guided by Turak Runetotem in Thunder Bluff, the initiate learns to cross the waking world and commune with them directly.",h="In Moonglade, a young tauren druid learns to reach nature’s ancient keepers.",sec={{t="A Sacred Haven Beyond Faction",b="Moonglade lies beyond Kalimdor’s faction struggles. Keeper Remulos, son of Cenarius, watches over the ancient valley, a neutral refuge for all who follow nature. Night elf and tauren druids enter Nighthaven as equals, beneath the Cenarion Circle’s timeless mantle.",sp=0},{t="The Leap Across Kalimdor",b="Turak Runetotem teaches you a unique transport spell bound to Moonglade, aiding your spiritual and martial growth. Through your bond with the natural world, you cross hundreds of leagues in a heartbeat. The valley offers a place to study and a lasting refuge throughout your journey.",sp=0},{t="Awakening the Bear",b="In Nighthaven, you meet Dendrite Starblaze, an elder night elf druid who awaits new pupils. Under his guidance, you begin the first true trial of your calling: learning the bear’s perspective. To embrace the ways of the Claw, you must prove strength, courage, and balance before the Great Bear Spirit.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why can tauren visit a night elf haven like Moonglade?",a="Moonglade is sovereign sacred ground guided by the Cenarion Circle. Devotion to nature and Cenarius takes precedence over the Horde and Alliance conflict there, allowing tauren and night elf druids to train and dwell together in peace.",al={"why tauren in moonglade","horde allowed in moonglade","is moonglade neutral"},it="place"},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is an elder night elf druid in Nighthaven. He mentors newly arrived initiates of both races and administers their early trials as they attune to the ancient animal aspects.",al={"dendrite starblaze","who is dendrite","night elf quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Keeper Remulos?",a="Keeper Remulos is a mighty Keeper of the Grove and son of Cenarius. He is Moonglade’s supreme guardian, watching over the sacred barrows where sleeping druids hibernate and protecting the valley’s sanctity.",al={"keeper remulos","remulos moonglade","who protects moonglade"},it="identity"},{q="What happens after reaching Moonglade?",a="Speaking with Dendrite Starblaze begins your trial with the Great Bear Spirit. He sends you to the spirit’s home in northwestern Moonglade to learn strength of body and heart, the first step toward unlocking bear form.",al={"what do i do next","bear questline","after moonglade quest"},it="next_step"},{q="How does Teleport: Moonglade work lore-wise?",a="Druids weave natural ley energies and their spiritual bond with the Cenarion Circle to cross instantly from wherever they stand to Moonglade’s heart. Teleport: Moonglade is a spiritual anchor, letting them return for instruction and solace whenever summoned.",al={"moonglade teleport lore","teleport spell druid"},it="power"},{q="Where is Turak Runetotem located?",a="Turak Runetotem resides atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. He mentors young tauren who heed the call of the wild before sending them onward to Moonglade.",al={"turak runetotem location","where is turak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Turak Runetotem send you to Moonglade?",a="You are beginning your instruction in the ways of the Claw, specifically learning to commune with and embrace the aspect of the bear. Turak Runetotem cannot guide you through this sacred initiation from Thunder Bluff alone; you must walk the sacred grounds of Moonglade and study under Dendrite Starblaze to forge a genuine bond with nature's wild spirits.",al={"why does turak send me to moonglade","turak runetotem motive","why go to moonglade"},it="motive",add="cadcf30c",nx={8}},{q="Why must you make the pilgrimage to Moonglade yourself?",a="The druidic path demands individual spiritual communion. Moonglade is the sanctuary where Cenarion druids commune directly with ancient forest spirits and the teachings of Cenarius. Embracing the bear's spirit is an intimate, personal trial of character and nature magic that no elder or mentor can undergo on your behalf.",al={"why must i go to moonglade","why cant turak train me here","why me moonglade"},it="why_me",add="979ecc1c"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, this rite of passage bridges traditional tribal beliefs and the broader teachings of the Cenarion Circle. It opens the way to ancient shapeshifting forms.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, arriving in Moonglade is a profound awakening. Your ancient ties to the Earth Mother align with the teachings of Cenarius.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde druid, you can cross paths peacefully with night elf druids in Moonglade, one of the few places in Kalimdor where this is possible."},kw={"bear form","cenarius","dendrite starblaze","moonglade","nighthaven","remulos","teleport moonglade","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:turak-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:nighthaven","npc:remulos","topic:druid","topic:cenarius","topic:tauren","quest:5921"},m={start="Turak Runetotem",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="10",faction="Horde",id=5922},src={"Moonglade (Horde)"}}
E["quest:5926"] = {t="quest",n="Heeding the Call",z="thunderbluff",s="A summons brings a novice druid to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff for personal instruction. Word reaches aspiring shapeshifters through innkeepers and kin across Horde settlements, directing them to Turak Runetotem. There, the sacred trials begin, leading toward mastery of the bear's form and spirit.",h="A summons brings a novice druid to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff for personal instruction.",sec={{t="A Word in the Inn",b="Across Mulgore and Orgrimmar, word reaches you that Turak Runetotem has noticed your early progress. Innkeeper Gryshka in Orgrimmar, Innkeeper Pala in Thunder Bluff, or Gennia Runetotem in Bloodhoof Village may carry the message. The Cenarion Circle does not summon practitioners lightly. Your work with herbs and simple spells has earned you a chance to deepen your bond with nature's wild spirits.",sp=0},{t="The Circle on Elder Rise",b="On Elder Rise, Turak Runetotem guides young tauren toward their ancestral duty. He assists Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem and welcomes you inside the large Cenarion tent. Turak teaches that animals and plants are allies, and solemn charges. Meeting him opens a path beyond basic instruction, toward trials of body and heart and communion with the Great Bear Spirit.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who sends me to speak with Turak Runetotem?",a="Gennia Runetotem in Bloodhoof Village, Innkeeper Pala in Thunder Bluff, or Innkeeper Gryshka in Orgrimmar may deliver the summons. Each has heard that Turak wishes to guide your training personally.",al={"who gives heeding the call","quest giver heeding the call","where do i start heeding the call"},it="identity"},{q="Where can I find Turak Runetotem?",a="Turak Runetotem is inside the Cenarion Circle tent on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, near the city's other druidic mentors.",al={"turak runetotem location","where is turak","how to find turak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this summons so important for young druids?",a="The summons begins your formal shapeshifting trials. Turak directs you to sacred ground in Moonglade to learn the way of the bear and gain your first animal form.",al={"why do i need turak","what is this quest for","druid level 10 quest horde"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Turak Runetotem in the Cenarion hierarchy?",a="Turak Runetotem is a respected tauren druid and a trusted assistant to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. He teaches young initiates about nature's balance with patience and wisdom.",al={"who is turak runetotem","turak lore"},it="identity"},{q="Can other classes accept this quest?",a="No. Only druids who have reached their tenth season of experience receive this summons, as a rite of passage into shapeshifting.",al={"is heeding the call druid only","can shaman do this quest"},gp=true},{q="What happens after I speak to Turak?",a="Turak welcomes you into Cenarius's service and sends you to Moonglade. There, you seek Dendrite Starblaze and begin communion with the Great Bear Spirit.",al={"what comes after heeding the call","next quest after turak"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why am I being sent to Turak Runetotem?",a="Word has reached the settlements that Turak Runetotem, assistant to the Arch Druid, seeks promising young druids in need of deeper instruction. The quest givers simply act as messengers to ensure you do not miss his summons. Turak has offered to instruct you personally, marking the moment your rudimentary training blossoms into true communion with nature and the ways of the wild.",al={"why send to turak","why does gennia want me to speak to turak","why see turak runetotem"},it="motive",add="309dc9df"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you begin the path to mastering animal forms and the sacred journey toward the bear's spirit and fortitude.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, studying under Turak on Elder Rise renews your ancestral bond with the Cenarion Circle and Kalimdor's wild spirits.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you hear the calling through innkeepers in orcish and tauren lands, sustaining your people's bond with the wild earth."},kw={"bear form","bloodhoof village","cenarion circle","druid","elder rise","gennia runetotem","heeding the call","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:turak-runetotem","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:cenarius","subzone:bloodhoof-village","npc:innkeeper-gryshka"},m={start="Gennia RunetotemInnkeeper GryshkaInnkeeper Pala",["end"]="Turak Runetotem",level="10",faction="Horde",id=5926},src={"Heeding the Call (Horde)"}}
E["quest:5932"] = {t="quest",n="Back to Thunder Bluff",z="thunderbluff",s="Your return from Moonglade brings you back to Elder Rise, where Turak Runetotem awaits. Dendrite Starblaze sends you home after your communion with the Great Bear Spirit, so your training can continue among your people.",h="Your return from Moonglade brings you back to Elder Rise, where Turak Runetotem awaits.",sec={{t="A Bridged Fellowship",b="Moonglade brings night elf and tauren practitioners of nature magic together in the Cenarion Circle, apart from the mortal world’s factional divides. After your communion with the Great Bear Spirit, Dendrite Starblaze sends you back to your people. Night elves often see tauren as fledglings in Cenarius’s formal teachings, yet Starblaze recognizes the wisdom and balance of Turak Runetotem.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Bluffs",b="You climb back to Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff and stand before Turak Runetotem, changed by your rite. Communion with ancient totemic spirits such as the Great Bear Spirit runs deep in tauren culture, but the Path of the Claw asks for serious commitment. Your spiritual bond is forged, and Turak prepares you to put your new strength and endurance into practice.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why was a night elf teaching a tauren in Moonglade?",a="The Cenarion Circle is neutral and devoted to preserving nature. In Moonglade, night elf and tauren practitioners set aside the Horde and Alliance divide, so Dendrite Starblaze can guide young tauren druids.",al={"dendrite starblaze horde","why night elf mentor","cenarion circle tauren"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Turak Runetotem?",a="Turak Runetotem is an esteemed tauren druid and one of the Arch Druid’s assistants. He is stationed on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, where he trains young tauren in the path of nature and the claw and links them with the Cenarion Circle.",al={"turak runetotem role","elder rise druid leader"},it="identity"},{q="What did the young druid do right before this quest?",a="Before returning to Mulgore, you traveled to Moonglade to seek and commune with the ancient Great Bear Spirit. You gained its blessing and learned the spiritual core of bear form.",al={"what came before back to thunder bluff","great bear spirit quest"},it="history"},{q="How do young druids travel back to Thunder Bluff from Moonglade?",a="Bunthen Plainswind, in southwestern Nighthaven, offers flight services to carry tauren druids safely back to Thunder Bluff after their rites.",al={"how to get back from moonglade","moonglade flight back"},gp=true},{q="What comes next in the druid's training?",a="After your return, Turak Runetotem sends you to face a physical challenge at the Moonkin Stone, where the Barrens meet Mulgore. There you prove you can channel the spirit’s strength into beast form.",al={"next druid quest","after back to thunder bluff"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze call tauren 'young in the ways of Cenarius'?",a="Tauren legends tell of ancient communion with Cenarius at the dawn of the world, while night elves developed and sustained formal Cenarion druidism for over ten thousand years. Tauren only recently renewed structured study within the Cenarion Circle.",al={"are tauren new druids","tauren druid history cenarius"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze send you back to Thunder Bluff?",a="Your initial commune with the Great Bear Spirit in Moonglade was only the opening step of your awakening. Dendrite Starblaze recognizes that applying the lessons of the wild requires hands-on guidance from your own mentor. He entrusts the next phase of your instruction to Turak Runetotem, a tauren druid who walks with deep balance, so you may prove yourself worthy of the bear's enduring strength.",al={"why send to turak","dendrite starblaze motive","why back to thunder bluff"},it="motive",add="9396c536"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, your journey links Moonglade with the heights of Thunder Bluff and marks your growth along the Path of the Claw.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you bring the wisdom of the ancient spirits home to help and protect your tribes across Mulgore.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help bring shapeshifting defenders to its ranks on the plains of Kalimdor."},kw={"back to thunder bluff","bear form","dendrite starblaze","elder rise","great bear spirit","moonglade","nighthaven","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:turak-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:elder-rise","subzone:nighthaven","topic:druid","topic:cenarius","topic:tauren"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Turak Runetotem",level="10",faction="Horde",id=5932},src={"Back to Thunder Bluff"}}
E["quest:6002"] = {t="quest",n="Body and Heart",z="thunderbluff",s="At the Moonkin Stone, you face a trial of body and heart to master Bear Form. Turak Runetotem sends young tauren druids from Thunder Bluff to summon and defeat Lunaclaw near the border of Mulgore and the Barrens.",h="At the Moonkin Stone, you face a trial of body and heart to master Bear Form.",sec={{t="The Way of the Claw",b="Turak Runetotem tests young tauren druids who seek the path of the Druid of the Claw. After you commune with the Great Bear Spirit in Moonglade, your training turns to a trial of strength. Turak, the elder druid trainer atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, gives worthy aspirants Cenarion Lunardust. He sends you to a sacred stone near the dry frontier where Mulgore meets the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="The Trial of Lunaclaw",b="West of Camp Taurajo, the Moonkin Stone marks a rare Cenarion site in southern Kalimdor. Moonkin are not native to the sun-scorched plains of central Kalimdor, and Lunaclaw guards the stone. Scatter the lunardust across the ancient monument to call Lunaclaw into battle. Defeating the guardian proves your strength and clarity of heart, earning its blessing and awakening the bear's inner essence.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this trial?",a="The trial is the final step for Horde druids seeking Bear Form. By meeting its challenge, you prove yourself ready to follow the path of the Druid of the Claw under Turak Runetotem's guidance.",al={"why do body and heart","what does body and heart do","what do i get from body and heart"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Moonkin Stone located?",a="The Moonkin Stone lies in the Barrens, west of Camp Taurajo along the road toward the Mulgore gate. Just south of the road, behind a tree near a lone tent, you find the sacred stone.",al={"moonkin stone location","where is moonkin stone","where to find moonkin stone"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Lunaclaw?",a="Lunaclaw is a fierce moonkin guardian bound to the Moonkin Stone. Cenarion Lunardust summons it to test whether you have the resolve and calm needed to wield the bear's power.",al={"who is lunaclaw","what is lunaclaw"},it="target"},{q="What happens if I lose the battle against Lunaclaw?",a="If Lunaclaw defeats you, your Cenarion Lunardust is spent. Return to Turak Runetotem atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff for another pouch of dust before trying again.",al={"failed lunaclaw","lost lunardust","died to lunaclaw"},gp=true},{q="Are moonkin native to the Barrens?",a="No. Moonkin are not native to the Barrens or Mulgore. Lunaclaw is an unusual sight on the savannah, bound to Cenarion rites and ancient sites of celestial power.",al={"moonkin in barrens","why are moonkin here","barrens moonkin"},it="origin"},{q="Who gives the quest Body and Heart?",a="Turak Runetotem gives this challenge to initiates returning from Moonglade. He is the senior druid trainer on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"who starts body and heart","body and heart questgiver"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Why does Turak Runetotem want you to face Lunaclaw?",a="Turak Runetotem serves as your mentor in Thunder Bluff and must ensure you are truly prepared to walk the path of the Druid of the Claw. A druid cannot simply be handed the secrets of shifting into a bear; you must prove that you possess both the inner fortitude of spirit and the physical prowess necessary to handle the form's raw power. By invoking and overcoming Lunaclaw, you demonstrate the strength of heart and body needed before he will teach you.",al={"turak runetotem motive","why defeat lunaclaw","turak test motive"},it="motive",add="928957c5"},{q="Why must you complete this trial alone instead of sending guards?",a="This is a sacred rite of passage unique to your spiritual journey as an aspiring druid. Turak cannot undertake the rite for you, nor could the braves of Thunder Bluff assist, because the goal is not to eliminate a menace but to absorb a spiritual lesson. Lunaclaw offers a communion of strength that can only be earned by testing your own balance, resolve, and devotion against the guardian.",al={"why me body and heart","why do i have to fight lunaclaw alone","can guards help face lunaclaw"},it="why_me",add="ac0863bb"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, this rite joins Cenarion teachings with tauren heritage. It lets you take on Bear Form and its fierce resilience.",["race:Tauren"]="As Shu'halo, awakening the bear within joins communion with nature spirits and a way to defend Mulgore's plains from encroaching threats.",["faction:Horde"]="As a tauren druid, you bring resilience to the Horde's front lines and ground its magic in the guardianship of the wild."},kw={"barrens","bear form","body and heart","camp taurajo","cenarion lunardust","lunaclaw","moonkin stone","mulgore","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"quest:5932","npc:turak-runetotem","zone:thunderbluff","zone:barrens","subzone:camp-taurajo","zone:mulgore","quest:6001","topic:druid"},m={start="Turak Runetotem",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6002},src={"Body and Heart (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6126"] = {t="quest",n="Lessons Anew",z="thunderbluff",s="At Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem sends young tauren druids to Moonglade to learn how to cleanse natural and unnatural poisons. The sacred haven is where apprentices begin mastering that art under Dendrite Starblaze, a night elf druid, as real poisonings demand more than practice.",h="At Thunder Bluff, Turak Runetotem sends young tauren druids to Moonglade to learn how to cleanse natural and...",sec={{t="The Gift of Cenarius",b="Cenarius gave druids the power to purge virulent toxins with an incantation, and their charge is to protect the wilds. Turak Runetotem teaches that such magic needs a firm grounding. Before a druid uses it to clear a blight, they must understand venom’s physical toll and learn to treat it by ordinary means.",sp=0},{t="Summons to Nighthaven",b="Turak sends promising acolytes north from Mulgore along sacred pathways to Moonglade. In its peaceful village of Nighthaven, ancient night elf mentors such as Dendrite Starblaze teach elf and tauren practitioners alike. Their shared study reflects the Cenarion Circle’s delicate truce, which rises above the political strife between Horde and Alliance.",sp=0},{t="A Real Crisis in the Barrens",b="Near the Crossroads in the Barrens, uncontrolled poisonings are spreading among the animals. Dendrite Starblaze has no time for a practice exercise: a plea for aid has come from the Crossroads. The request turns a rite of passage into urgent fieldwork, where young druids must face the suffering of wild beasts.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest and where do I find them?",a="Turak Runetotem, the tauren druid trainer, offers the rite on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. He calls on initiates who have shown an early commitment to the Cenarion teachings.",al={"who gives lessons anew","where to get lessons anew","lessons anew quest giver"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is an elder night elf druid who lives in Nighthaven, Moonglade. Despite tensions between night elves and tauren, he teaches young druids of both races the traditions of the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who is dendrite","dendrite starblaze role","who is the night elf in moonglade"},it="identity"},{q="What power is this quest teaching me?",a="Your instruction begins with Cure Poison. The lessons cover venom’s physical and magical nature and teach druids to purge harmful afflictions from allies and wild creatures in their care.",al={"what ability do i learn","what spell is this for","curing poison quest"},it="power"},{q="Why does a tauren have to study under a night elf?",a="The Cenarion Circle is a neutral brotherhood dedicated to the balance of nature. Night elves first formalized modern druidism under Cenarius, then welcomed the tauren back into the order and shared sacred places such as Moonglade despite the faction war.",al={"why night elf trainer","tauren night elf druids","cenarion circle faction"},it="ties"},{q="What is happening at the Crossroads?",a="Wildlife around the Crossroads in the Barrens is suffering an aggressive wave of poisonings that local handlers cannot contain. Dendrite Starblaze turns your training toward the field, where you are to find the source and make a remedy.",al={"crossroads problem","what is poisoning the animals","crossroads sickness"},it="threat"},{q="What is the fastest way to get to Moonglade for this quest?",a="As a druid, you have the innate spell Teleport: Moonglade, which takes you straight to Nighthaven. It avoids the need to travel on foot through treacherous contested lands.",al={"how to get to moonglade","travel to nighthaven","teleport moonglade"},gp=true},{q="Why does Turak Runetotem send you to Moonglade?",a="Turak believes you are finally ready to inherit one of the greatest blessings Cenarius bestowed upon druids: the art of curing deadly toxins through incantation. Such sacred magic is not granted casually. To ensure you respect this power, Turak requires you to first understand poison as an ordinary healer would, directing you to Dendrite Starblaze in Moonglade to begin your formal instruction.",al={"why does turak send me","turak runetotem motive","why go to moonglade"},it="motive",add="be063b64"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you move from basic shapeshifting and skirmishing toward stewardship of the wilds. Your path now begins with learning Cure Poison.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your pilgrimage shows how deeply the Earth Mother's children have reconnected with Cenarius's teachings alongside their night elf peers.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find safe harbor in Moonglade under the Cenarion Circle's sacred protection, even while Horde warriors clash with night elves in Ashenvale."},kw={"cenarion circle","crossroads","cure poison","dendrite starblaze","lessons anew","moonglade","nighthaven","turak runetotem"},rel={"quest:6125","npc:turak-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:nighthaven","quest:5921","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","topic:cenarius"},m={start="Turak Runetotem",["end"]="Dendrite Starblaze",level="14",faction="Horde",id=6126},src={"Lessons Anew (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6130"] = {t="quest",n="Power over Poison",z="thunderbluff",s="At Thunder Bluff, a young Horde druid returns to claim the gift of Cure Poison. After healing poisoned gazelles near the Crossroads with herbal mixtures, the initiate faces Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.",h="At Thunder Bluff, a young Horde druid returns to claim the gift of Cure Poison.",sec={{t="A Lesson in Suffering",b="Before granting a druid the power to cleanse venom, the Cenarion Circle asks them to learn what affliction feels like. Dendrite Starblaze sends the novice to the Crossroads, where Tonga Runetotem has them gather ingredients for a salve. The druid treats poisoned gazelles of the Barrens by hand, without spiritual aid, and sees the struggle ordinary creatures face against natural and unnatural toxins.",sp=0},{t="Return to the Elder Rise",b="After the trial, Dendrite sends the initiate to Turak Runetotem, the grand druid trainer on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. Turak warns that strange, virulent poisons near the Crossroads threaten the plains' natural balance. He commends the initiate's grace under pressure and grants the spiritual art of curing poisons, placing Kalimdor's living creatures in their care.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The trial teaches a Horde druid to cure venom. After preparing remedies by hand to save suffering gazelles, the initiate returns to Turak Runetotem and learns Cure Poison through druidic communion.",al={"why do power over poison","what does this quest do","druid poison quest purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Turak Runetotem located?",a="Turak Runetotem lives atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. He resides in the tent and hollowed roosts where tauren druids commune and train.",al={"turak runetotem location","where is turak","find turak runetotem"},gp=true},{q="Who sends the druid back to Thunder Bluff?",a="Dendrite Starblaze sends the druid back to Thunder Bluff after they heal wildlife near the Crossroads. The night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle is stationed in Moonglade.",al={"who gives power over poison","quest giver","dendrite starblaze"},gp=true},{q="Why did the Cenarion Circle make the druid cure beasts manually first?",a="Dendrite Starblaze teaches the druid to understand the labor and limits involved in curing venom before wielding spiritual magic. Seeing afflicted creatures struggle teaches empathy and respect for nature's balance.",al={"why cure sick manually","why use salves first","druid poison lesson"},it="motive"},{q="What concerns Turak Runetotem about the Crossroads?",a="Turak warns that unnatural, aggressive venoms are reaching wildlife near the Crossroads. He sees this as a grave disruption to the land's balance that calls for vigilance.",al={"turak crossroads concern","crossroads poison balance"},it="threat"},{q="Is this quest available to Alliance druids?",a="Alliance druids take a parallel trial of the same name. Night elf initiates return to Mathrengyl Bearwalker in Darnassus instead of Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise.",al={"can night elves do this","alliance power over poison"},gp=true}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you join physical herbalism in Kalimdor with nature magic and gain the lasting power to purge toxins from allies.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you prove your dedication to the Cenarion Circle and keep the Earth Mother's wisdom alive on the Elder Rise.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help safeguard central Kalimdor's wild lands from unnatural corruption."},kw={"barrens","crossroads","cure poison","dendrite starblaze","elder rise","moonglade","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:turak-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid","subzone:crossroads","quest:6125"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Turak Runetotem",level="14",faction="Horde",id=6130},src={"Power over Poison (Horde)"}}
E["quest:6362"] = {t="quest",n="Ride to Thunder Bluff",z="thunderbluff",s="You carry cured hides from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff by wind rider. The flight links the Barrens to the Horde capital above the plains.",h="You carry cured hides from the Crossroads to Thunder Bluff by wind rider.",sec={{t="Wings Across the Savannah",b="Devrak carries travelers over the Barrens on the back of a wind rider. For many, this is their first flight across Kalimdor. The wyverns link the young Horde's scattered settlements and spare travelers the ground roads, where quilboar and centaur packs roam.",sp=0},{t="Hides for the Armory",b="A bundle of cured hides from the Barrens is bound for Ahanu, a craftsman at Hewa's Armory in Thunder Bluff. Ahanu works beneath the great wind rider roost on the central mesa. Supplies from hunting outposts across the plains help him outfit local warriors and hunters.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Ride to Thunder Bluff?",a="Devrak, the wind rider master at the Crossroads in the Barrens, offers travelers passage when they carry a bundle of hides.",al={"quest giver","where to start ride to thunder bluff","devrak location"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ahanu and where can he be found?",a="Ahanu is a tauren artisan at Hewa's Armory in Thunder Bluff, near the base of the city's wind rider roost.",al={"where is ahanu","ahanu location","hewa's armory"},it="identity"},{q="What is being transported in this delivery?",a="You carry a bundle of cured hides from the Barrens for Ahanu to use in leatherwork and armor crafting.",al={"what am i delivering","bundle of hides"},it="item"},{q="Why use wind riders instead of walking?",a="Wind riders cross the Barrens to Thunder Bluff's high mesas, avoiding the longer ground route through Mulgore and landing at the city's wind rider tower.",al={"why fly to thunder bluff","flight path benefit"},it="purpose"},{q="Where does this delivery chain begin?",a="The delivery begins with Jahan Hawkwing at the Crossroads, who arranged the cured pelts in the earlier task, A Bundle of Hides.",al={"previous quest","hides questline"},it="history"},{q="What comes next after delivering the hides?",a="After receiving the hides, Ahanu sends you upstairs to speak with Tal, Thunder Bluff's Wind Rider Master.",al={"next quest","followup to ride to thunder bluff"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Devrak send you with the hides to Thunder Bluff?",a="As the flight master of Crossroads, Devrak manages the wind riders that connect the disparate settlements of the Horde across Kalimdor. When a courier arrives carrying an urgent bundle of hides bound for Ahanu in Thunder Bluff, Devrak's duty is to provide swift passage and direct travelers to their destination upon landing on the high mesas.",al={"why does devrak want this done","devrak motive","why send bundle of hides"},it="motive",add="ae176b23"},{q="Why does Devrak need you to deliver the hides instead of handling it himself?",a="Devrak is bound to his post at the Crossroads roost, overseeing the wind riders and attending to travelers entering and leaving central Kalimdor. He cannot abandon his duties to run errands into Mulgore, making a willing traveler already headed in that direction the natural choice to complete the delivery.",al={"why not devrak deliver","why send me devrak","why devrak needs a traveler"},it="why_me",add="1fe41edb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a young tauren returning from the Barrens, you can fly straight to the towering capital of your people.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you rely on wind riders to link the Barrens outposts with the strongholds of Durotar and Mulgore."},kw={"ahanu","barrens","bundle of hides","crossroads","devrak","hewa's armory","ride to thunder bluff","wind rider"},rel={"npc:devrak","npc:ahanu","zone:thunderbluff","zone:barrens","quest:4767"},m={start="Devrak",["end"]="Ahanu",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6362},src={"Ride to Thunder Bluff (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6363"] = {t="quest",n="Tal the Wind Rider Master",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, Tal the Wind Rider Master awaits a parcel from Ahanu. It is bound for Jahan Hawkwing at the Crossroads, linking Mulgore’s leatherworkers with Barrens merchants.",h="In Thunder Bluff, Tal the Wind Rider Master awaits a parcel from Ahanu.",sec={{t="Supplies for the Crossroads",b="Ahanu, a leatherworker on Thunder Bluff’s lower rise, sends finished hides to Jahan Hawkwing’s trade stall at the Crossroads. Trade between Mulgore and the Barrens matters to the young Horde, but the journey down the bluffs and across the plains takes hours on foot. Winged couriers carry parcels over the divide.",sp=0},{t="Master of the Mesa's Roost",b="On Thunder Bluff’s highest central tier, Tal tends the city’s wind riders, also called wyverns. The winged beasts cross Kalimdor’s rugged peaks and shifting thermal drafts. Tal arranges flights to outposts such as the Crossroads, carrying messengers and cargo between the tauren capital and its orcish allies.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tal?",a="Tal tends Thunder Bluff’s wind rider roost on the central mesa. He arranges aerial transport for travelers and couriers bound for the Barrens and beyond.",al={"who is tal","tal thunder bluff","wind rider master tal"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Ahanu?",a="Ahanu is a tauren leatherworker in Thunder Bluff. He prepares leather goods for vendors at Kalimdor outposts, including Jahan Hawkwing at the Crossroads.",al={"ahanu","who is ahanu","ahanu thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="Why do the goods need to go to the Crossroads?",a="The Crossroads is a trade and military junction in the Barrens. Goods from Mulgore, including hides and leather garments, supply travelers, hunters, and Horde patrols there.",al={"why crossroads","leather goods crossroads","jahan leather"},it="purpose"},{q="Can I fly straight to the Crossroads with this parcel?",a="You can fly to the Crossroads after visiting the settlement and making contact with Devrak, its wind rider master. Until then, you travel overland on foot.",al={"can i fly to crossroads","tal flight path","how to fly to crossroads"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What are wind riders?",a="Wind riders, also called wyverns, are sentient, venomous winged predators native to Kalimdor’s crags. They allied with the Horde since the Third War and are its chief aerial mounts.",al={"wyverns","what is a wind rider","tauren mounts"},it="origin"},{q="Where does this courier errand lead next?",a="After you deliver the goods to Tal, he directs you to take Ahanu’s parcel across the plains to Jahan Hawkwing at the Crossroads.",al={"next quest","what after tal","where do leather goods go"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Ahanu want this done?",a="Ahanu has crafted a supply of finished leather goods intended for Jahan, a merchant trading out of the Crossroads in the Barrens. To keep commerce flowing between Mulgore and the rest of the Horde territories, craftsmen like Ahanu rely on dependable couriers and the wind riders to transport their wares across the rugged expanse.",al={"ahanu motive","why send leather goods","ahanu jahan delivery"},it="motive",add="989dcaf5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you rely on Thunder Bluff’s wind riders to connect your people with the wider Horde.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you rely on flight routes between the Barrens and Thunder Bluff to carry reinforcements, trade goods, and messages across central Kalimdor."},kw={"ahanu","crossroads","devrak","flight master","jahan","leather goods","tal","thunder bluff","wind rider"},rel={"npc:tal","npc:ahanu","quest:6364","subzone:crossroads","npc:devrak","zone:thunderbluff","quest:4767"},m={start="Ahanu",["end"]="Tal",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6363},src={"Tal the Wind Rider Master (Classic)"}}
E["quest:6364"] = {t="quest",n="Return to Jahan",z="thunderbluff",s="You carry finished leather goods from Thunder Bluff back to Jahan Hawkwing at the Crossroads. The trip introduces travelers to the Horde’s wind rider routes between Mulgore and the Barrens, after they bring hides to Ahanu, the skinner in Thunder Bluff.",h="You carry finished leather goods from Thunder Bluff back to Jahan Hawkwing at the Crossroads.",sec={{t="Wings Over Kalimdor",b="Tal, the wind rider master on Thunder Bluff’s central mesa, arranges flights across central Kalimdor. For many travelers, this is their first ride on a trained wind rider. A rider can take you to another settlement once you have met its wind rider master, such as Devrak at the Crossroads. The beasts cross leagues that would otherwise mean a dangerous journey overland through the Red Rocks and northern Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Commerce of the Crossroads",b="Jahan Hawkwing trades from the Crossroads, where hunters, scouts, and mercenaries gather each day. The flight also carries goods between the settlements. Hides sent to Ahanu on Thunder Bluff’s high rises are made into durable armor and equipment, then flown back to the Barrens crossroads to supply the Horde’s growing frontier efforts.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Jahan Hawkwing?",a="Jahan Hawkwing is a tauren merchant at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He buys and sells leather goods, including gear made by Thunder Bluff artisans from raw beast hides.",al={"jahan","jahan hawkwing lore","who is jahan"},it="identity"},{q="Why do I need to take a wind rider back to the Crossroads?",a="The wind rider carries finished leather goods to Jahan and introduces travelers to the flight network. Tal in Thunder Bluff can send riders only to settlements already connected to the roost, such as Devrak’s at the Crossroads.",al={"why fly back","wind rider return","how do flight paths work"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Ahanu?",a="Ahanu is a leatherworker and skinner on the high rises of Thunder Bluff. He takes raw skins from Barrens hunters and crafts them into finished goods to be sent back for sale.",al={"ahanu","ahanu thunder bluff","who crafted the goods"},it="people"},{q="Who is Devrak?",a="Devrak is the orcish wind rider master at the Crossroads. He manages the roost connecting the Barrens with Horde strongholds such as Orgrimmar and Thunder Bluff.",al={"devrak","crossroads flight master","wind rider master devrak"},it="people"},{q="Can you use a wind rider without speaking to the destination master first?",a="No. A traveler can ride only to outposts where they have already met the local wind rider master and established a connection between the roosts.",al={"flight path rules","unlock flight master","can I fly anywhere"},gp=true},{q="What happens after returning the leather goods to Jahan?",a="Returning the leather goods to Jahan completes the courier chain between Mulgore and the Barrens. Travelers learn how air travel works and can continue helping the Crossroads garrison and merchants.",al={"quest followup","what next","after return to jahan"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tal want the leather goods returned to Jahan?",a="As Thunder Bluff's wind rider master, Tal oversees aerial travel between the mesa and outpost settlements like the Crossroads. Sending you back on a mount with Ahanu's finished leather goods proves the efficiency of the wind riders while completing the trade route between the craftsmen on the heights and Jahan Hawkwing's thriving shop below.",al={"why does tal want this done","tal motive","why send leather to jahan"},it="motive",add="65054dbe"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on wind rider routes linking Mulgore, Durotar, and the Barrens. They bind the Horde’s central Kalimdor territories together.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can see how trade links Mulgore tanners with Barrens outposts and supports the Horde’s frontier."},kw={"ahanu","barrens","crossroads","devrak","jahan hawkwing","tal","thunder bluff","wind rider"},rel={"npc:jahan-hawkwing","npc:tal","npc:devrak","npc:ahanu","zone:thunderbluff","subzone:crossroads","quest:4767"},m={start="Tal",["end"]="Jahan Hawkwing",level="10",faction="Horde",id=6364},src={"Return to Jahan"}}
E["quest:742"] = {t="quest",n="The Ashenvale Hunt",z="thunderbluff",s="In Thunder Bluff, the Ashenvale Hunt calls young Horde champions north to serve at the forest outposts. Heralds direct them to report to Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post for a proving hunt.",h="In Thunder Bluff, the Ashenvale Hunt calls young Horde champions north to serve at the forest outposts.",sec={{t="A Summons from the High Rise",b="Bluff Runner Windstrider carries an open invitation through Thunder Bluff for proven adventurers. The Horde has established footholds in the ancient forest north of the Barrens, and its outposts need young warriors. Those who answer will face a harsher land and test their survival skills beyond Mulgore.",sp=0},{t="The Northern Frontier",b="Ashenvale offers the Horde rich resources and severe peril. Splintertree Post stands along the main road, while a remote outpost lies on the western coast at Zoram Strand. At Splintertree Post, Senani Thunderheart, a veteran outdoorswoman, organizes a great hunt to tame the wilderness and win glory for the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers this quest in Thunder Bluff?",a="Bluff Runner Windstrider offers the summons to passing adventurers in Thunder Bluff. He alerts capable fighters to the Horde's efforts to expand and points them toward outposts that need aid.",al={"who starts ashenvale hunt","quest giver ashenvale hunt","bluff runner windstrider"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Splintertree Post located?",a="Splintertree Post is a fortified Horde settlement in eastern Ashenvale. Travel north across the Barrens border, then follow the eastern forest trail deeper into the woods.",al={"splintertree post location","how to get to splintertree post","where is splintertree"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Senani Thunderheart?",a="Senani Thunderheart is a seasoned tauren tracker stationed at Splintertree Post. She organizes hunts in Ashenvale, testing Horde recruits against the local predators.",al={"senani thunderheart","who is senani","thunderheart npc"},it="target"},{q="Why is the Horde hunting in Ashenvale?",a="The Horde hunts in Ashenvale to gather timber and secure territory. The hunt thins the wild beasts that threaten its camps and lets young adventurers prove themselves in unfamiliar terrain.",al={"why hunt in ashenvale","ashenvale hunt purpose","horde ashenvale goals"},it="conflict"},{q="What is the Zoram Strand mentioned in the briefing?",a="Zoram Strand is a Horde encampment on Ashenvale's far western coast, facing the sea. It is a secondary naval foothold and a bastion against naga and hostile forest dwellers.",al={"what is zoram strand","zoram strand outpost","zoram outpost"},it="place"},{q="What happens after reporting to Senani?",a="When you report to Senani Thunderheart, she welcomes you to the outpost and sets you to the broader hunt, directing you to stalk and conquer Ashenvale's fiercest beasts.",al={"what follows ashenvale hunt","next quest after senani","hunt continuation"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Bluff Runner Windstrider want you to go to Ashenvale?",a="Bluff Runner Windstrider serves as a herald for the Horde, directing capable young champions to where they are needed most. The Horde is aggressively securing its frontier outposts in the untamed forests north of the Barrens, and hunters like Senani Thunderheart require fresh recruits to reinforce their presence and claim glory in the wild.",al={"why send to ashenvale","bluff runner windstrider motive","why does windstrider want this"},it="motive",add="af70e220"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren raised on Mulgore's open plains, you face an unfamiliar challenge beneath Ashenvale's dense, shadowed canopy, watched by kin such as Senani.",["faction:Horde"]="As Horde, you rely on Splintertree Post and Zoram Strand to support the northern supply lines. Fresh recruits help keep wild beasts and hostile natives at bay.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can hone your tracking in Ashenvale's dense woodland, where prowlers move through terrain unlike the dry, open southern savannas."},kw={"ashenvale","hunt","senani","splintertree","thunder bluff","thunderheart","windstrider","zoram strand"},rel={"npc:senani-thunderheart","npc:bluff-runner-windstrider","subzone:splintertree-post","zone:ashenvale","subzone:zoram-strand","zone:barrens","quest:1008","topic:horde"},m={start="Bluff Runner Windstrider",["end"]="Senani Thunderheart",level="20",faction="Horde",id=742},src={"The Ashenvale Hunt (Thunder Bluff)"}}
E["quest:766"] = {t="quest",n="Mazzranache",z="thunderbluff",s="In Bloodhoof Village, Mazzranache's bite leaves Maur Raincaller feverish and near death. A generation ago, the plainstrider haunted his grandfather's tales. Now Maur suffers delirious nightmares as the venom threatens his life.",h="In Bloodhoof Village, Mazzranache's bite leaves Maur Raincaller feverish and near death.",sec={{t="A Legacy of the Plains",b="Maur Raincaller knew Mazzranache only through his grandfather's tales. The elder tauren spoke of a savage plainstrider with glowing red eyes, razor-sharp talons, and a toxic bite unlike that of most Mulgore wildlife. Then Maur met the beast on the open grass. His grandfather's warning came true, and the bite left him badly wounded as he struggled to reach safety.",sp=0},{t="Racing the Infection",b="Mazzranache's venom brings Maur a high fever and nightmarish delirium. He needs a remedy before the infection turns fatal. Traditional tauren medicine draws on the vitality of local beasts, so Maur needs a prairie wolf heart, a flatland cougar femur, a plainstrider scale, and a swoop gizzard. Together, these parts can make a brew to halt the necrotic spread and nurse him back to health.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Mazzranache?",a="Across Mulgore's grasslands, Mazzranache is a savage plainstrider. Its vivid plumage, demonic red eyes, fierce talons, and venomous bite have terrorized travelers for generations.",al={"who is mazzranache","what kind of beast is mazzranache","mazzranache lore"},it="target"},{q="Who is Maur Raincaller?",a="Maur Raincaller lives in Bloodhoof Village. Mazzranache ambushed him and bit his shoulder as he crossed Mulgore, leaving him bedridden with a life-threatening infection.",al={"maur raincaller","who gave me this quest","who is the sick tauren"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Maur need parts from four different beasts?",a="Tauren remedies draw on the strengths and spiritual essences of plains animals to counter potent toxins. A wolf heart, cougar femur marrow, plainstrider scale, and swoop gizzard together make an antidote strong enough to fight Mazzranache's venom.",al={"why wolf heart cougar femur","why animal ingredients","mazzranache remedy ingredients"},it="item"},{q="Did Maur's grandfather kill Mazzranache?",a="No. Maur's grandfather fought Mazzranache years ago but could not defeat the fierce plainstrider. He survived and warned his descendants of its bright colors and vicious attacks.",al={"did grandfather defeat mazzranache","maur grandfather mazzranache","who fought mazzranache before"},it="history"},{q="Does this quest ask me to hunt down Mazzranache itself?",a="No. Maur needs to survive the fever, so the immediate need is to gather the parts for his cure.",al={"do i kill mazzranache","where is mazzranache","hunt mazzranache"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Bloodhoof Village located?",a="Bloodhoof Village lies in central Mulgore, south of Thunder Bluff and east of Stonebull Lake. Young tauren braves begin their journeys across the plains from this settlement.",al={"where is bloodhoof village","bloodhoof village location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Maur Raincaller want this done?",a="Maur's life is directly on the line. While traveling the plains of Mulgore, he crossed paths with Mazzranache, a legendary plainstrider that famously terrorized his grandfather. The creature took a savage, venomous bite out of Maur's shoulder. A debilitating fever has set in, causing delirious nightmares and steadily spreading through his body. Without the animal ingredients required to brew a medicinal cure, the raging infection will soon kill him.",al={"maur raincaller motive","why help maur raincaller","what happened to maur"},it="motive",add="3b88d77e"},{q="Why does Maur need an outsider instead of curing himself?",a="Maur is too grievously wounded and feverish to hunt the beasts of Mulgore himself. Mazzranache's venomous bite has incapacitated him with delirium and exhaustion, leaving him confined to Bloodhoof Village. With time running out before the infection turns fatal, he must rely on passing travelers to track down the swift cougars, swoops, wolves, and plainstriders needed for his remedy.",al={"why can't maur get the parts","why does maur need you","why me mazzranache"},it="why_me",add="ce37bf7e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Maur's remedy follow an old practice: drawing cures from the flora and fauna of the Earth Mother.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can read the plains by tracking prairie wolves, cougars, plainstriders, and swoops across Mulgore.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Bloodhoof Village against Mulgore's dangers and support peace and stability in the tauren homeland."},kw={"bloodhoof village","flatland cougar","maur raincaller","mazzranache","mulgore","plainstrider","prairie wolf","swoop"},rel={"npc:maur-raincaller","subzone:bloodhoof-village"},m={start="Maur Raincaller",level="8",faction="Horde",id=766,ri={"Flatland Cougar Femur","Plainstrider Scale","Prairie Wolf Heart","Swoop Gizzard"}},src={"Mazzranache (Classic)"}}
E["quest:768"] = {t="quest",n="Gathering Leather",z="thunderbluff",s="On Thunder Bluff, Veren Tallstrider asks hunters to bring light leather for the capital. He trades crafted goods for the hides, following the tauren way of making clothing and armor from the plains hunt.",h="On Thunder Bluff, Veren Tallstrider asks hunters to bring light leather for the capital.",sec={{t="Sustaining Thunder Bluff",b="Thunder Bluff needs skilled hands to make clothing and armor for its growing population. Veren Tallstrider works skins into useful goods and asks young hunters returning from the plains to bring him their quarry. Their hunts help supply the capital and feed the tribe.",sp=0},{t="The Way of the Hunt",b="Tauren hunt across the grasslands to feed, clothe, and shelter the tribe. Veren Tallstrider asks hunters who would bring honor to their clan for light leather from local wildlife. In return, he trades crafted goods for twelve well-kept hides, sustaining the ties that bind tauren society.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Veren Tallstrider?",a="Veren Tallstrider is a leatherworker in Thunder Bluff. He crafts clothing and armor for the tauren, and trades his work for skins from the plains.",al={"veren tallstrider","who gives gathering leather","leather questgiver thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="What does Veren Tallstrider need?",a="Veren needs twelve pieces of light leather from beasts in Mulgore and neighboring territories. He uses the hides to craft goods for Thunder Bluff.",al={"gathering leather requirements","what to bring veren","gathering leather materials"},it="wants"},{q="Where does this quest take place?",a="You meet Veren Tallstrider atop Thunder Bluff. To bring him what he needs, hunt wild beasts in the grasslands below.",al={"where is veren tallstrider","gathering leather location"},it="place"},{q="Why do the tauren place so much importance on hunting beasts?",a="Tauren hunting honors the balance with the Earth Mother. The tribe uses every part of a fallen beast: its flesh for food, and its bones and cured hides for tools, tents, and armor.",al={"tauren hunting culture","why hunt leather","tauren leather lore"},it="history"},{q="Can any Horde adventurer undertake this task?",a="Yes. Any traveler loyal to the Horde can help gather leather if Veren believes they are eager to test their mettle on the plains.",al={"who can do gathering leather","is gathering leather horde only"},gp=true},{q="What happens once the leather is delivered?",a="After you deliver the hides, Veren inspects their quality and commends your work. He gives you a crafted piece of gear in fair trade.",al={"gathering leather turn in","veren tallstrider reward"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Veren Tallstrider want Light Leather?",a="Veren Tallstrider is a leatherworker who crafts clothing and armor for the residents of Thunder Bluff. To supply the city and sustain his craft, he relies on hunters to bring in quality hides from the plains of Mulgore.",al={"why veren needs leather","veren tallstrider motive","why light leather veren"},it="motive",add="1249c214"},{q="What is the Light Leather used for?",a="The leather is turned into essential garments, protective armor, and useful goods for the tauren dwelling high on the mesas of Thunder Bluff, as well as gear fashioned in trade for traveling hunters.",al={"what is light leather for","light leather use","how does veren use light leather"},it="item",add="cd30155e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren hunter, you honor a fallen beast by turning its hide into useful goods. This discipline has passed through generations.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you are well suited to track prey across Mulgore's plains and gather the light hides Veren needs.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help supply Thunder Bluff's artisans while the young capital strengthens its defenses and trade networks."},kw={"gathering leather","leatherworking","light leather","mulgore","tauren hunt","thunder bluff","veren tallstrider"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Veren Tallstrider",faction="Horde",id=768,ri={"Light Leather"}},src={"Gathering Leather"}}
E["quest:769"] = {t="quest",n="Kodo Hide Bag",z="thunderbluff",s="Veren Tallstrider teaches Thunder Bluff's apprentice leatherworkers a craft drawn from the plains. He asks for cured light leather and sturdy thread.",h="Veren Tallstrider teaches Thunder Bluff's apprentice leatherworkers a craft drawn from the plains.",sec={{t="A Lesson on the Mesa",b="Veren Tallstrider teaches leatherworking on Thunder Bluff's crafting rises. He follows the nomadic way of wasting nothing from the hunt. Bring cured light leather and sturdy thread, and he will teach you. With these basic materials, apprentices show they can make goods to carry survival gear across Kalimdor's rugged expanses.",sp=0},{t="Spirit of the Kodo",b="To the tauren, the kodo is a sign of endurance, strength, and steady resolve. Its thick hide guards against brambles, biting wind, and beast claws. Making bags and garments from kodo hide is useful work, and it honors the animal that has fed and carried the Shu'halo across Mulgore's plains for generations.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who offers the Kodo Hide Bag quest?",a="Veren Tallstrider, a tauren leatherworking trainer and merchant in Thunder Bluff, offers the training.",al={"quest giver","where to get kodo hide bag quest","veren tallstrider location"},it="identity"},{q="Who is eligible to undertake this task?",a="Leatherworkers with at least apprentice skill level ten can receive this training from Veren Tallstrider.",al={"who can take this quest","quest requirements","profession requirement"},gp=true},{q="What materials does Veren Tallstrider require?",a="Veren Tallstrider asks for four pieces of Light Leather and four spools of Coarse Thread to replenish his trade supplies before he shares his pattern.",al={"what items are needed","kodo hide bag materials","quest turn-in items"},gp=true},{q="Why is kodo hide considered significant to tauren crafters?",a="Kodos embody resilience and physical might, qualities the tauren cherish. Gear made from their hides honors the creature's spirit and equips travelers crossing the plains.",al={"why kodo hide","tauren kodo meaning","kodo importance"},it="origin"},{q="What does Veren Tallstrider teach upon completion?",a="After receiving the supplies, Veren teaches the crafter to stitch a Kodo Hide Bag.",al={"quest reward","what do i get","bag pattern"},gp=true},{q="Where can the necessary materials be acquired?",a="You can skin low-level beasts throughout Mulgore and nearby lands for Light Leather. Trade and tailoring vendors sell Coarse Thread.",al={"where to get light leather","where to get coarse thread"},gp=true},{q="Why does Veren Tallstrider want this done?",a="Veren Tallstrider takes pride in nurturing the next generation of tauren leatherworkers. Mulgore's kodo beasts are revered for their strength and endurance, and crafting a traditional bag from their hides is a foundational skill. By asking you to gather working materials for his trade, Veren tests your dedication and resourcefulness before passing down the techniques of the craft.",al={"why does veren tallstrider want leather","veren tallstrider motive","why kodo hide bag quest"},it="motive",add="c94273ea"},{q="What is the Light Leather for?",a="Light Leather serves as the fundamental trade supply Veren Tallstrider requires in exchange for his instruction. Working cured hides is the core of tauren leathercraft, and providing quality leather proves you have mastered the basics of treating animal skins before learning how to stitch specialized containers like kodo hide bags.",al={"what is light leather used for","why bring light leather","light leather purpose"},it="item",add="1f62e959"},{q="What is the Coarse Thread for?",a="Coarse Thread is a vital tailoring and leatherworking staple used to bind thick hides together. To construct durable packs capable of enduring the plains of Mulgore, a craftsman needs sturdy cordage that will not snap under heavy strain or harsh weather.",al={"why coarse thread","coarse thread purpose","what is coarse thread for"},it="item",add="7d0f7d7f"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As Shu'halo, you honor the Earth Mother's bounty and preserve ancestral ways by learning to craft reliable gear from the mighty kodo.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rely on Thunder Bluff's craftsmen for goods that keep hunters, scouts, and warriors equipped across central Kalimdor."},kw={"coarse thread","kodo","kodo hide bag","leatherworking","light leather","mulgore","thunder bluff","veren tallstrider"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore"},m={start="Veren Tallstrider",faction="Horde",id=769,ri={"Coarse Thread","Light Leather"}},src={"Kodo Hide Bag (quest)"}}
E["quest:776"] = {t="quest",n="Rites of the Earthmother",z="thunderbluff",s="High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof sends you across Mulgore to track down the great kodo Arra'chea. Even after the old rites, he asks his people to prove their strength, tracking, and devotion anew. Arra'chea's horn shows Cairne you are ready to serve the wider Horde.",h="High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof sends you across Mulgore to track down the great kodo Arra'chea.",sec={{t="A Chieftain's Measure",b="In Thunder Bluff, a young tauren's childhood gives way to duty. High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof asks young hunters to keep proving themselves. Reaching the high bluffs begins a life of service to the United Tauren Tribes. Cairne asks for more than a hunt for small pests: he wants proof of fieldcraft, shown by tracking and cleanly harvesting one of Mulgore's renowned wandering beasts.",sp=0},{t="The Hunt for Arra'chea",b="Arra'chea is a massive, legendary kodo whose looping path crosses the golden grasses northeast of Thunder Bluff. Bringing down this great beast takes patient stalking across the open savannah, not brute force alone. Return Arra'chea's horn to the high rise, and Cairne sends skinners and gatherers to use every part of the sacred beast for the city's provisions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest?",a="High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof gives you this hunt from his seat atop Thunder Bluff's high rise.",al={"quest giver","who gives rites of the earthmother","cairne quest"},it="leader"},{q="What is Arra'chea?",a="Arra'chea is a renowned kodo who wanders Mulgore's plains. His great horn proves a hunter's tracking skill and martial prowess.",al={"who is arrachea","what is arrachea","arrachea lore"},it="target"},{q="Where can I find Arra'chea?",a="Arra'chea roams a broad circular path northeast of Thunder Bluff's bluffs, circling the open plains clockwise.",al={"where is arrachea","arrachea location","arrachea path"},gp=true},{q="Why does Cairne ask for this hunt after I already completed the earlier rites?",a="For the tauren, earning an initial place is only the beginning of duty. Cairne asks you to keep proving your strength, humility, and hunting skill for the tribe.",al={"why do this quest","why kill arrachea","point of rites"},it="motive"},{q="What happens to Arra'chea's body after the horn is taken?",a="Cairne sends a gathering party to retrieve Arra'chea's meat and hide. The kill feeds and clothes Thunder Bluff, as tauren tradition teaches them to honor their prey.",al={"arrachea meat","what happens to the kodo","carcass lore"},it="next_step"},{q="Is this the same quest as the early starter rites?",a="No. The early trials in Camp Narache teach an initiate the foundational Rites of the Earthmother. This hunt in Thunder Bluff is Cairne's personal test of your continuing worth as a hunter.",al={"rites of the earthmother differences","which rites quest","camp narache rites"},gp=true},{q="What is the Horn of Arra'chea for?",a="The horn serves as physical proof of your successful hunt. Tauren tradition places great honor on the skills of tracking and taking down mighty beasts, and presenting Arra'chea's horn directly to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof proves you possess the prowess needed to provide for and protect your people.",al={"horn of arra'chea use","why take horn of arrachea","horn of arrachea purpose"},it="item",add="d7a516d7"},{q="Why does Cairne Bloodhoof send you instead of the city guards?",a="This hunt is not an errand of defense or simple resource gathering—it is a traditional trial. While you may have passed the initial Rites of the Earthmother to reach Thunder Bluff, Cairne expects every hunter of the tribe to continually prove their worth and self-reliance through great deeds rather than resting on past accomplishments.",al={"why send me","why not send guards for arrachea","why does cairne need me"},it="why_me",add="a7e696eb"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a young shu'halo, you stand before Cairne Bloodhoof to bring him Arra'chea's horn. The rite proves your prowess honors your ancestors and Mulgore's herds.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you stalk a solitary, wandering behemoth across the golden plains. Tauren trackmasters pass this ancient hunting way down through generations.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help provide Thunder Bluff with food, leather, and materials by felling Arra'chea. The hunt reflects the shared struggle to survive that sustains the young Horde."},kw={"arra'chea","arrachea","bloodhoof","cairne","earthmother","horn","hunt","kodo","mulgore","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:cairne-bloodhoof","zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","quest:763","quest:421"},m={start="Cairne Bloodhoof",level="14",faction="Horde",id=776,ri={"Horn of Arra'chea"}},src={"Rites of the Earthmother (3)"}}
E["quest:8360"] = {t="quest",n="Dancing for Marzipan",z="thunderbluff",s="Innkeeper Pala asks Dancing for Marzipan visitors to dance during Hallow's End in Thunder Bluff. The treat is meant for a sick orphan, and the custom brings holiday cheer to Mulgore's high mesas.",h="Innkeeper Pala asks Dancing for Marzipan visitors to dance during Hallow's End in Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Dance on the Bluff",b="During Hallow's End, Innkeeper Pala keeps the trick-or-treat custom in Thunder Bluff. Even when you come for an ailing child, she asks for a festive dance before giving up her Thunder Bluff Marzipan.",sp=0},{t="Tricks for Treats",b="For Pala, the custom is simple: step forward and dance to earn a sweet. When you have entertained her, she gives you the marzipan and warm wishes for the sick youth waiting for it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of Dancing for Marzipan?",a="You dance for Innkeeper Pala in Thunder Bluff to receive a piece of Thunder Bluff Marzipan. It joins the holiday treats gathered for a sick orphan during Hallow's End.",al={"why dance for marzipan","marzipan quest goal","dancing for marzipan objective"},it="purpose"},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Innkeeper Pala, the tauren innkeeper who serves visitors and locals in Thunder Bluff, offers it during Hallow's End.",al={"who starts dancing for marzipan","pala quest","innkeeper pala thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Pala insist on a dance if the candy is for a sick child?",a="Pala honors the trick-or-treat custom: you perform a trick to earn a sweet, keeping Hallow's End joyful and lively.",al={"why do i have to dance","why does pala want a dance"},it="motive"},{q="What reward do you receive for dancing?",a="You receive a piece of Thunder Bluff Marzipan, a local festive confection needed for the larger Hallow's End treat collection for the sick child.",al={"marzipan reward","dancing for marzipan item"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Can Alliance players complete this quest?",a="No. Innkeeper Pala lives in Thunder Bluff, so only members of the Horde can visit her for this stop on the holiday treat run.",al={"is this horde only","alliance dancing for marzipan"},it="side",gp=true},{q="When is this quest available?",a="It is available during Hallow's End, the annual autumn holiday when innkeepers across Azeroth offer special sweets and festive games.",al={"when can i get marzipan","hallows end marzipan quest"},gp=true}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you can find Innkeeper Pala bringing holiday cheer to Mulgore with a dance for a sweet cause.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can share a lighter moment amid the faction's daily struggles and bring holiday joy to an orphan as you travel between capital cities."},kw={"dancing for marzipan","hallow's end","innkeeper pala","marzipan","mulgore","thunder bluff","trick-or-treat"},rel={"npc:innkeeper-pala","zone:thunderbluff"},m={start="Innkeeper Pala",faction="Horde",id=8360},src={"Dancing for Marzipan (Horde)"}}
E["quest:853"] = {t="quest",n="Apothecary Zamah",z="thunderbluff",s="Apothecary Helbrim needs his volatile fungal emulsion carried from the Barrens to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff. The mixture must reach her laboratory beneath Spirit Rise before it loses its potency.",h="Apothecary Helbrim needs his volatile fungal emulsion carried from the Barrens to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder...",sec={{t="A Fragile Cargo",b="Apothecary Helbrim has cooked fungal blooms from the Barrens oases into a delicate emulsion. The brew quickly loses strength once prepared. Helbrim cannot travel to Mulgore in time, so he entrusts the flask to a reliable runner bound for Thunder Bluff.",sp=0},{t="Under the Gazes of the Shamans",b="Apothecary Zamah works in the Pools of Vision, a cavern beneath the sacred heights of Spirit Rise. Forsaken mages and priests share the underground refuge. Beneath the tauren sanctuary, the Royal Apothecary Society quietly studies raw materials gathered across the continent.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is there a time limit on this delivery?",a="Helbrim's rendered fungal emulsion is chemically volatile. Left exposed or untreated too long, its compounds break down and lose potency, leaving the mixture useless for Zamah's work.",al={"why timed","quest timer","rendered spores timer"},it="item"},{q="Where can I find Apothecary Zamah?",a="Apothecary Zamah can be found in the Pools of Vision in Thunder Bluff. The cavern entrance lies concealed on Spirit Rise, beneath the shamans' tents.",al={"where is zamah","zamah location","find zamah"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Apothecary Helbrim?",a="Apothecary Helbrim is an alchemist of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed at the Crossroads in the Barrens. He studies local plants and animals to learn how Kalimdor's native life might serve the Forsaken.",al={"who is helbrim","helbrim crossroad"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Royal Apothecary Society doing in Thunder Bluff?",a="The Royal Apothecary Society quietly studies specimens gathered across Kalimdor in Thunder Bluff's Pools of Vision. The Forsaken, allies within the Horde, keep representatives such as Zamah there and maintain supply links with other outposts.",al={"why forsaken in thunder bluff","apothecaries in pools of vision"},it="purpose"},{q="What were the fungal spores originally used for?",a="The fungal spores grow around the Barrens' lush oases, thriving in the desert. Helbrim rendered them down to study their biological traits and alchemical uses before sending them to Zamah.",al={"why spores","barrens fungi use"},it="origin"},{q="What happens if the timer runs out?",a="If the timer expires, the emulsion spoils and loses its potency. You must return to Apothecary Helbrim at the Crossroads for a fresh batch to carry to Thunder Bluff.",al={"failed timer","spores expired"},gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Helbrim want the rendered spores delivered so quickly?",a="Apothecary Helbrim has successfully processed the strange fungal spores harvested from the Barrens into an unstable emulsion. The mixture degrades rapidly, and only his associate, Apothecary Zamah, has the specialized reagents and facilities in the Pools of Vision required to properly stabilize, reseal, and analyze it before its potency is lost forever.",al={"why send spores to zamah","helbrim motive","why does helbrim want this delivered"},it="motive",add="f0da41d1"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As an Undead, carrying Helbrim's work to Zamah strengthens the Royal Apothecary Society's hidden research network across central Kalimdor's frontier.",["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you may welcome the Forsaken as allies while still eyeing their strange brews in the sacred Pools of Vision with suspicion.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help keep communication and supplies moving between the Barrens outposts and Thunder Bluff's high mesa."},kw={"apothecary helbrim","apothecary zamah","fungal spores","pools of vision","rendered spores","royal apothecary society","spirit rise","the barrens","thunder bluff"},rel={"quest:848","npc:apothecary-helbrim","subzone:pools-of-vision","subzone:spirit-rise","zone:thunderbluff","zone:barrens"},m={level="15",faction="Horde",id=853},src={"Apothecary Zamah (quest)"}}
E["quest:860"] = {t="quest",n="Sergra Darkthorn",z="thunderbluff",s="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn awaits tauren hunters leaving Mulgore behind. Melor Stonehoof sends them north into the Barrens, where danger grows harsher and the Horde's lands reach beyond their home.",h="At the Crossroads, Sergra Darkthorn awaits tauren hunters leaving Mulgore behind.",sec={{t="Leaving the Sacred Hills",b="When their first trials are done, Melor Stonehoof sends young tauren hunters east from Mulgore. Bloodhoof Village and its valleys are familiar ground, where patient tracking has prepared them for what comes next. Now he tells them to pack their gear and cross the mountain pass into the Barrens, leaving their homeland's safety for harsher country.",sp=0},{t="The Road to the Crossroads",b="The road winds through red rock canyons before opening onto the Barrens' broad, sun-scorched savanna. There, where Kalimdor's central trade routes meet, the Crossroads is a fortified settlement shared by orcs, trolls, and tauren.\n\nSergra Darkthorn waits on its eastern side. The experienced orc shaman demands much of the hunters she guides. She teaches those who come to stalk the Barrens' fierce wildlife, testing their eagerness against the discipline the wilderness requires.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives this quest and where do I find them?",a="Melor Stonehoof gives the task to tauren hunters. You can find the hunter mentor on Hunter Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"who gives sergra darkthorn quest","melor stonehoof location","where to start"},gp=true},{q="Where is Sergra Darkthorn located?",a="Sergra Darkthorn waits at the Crossroads in the central Barrens, near its eastern side, watchtowers, and corrals.",al={"sergra darkthorn location","where is sergra","find sergra"},gp=true},{q="How do I get to the Crossroads from Mulgore?",a="From Thunder Bluff, travel south past Bloodhoof Village, then take the eastern road through the canyon pass into the Barrens. After the border gate, follow the main dirt road east to its fork, then head north to the Crossroads.",al={"directions to crossroads","mulgore to barrens","how to get to crossroads from thunder bluff"},gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="The journey guides hunters from Mulgore to the Crossroads, a major center in the Barrens, where local hunting work awaits.",al={"why do this quest","sergra darkthorn purpose","is this a breadcrumb"},it="purpose"},{q="Do orcs and trolls get this quest?",a="Orcs and trolls receive a similar task called Conscript of the Horde in Durotar. It sends them from Razor Hill to the Barrens, where they can also meet Sergra and take work from her.",al={"orc version","troll version","durotar breadcrumb"},gp=true},{q="What does Sergra Darkthorn teach hunters?",a="Sergra tests incoming hunters against Barrens wildlife, beginning with plainstriders and prowlers. She teaches endurance, respect for the land, and mental resilience over brute force.",al={"sergra role","what does sergra do","sergra hunting"}},{q="Why does Melor Stonehoof send you to Sergra Darkthorn?",a="Melor Stonehoof recognizes that you have outgrown the gentle hunting grounds of Mulgore. To truly walk the hunter's path and test your spirit, you must pit yourself against the fierce, strong-willed beasts of the Barrens. Melor sends you to Sergra Darkthorn at the Crossroads because she has the seasoned expertise needed to guide your training across those harsh, sun-baked plains.",al={"why send to sergra","melor stonehoof motive","why go to crossroads"},it="motive",add="94d282e7"},{q="Why does Melor choose you for this journey?",a="This journey is not a chore or an errand for Thunder Bluff's guards; it is an essential rite of passage for an aspiring hunter. Melor cannot walk the path for you. You have shown the dedication and spirit needed to advance your training, and only by traveling into the wild Barrens yourself can you temper your instincts and grow into a master of the hunt.",al={"why me melor","why does melor send me"},it="why_me",add="bb525daf"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren raised in Mulgore, reporting to Sergra takes you beyond your ancestral homeland and into the wider Horde's service.",["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you leave simple tracking of local game behind and face the predators and harsh conditions of Kalimdor's inner savannas.",["faction:Horde"]="At the Crossroads, you find a center of Horde logistics where orcish resilience, Darkspear cunning, and tauren tradition meet under veterans such as Sergra."},kw={"crossroads","hunter's way","melor stonehoof","mulgore","plainstrider","sergra darkthorn","the barrens","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:melor-stonehoof","subzone:crossroads","zone:barrens","zone:mulgore","quest:840","topic:tauren","topic:horde","subzone:bloodhoof-village"},m={start="Melor Stonehoof",["end"]="Sergra Darkthorn",level="10",faction="Horde",id=860},src={"Sergra Darkthorn (quest)"}}
E["quest:8678"] = {t="quest",n="Proudhorn the Elder",z="thunderbluff",s="During the Lunar Festival, Proudhorn the Elder receives visitors atop Thunder Bluff. Tauren honor him as an ancestral spirit and pay respect to the wisdom of those who watch over Mulgore and the Horde.",h="During the Lunar Festival, Proudhorn the Elder receives visitors atop Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Spirit of Mulgore",b="During the Lunar Festival, Proudhorn the Elder appears high on Thunder Bluff's windblown mesas. Tauren hold their ancestors' voices in the highest regard. They believe ancient leaders and sages remain as spirits, offering guidance and strength to the living.",sp=0},{t="Homage and Ancestral Blessing",b="Travelers who climb Thunder Bluff's heights to honor Elder Proudhorn are welcomed as vital flames of life. In return for their homage, he gives them a Coin of Ancestry, a sign of communion between the enduring past and the living champions who fight for the world's future.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Proudhorn the Elder?",a="Proudhorn the Elder is an honored tauren ancestral spirit who appears atop Thunder Bluff during the Lunar Festival to receive homage from champions across Azeroth.",al={"wheathoof","elder wheathoof","who is wheathoof"}},{q="Where can I find Proudhorn the Elder?",a="You can find Elder Proudhorn atop Thunder Bluff, the tauren capital on the central mesas overlooking Mulgore's plains.",al={"where is elder wheathoof","wheathoof location","thunder bluff elder"}},{q="What is the purpose of visiting him?",a="Visiting Elder Proudhorn lets you honor the spirits of the past during the Lunar Festival. He gives visitors his blessing and a Coin of Ancestry.",al={"why visit wheathoof","wheathoof quest","lunar festival elder"}},{q="Can Alliance players visit Elder Proudhorn?",a="Elder Proudhorn blesses any respectful traveler, but Alliance travelers face great danger in Thunder Bluff from its vigilant guards and Horde defenders.",al={"can alliance talk to wheathoof","alliance thunder bluff elder"}},{q="What is a Coin of Ancestry?",a="A Coin of Ancestry is a ceremonial token granted by ancient spirits during the Lunar Festival. It symbolizes respect and communion between the living and their ancestors.",al={"coin of ancestry","lunar festival coin"}},{q="How do the tauren view their elders?",a="Tauren revere their ancestors as guardians and teachers. Their spirits remain woven into the land, guiding those attuned to the Earth Mother.",al={"tauren ancestor worship","tauren elders lore"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, honoring Elder Proudhorn is a sacred homecoming that renews your bond with the spirits watching over Mulgore.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you are welcome to climb Thunder Bluff and pay homage to this elder at the heart of tauren power.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can commune with an ancestral elder through a profound rite with the enduring spirit world."},kw={"ancestor","coin of ancestry","elder","lunar festival","mulgore","spirit","thunder bluff","proudhorn"},m={id=8678},src={"Wheathoof the Elder"}}
E["quest:886"] = {t="quest",n="The Barrens Oases",z="thunderbluff",s="Beneath the Barrens, strange power stirs, and Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem takes heed from Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. He sends travelers east through Mulgore to meet Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads and investigate the new waters.",h="Beneath the Barrens, strange power stirs, and Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem takes heed from Thunder Bluff's...",sec={{t="A Disturbance in the Drought",b="For generations, the Barrens have known drought while Mulgore flourishes under the Earth Mother's care. Now tauren druids on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise feel strange currents waking beneath the plains. Life stirs where it should not, and the Cenarion Circle fears the power behind it may endanger the land and its creatures.",sp=0},{t="East Beyond Mulgore",b="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem sends Tonga Runetotem to investigate the strange stirrings. The wilderness is too dangerous for one investigator, so Hamuul asks travelers leaving Mulgore to follow. Go east past Bloodhoof Village and through the mountain passes to the Crossroads, where Tonga waits for news. There, in the Barrens, stands the Horde's busy heart.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Hamuul Runetotem concerned about the Barrens?",a="Hamuul Runetotem and Thunder Bluff's druids sense an unnatural power flowing into the Barrens soil. Life quickens in a land known for drought, pointing to forces at work beneath the plains.",al={"why barrens oases","hamuul concern","why send to cross roads"},it="motive"},{q="Where can I find Tonga Runetotem?",a="Tonga Runetotem waits at the Crossroads in the central Barrens. Follow the main road east from Mulgore, then take the northern trail to the settlement.",al={"tonga runetotem location","where is tonga","tonga crossroads"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Is this quest only available to tauren?",a="Hamuul Runetotem offers this work mainly to travelers leaving Mulgore. Any Horde traveler can meet Tonga Runetotem at the Crossroads and help investigate the oases.",al={"can non tauren get barrens oases","who gives the barrens oases"},gp=true},{q="What awaits at the end of the road from Bloodhoof Village?",a="The road east from Bloodhoof Village crosses the mountain pass into the Barrens. Turn north at the fork to reach the Crossroads through the wilderness.",al={"road to crossroads","mulgore to barrens path"},it="place"},{q="What are the strange powers Hamuul senses?",a="The druids sense magical currents behind spring-fed oases in a land known for drought. Tonga Runetotem is there to learn whether this growth brings a blessing or dangerous corruption.",al={"what powers in barrens","oases mystery","unnatural energy barrens"},it="danger"},{q="Why are the Barrens considered so dangerous for young adventurers?",a="Raptors, plainstriders, and hostile centaur tribes roam the vast Barrens. Hamuul warns travelers to stay on patrolled trade paths, where the wilderness is less likely to overwhelm them.",al={"barrens danger","why stay on road"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem send you instead of going himself?",a="As the Arch Druid and spiritual leader of the tauren druids in Thunder Bluff, Hamuul Runetotem must remain atop the mesa to guide his brethren and counsel the High Chieftain. He has already dispatched Tonga Runetotem into the field to investigate the disturbances, but Tonga cannot unravel the mystery alone. Hamuul relies on capable, rising champions like you to act as Tonga's hands and eyes in the wider world.",al={"why send me","why not go himself","why does hamuul need me"},it="why_me",add="caac276a"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For a tauren leaving Mulgore's sacred meadows for the first time, this is a step into the wider duty of protecting Kalimdor's balance.",["class:Druid"]="As a young druid trained under Hamuul Runetotem, you are entrusted to heed the earth and heal nature's fragile balance.",["faction:Horde"]="The Crossroads links the Horde's western holdings to the coast. A magical disturbance nearby brings deep strategic and spiritual concern."},kw={"bloodhoof village","cenarion circle","crossroads","elder rise","hamuul runetotem","mulgore","oases","the barrens","thunder bluff","tonga runetotem"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","quest:870","zone:barrens","subzone:crossroads","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid","topic:tauren","zone:mulgore"},m={start="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem",["end"]="Tonga Runetotem",level="10",faction="Horde",id=886},src={"The Barrens Oases"}}
E["quest:98362"] = {t="quest",n="To Thunder Bluff",z="thunderbluff",s="After communion in Moonglade, a young tauren druid makes a triumphant return to Thunder Bluff. Having earned the Great Cat Spirit's favor, the initiate goes to Turak Runetotem on the Elder Rise to master feline shapeshifting.",h="After communion in Moonglade, a young tauren druid makes a triumphant return to Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="Return from Moonglade",b="You return to Mulgore after meeting Dendrite Starblaze and the Great Cat Spirit in Moonglade's sacred groves. The communion joins ancient night elven teachings with the tauren's earthen heritage, marking a pivotal milestone in a druid's training.",sp=0},{t="Mastering the Cat Form",b="Turak Runetotem awaits you atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Dendrite guided your communion with the Great Cat Spirit; Turak now teaches the physical change. With the spirit's blessing acknowledged, the elder trainer shares the knowledge to take the cat's swift, predatory shape.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this quest begin and end?",a="Dendrite Starblaze gives you this charge in Moonglade's sacred haven. You return to the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff to speak with Turak Runetotem.",al={"where do i turn this in","who starts to thunder bluff","to thunder bluff quest turn in"},gp=true},{q="What is the purpose of this quest?",a="It is the concluding transition in the druid trial of the cat. After earning the Great Cat Spirit's blessing in Moonglade, you return to your mentor in Thunder Bluff to learn Cat Form.",al={"why do to thunder bluff","what do i get from to thunder bluff","cat form quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who is Turak Runetotem?",a="Turak Runetotem is a respected elder of the tauren druids on Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise. He oversees the training and initiation of young Horde druids who seek to harmonize with nature and master their shapeshifting forms.",al={"turak runetotem lore","who is turak"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Dendrite Starblaze?",a="Dendrite Starblaze is a night elf keeper of the Cenarion Circle who guides visiting druids in Nighthaven, Moonglade. He bridges instruction between ancient kaldorei traditions and tauren practitioners despite factional tensions.",al={"dendrite starblaze role","night elf in moonglade"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Great Cat Spirit?",a="The Great Cat Spirit is an ancient primal entity revered by druids, embodying predatory instinct, stealth, and agility. Druids seeking feline form must pass a trial to earn its blessing and understand its playful and deadly nature.",al={"cat spirit lore","spirit of the cat"},it="power"},{q="Do Alliance druids have an equivalent task?",a="Yes. Night elf druids undergo a parallel rite in Moonglade, then return to Darnassus to report to their own mentor instead of traveling to the wind-swept mesas of Mulgore.",al={"alliance version of to thunder bluff","night elf cat form return"},gp=true},{q="Why does Dendrite Starblaze send you back to Thunder Bluff?",a="Dendrite Starblaze serves as a mentor and proctor in Moonglade, guiding you through communing with the Great Cat Spirit. With that trial completed and the spirit's favor earned, his role in this stage of your training is finished. He sends you back to Turak Runetotem so your primary instructor can impart the final teachings and guide you in actually adopting the cat form.",al={"why send to thunder bluff","dendrite starblaze motive","why return to turak runetotem"},it="motive",add="cdfa9758"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you learn from Turak Runetotem to master stealth and claws through this rite.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, your journey reconnects you with Cenarion traditions as you carry lessons from Moonglade back to the Elder Rise of Thunder Bluff.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde druid, you return to your capital so your growing power can defend your kin. The Cenarion Circle remains neutral."},kw={"cat form","dendrite starblaze","druid","elder rise","great cat spirit","moonglade","thunder bluff","turak runetotem"},rel={"npc:turak-runetotem","npc:dendrite-starblaze","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid","quest:1067"},m={start="Dendrite Starblaze",["end"]="Turak Runetotem",level="20",faction="Horde",id=98362},src={"To Thunder Bluff"},fv=true}
E["subzone:elder-rise"] = {t="subzone",n="Elder Rise",z="thunderbluff",s="Elder Rise gathers Thunder Bluff's spiritual guides and elders east of the central plateau. Long suspension bridges connect it to the High Rise and Middle Rise.",h="Elder Rise gathers Thunder Bluff's spiritual guides and elders east of the central plateau.",sec={{t="Sanctuary of Faith and Council",b="Swaying rope bridges link Elder Rise to Thunder Bluff's main mesas. Tauren druids and priests gather here to teach acolytes nature and spiritual devotion. Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem lives atop the mesa. He brought druidism back to the tauren and formed close ties with the Cenarion Circle. Nearby, tribal leaders meet in the Hall of Elders to discuss matters facing their young capital.",sp=0},{t="A Precarious Presence",b="Elder Rise is a peaceful sanctuary, though political tension lingers. Magatha Grimtotem, matriarch of the secretive and haughty Grimtotem tribe, lives in a hut between the two bridges. Cairne Bloodhoof offers hospitality and council seats to all tauren lineages. Magatha's presence reminds the city that not every tribe shares the Bloodhoof's pacifist ideals or unquestioning alliance with the Horde.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Elder Rise used for?",a="Elder Rise is Thunder Bluff's center for spiritual learning and civic deliberation. The Cenarion Circle's druids, tauren priests, the Council of Elders, and tribal leaders gather here.",al={"purpose of elder rise","what is on elder rise","elder rise buildings"},it="purpose"},{q="Who leads the druids on Elder Rise?",a="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem leads the druids on Elder Rise. He is Cairne Bloodhoof's close friend and advisor, the highest-ranking tauren in the Cenarion Circle, and trains those called to follow nature's path.",al={"archdruid thunder bluff","tauren druid leader","hamuul location"},it="leader"},{q="Why does Magatha Grimtotem stay here?",a="Magatha Grimtotem stays in a tent between the bridges and attends the Council of Elders for her people. She is the elder crone and chieftain of the Grimtotem tribe, whose clan distrusts Cairne's allies.",al={"where is magatha","magatha grimtotem location","grimtotem on elder rise"},it="motive"},{q="How do you reach Elder Rise?",a="Cross a large wooden rope bridge from either the High Rise or the lower plateau to reach Elder Rise, directly east of the city's central plateau.",al={"getting to elder rise","elder rise bridges","directions elder rise"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Elder Rise?",a="Elder Rise is the eastern mesa of Thunder Bluff, connected to the central bluffs by sweeping rope bridges. It serves as the spiritual and contemplative heart of the tauren capital, housing the Council of Elders and serving as the local haven for the Cenarion Circle. Priests, druids, and wise elders gather here atop the windswept bluff to meditate, train practitioners of sacred arts, and discuss the matters of nature and tribe.",al={"elder rise","what is elder rise","about elder rise"},it="place",add="f529ee1a"},{q="Who lives on Elder Rise?",a="Elder Rise is home to the city's spiritual guides, including tauren druids and priests. Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem leads the Cenarion Circle's presence here, training disciples in balance and harmony. The mesa is also where the governing Council of Elders convenes, and Magatha Grimtotem, the matriarch of the Grimtotem tribe, maintains her residence between the bridges.",al={"who is on elder rise","elder rise residents","who lives on elder rise"},it="residents",add="bfedf1b8"},{q="Is Elder Rise dangerous?",a="Elder Rise is entirely peaceful and sheltered high above the plains of Mulgore, offering a sanctuary to members of the Horde and respectful travelers. The only true peril you might face is a careless misstep off the edge of the mesa or the high rope bridges swaying in the wind.",al={"is elder rise safe","danger on elder rise","elder rise enemies"},it="danger",add="ea2405f4"},{q="Why is it called Elder Rise?",a="The rise takes its name from the tauren Council of Elders, who convene here in the Hall of Elders to offer their collective wisdom and spiritual leadership to Thunder Bluff. Its cliffs and tents are set aside for these respected community leaders and mentors.",al={"why called elder rise","elder rise name origin","elder rise name"},it="name",add="06c00c52"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you find Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem's sanctuary on Elder Rise, the Cenarion Circle's regional seat in Kalimdor.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you find the Council of Elders and spiritual guides on Elder Rise, where they guide your tribes through peace, tradition, and the complex realities of the Horde."},kw={"cenarion circle","elder rise","hall of elders","hamuul runetotem","magatha grimtotem","mulgore","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","quest:1489","npc:magatha-grimtotem","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","subzone:high-rise","topic:tauren","topic:grimtotem-tribe"},src={"Elder Rise"}}
E["subzone:high-rise"] = {t="subzone",n="High Rise",z="thunderbluff",s="The High Rise gathers Thunder Bluff's tribes around its central fire, high above Mulgore.",h="The High Rise gathers Thunder Bluff's tribes around its central fire, high above Mulgore.",sec={{t="Summit of the Mesa",b="At Thunder Bluff's summit, the High Rise catches the open winds above Mulgore's rolling plains. Tauren gather in its open-air amphitheater around a fire pit to hear tribal announcements and witness decisions. Tents and wooden stalls hold merchants, armories, and culinary trainers, including Aska's Kitchen and Mountaintop Bait & Tackle. The lower tiers reach Mulgore's prairie floor by massive wooden elevators, but no elevator connects the plains to the High Rise. The wind rider roost and rope bridges to Elder Rise and Hunter Rise provide the way up.",sp=0}},faq={{q="How do you reach the High Rise?",a="Reach the High Rise from the lower tiers through the central wind rider roost, or cross a suspension bridge from Elder Rise or Hunter Rise. No lift runs directly from the Mulgore plains to this tier.",al={"how to get to high rise","high rise access","getting up to high rise"},gp=true},{q="What services are found on the High Rise?",a="The High Rise has tradesfolk and outdoor gathering places. Aska's Kitchen teaches cooking, Mountaintop Bait & Tackle sells fishing gear, and Ragetotem Arms and Thunderhoof's Firearms are among its weapon merchants.",al={"trainers on high rise","shops high rise","what is on high rise"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="What is the amphitheater on the High Rise used for?",a="The open-air amphitheater gathers the tauren around a central bonfire. They hear news, deliberate tribal affairs, and witness important proclamations atop the mesa.",al={"high rise bonfire","high rise auditorium","tauren meeting place"},it="purpose"},{q="What is the High Rise?",a="The High Rise is the uppermost tier of Thunder Bluff's central mesa. Sitting high above the windswept plains of Mulgore, it serves as the civic and ceremonial heart of the tauren capital. It features an open-air amphitheater gathered around a central bonfire, various trade shops, and direct rope bridges leading outward to both Hunter Rise and Elder Rise.",al={"what is high rise","high rise thunder bluff","tell me about high rise"},it="place",add="c9070a2e"},{q="Who lives in or runs the High Rise?",a="The High Rise serves as the seat of tauren leadership within Thunder Bluff. High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof and the elder council oversee tribal affairs from this summit, where the populace can gather to witness important decrees and fateful decisions. The tier is also home to respected craftsmen, weaponsmiths, cooks, and anglers who maintain stalls and dwellings around the central grounds.",al={"who leads high rise","who is in charge of high rise","high rise residents"},it="residents",add="b703b2f4"},{q="Is the High Rise dangerous?",a="No, the High Rise is entirely peaceful and well-guarded by Thunder Bluff's vigilant Bluffwatchers. The only real hazard you face is the perilous sheer drop from the mesa's edge or its narrow rope bridges, should you happen to lose your footing.",al={"is high rise safe","danger high rise","threats high rise"},it="danger",add="8703b6d5"},{q="Why is it called the High Rise?",a="The mesa of Thunder Bluff is layered in tiers, with the High Rise occupying the very pinnacle of the central plateau. Standing above the Lower and Middle Rises, it earns its name by being the highest tier of the city's central pillar.",al={"why high rise","high rise name meaning","high rise origin"},it="name",add="e2f731cc"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="At Aska's Kitchen on the High Rise, you can hone your cooking skills with the renowned pit masters over an open flame. It is Thunder Bluff's main place for learning the craft.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see the High Rise crown your capital and unite the tribes. Hunters, shamans, and elders gather around its high communal fire."},kw={"amphitheater","aska's kitchen","bonfire","high rise","mulgore","thunder bluff","wind rider roost"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","zone:mulgore","subzone:elder-rise","subzone:hunter-rise","quest:4767"},src={"High Rise"}}
E["subzone:hunter-rise"] = {t="subzone",n="Hunter Rise",z="thunderbluff",s="Hunters and warriors gather on Hunter Rise, the southern mesa of Thunder Bluff. Its platforms give tauren hunters, trackers, skinners, and warriors room to train and prepare for battle.",h="Hunters and warriors gather on Hunter Rise, the southern mesa of Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="The Gathering of Braves",b="Rope bridges link Hunter Rise to the neighboring bluffs of Thunder Bluff. At its center, the Hunter's Hall is where seasoned marksmen, trackers, and warriors teach the young. Practice grounds around the hall hold training dummies, weapon racks, and skinning posts. Here, tauren learn the skills needed to wield spear and bow and work hides.",sp=0},{t="Martial Duty and Defense",b="Hunter Rise's people hunt across the plains of Mulgore and help defend Thunder Bluff and the wider Horde. Battlemasters stationed along the rise recruit seasoned fighters for skirmishes against Alliance incursions across contested battlegrounds. Those sworn to protect the herd gather here when the Horde needs them.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Hunter Rise located?",a="Hunter Rise lies on the southern side of Thunder Bluff. Rope bridges connect it to the city's lower rise and high rise mesas.",al={"where is hunter rise","hunter rise location","how to get to hunter rise"},gp=true},{q="Who lives and trains on Hunter Rise?",a="Tauren hunters, warriors, trackers, trappers, and leatherworkers live and train on the mesa. Class and profession trainers teach here, and Horde battlemasters recruit fighters for the faction's wars.",al={"who is on hunter rise","hunter rise trainers","what is on hunter rise"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Hunter's Hall?",a="The Hunter's Hall is the main longhouse on Hunter Rise, where seasoned hunters and warriors gather. It is an armory and school for those learning tracking, marksmanship, and close combat.",al={"hunters hall","hunters lodge thunder bluff","thunder bluff hunter hall"}},{q="Can members of the Alliance visit Hunter Rise?",a="No. Thunder Bluff is a major Horde capital, and seasoned tauren braves guard Hunter Rise. City guards attack Alliance adventurers who try to cross its bridges.",al={"alliance on hunter rise","can alliance go to hunter rise"},gp=true},{q="What is Hunter Rise?",a="Hunter Rise is one of the grand mesas that forms the city of Thunder Bluff, situated just south of the central bluff and linked to the rest of the settlement by sweeping rope bridges. It serves as the martial heart of the tauren capital, dedicated to the training, gathering, and arming of warriors, hunters, and scouts who defend the tribes and hunt across the plains of Mulgore.",al={"what is hunter rise","hunter rise info","hunter rise lore"},it="place",add="fb082e53"},{q="Is Hunter Rise dangerous?",a="For members of the Horde and peaceful visitors, Hunter Rise is entirely safe. It is an orderly sanctuary filled with veterans, weapon masters, and seasoned trackers. For enemies of the Horde or members of the Alliance who dare venture onto the mesa, however, the bluff is lethal, guarded by watchful sentries and skilled combatants ready to strike down intruders on sight.",al={"is hunter rise safe","danger on hunter rise","hunter rise danger"},it="danger",add="328a4c07"},{q="Why is it called Hunter Rise?",a="The mesa takes its name from its central purpose: honoring and refining the ancient hunting traditions of the tauren. It is home to the renowned Hunter's Hall, where master trackers, tanners, and marksmen pass down survival skills essential to plains life, ensuring the hunt remains woven into the survival and spirit of their people.",al={"why called hunter rise","hunter rise name origin","how did hunter rise get its name"},it="name",add="5f696981"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a young tauren hunter, you can find training, pet supplies, and guidance from master trackers on Hunter Rise, the heart of your calling in the capital.",["class:Warrior"]="Hunter Rise's grounds offer training dummies, combat mentors, and battlemasters ready to test your strength as you help defend the Horde."},kw={"battlemasters","hunter rise","hunter's hall","mulgore","thunder bluff","trackers"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","subzone:high-rise","topic:tauren","topic:alliance"},src={"Hunter Rise"}}
E["subzone:pools-of-vision"] = {t="subzone",n="Pools of Vision",z="thunderbluff",s="Forsaken gather in the Pools of Vision, beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff. Still waters and dim caverns shelter their enclave within the tauren capital.",h="Forsaken gather in the Pools of Vision, beneath Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Haven Beneath the Mesa",b="The Pools of Vision lie beneath Spirit Rise, below Thunder Bluff's sunlit peaks. A cave path beside the bridge to the rise leads down into the grotto. Misty waters fill its shadowed chambers, where Horde spellcasters gather apart from the open-air lodges above.",sp=0},{t="The Undead Outpost",b="Forsaken make their base within the Pools of Vision. Undead priests practice shadowed arts, mages conjure arcane portals, and Defiler emissaries seek recruits for their campaigns in the Arathi Highlands. Whether tauren skepticism or the Forsaken's own preference for darkness brought them here, the cavern links Lordaeron's undead with their allies in Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the entrance to the Pools of Vision?",a="Cross the wooden rope bridge from the lower mesa to Spirit Rise. The cave mouth is immediately to your right.",al={"how to get to pools of vision","pools of vision entrance","where are pools of vision"},gp=true},{q="Why are the Forsaken living down here?",a="The cavern is the central hub for Forsaken stationed in Thunder Bluff. Its shelter keeps them from Kalimdor's harsh sunlight and gives them room for practices that may unsettle traditional tauren spiritualists.",al={"why undead here","why forsaken in cave","thunder bluff undead"},it="why_here"},{q="What services can you find inside the Pools of Vision?",a="Priests and mages train and practice in the cavern. Defiler emissaries also muster soldiers for the war effort in the Arathi Highlands.",al={"trainers in pools of vision","what is in pools of vision","pools of vision trainers"},gp=true},{q="Where do mages arrive when they teleport to Thunder Bluff?",a="A teleport or portal to Thunder Bluff brings mages directly to the sheltered waters of the Pools of Vision beneath Spirit Rise.",al={"mage teleport thunder bluff spot","tb teleport location"},it="arrival"},{q="What are the Pools of Vision?",a="The Pools of Vision are a subterranean cavern and water-filled grotto hidden beneath the high bluffs of Spirit Rise. Far removed from the open winds and sunlit plains above, this damp underground hollow serves as an enclave for arcane arts and the primary hub for the Forsaken stationed within Thunder Bluff.",al={"pools of vision","what is pools of vision","about pools of vision"},it="place",add="746eaf51"},{q="Who lives in the Pools of Vision?",a="The cavern is primarily inhabited by the Forsaken visiting or stationed in Thunder Bluff. Undead priests and mages practice their arts here away from the bustling rises above, alongside emissaries such as those representing the Defilers, who seek recruits for the ongoing struggle in the Arathi Basin.",al={"who is in pools of vision","pools of vision residents","who runs pools of vision"},it="residents",add="f71c91fd"},{q="Are the Pools of Vision dangerous?",a="No. Despite its dark and brooding atmosphere, the Pools of Vision is entirely secure for members and allies of the Horde. It functions as a safe haven within Thunder Bluff's borders, housing trainers, scholars, and envoys of the Undercity rather than hostile beasts or enemies.",al={"is pools of vision safe","danger in pools of vision","are the pools hostile"},it="danger",add="9510841e"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken crossing Kalimdor's plains, you can find familiar shade, arcane resources, priestly guidance, and fellowship in this cavern.",["class:Mage"]="As a mage, you arrive beside these secluded pools when you teleport to Thunder Bluff; the cavern anchors the arcane ley connections to the city."},kw={"defilers","forsaken","mage portal","pools of vision","spirit rise","thunder bluff","undead enclave"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","subzone:spirit-rise","topic:forsaken","topic:horde","topic:tauren"},src={"Pools of Vision"}}
E["subzone:spirit-rise"] = {t="subzone",n="Spirit Rise",z="thunderbluff",s="Spirit Rise gathers Thunder Bluff’s spiritual and shamanic study on its northwest mesa. The Skychaser tribe guides seekers above the Pools of Vision, where seers look into spirit-touched waters.",h="Spirit Rise gathers Thunder Bluff’s spiritual and shamanic study on its northwest mesa.",sec={{t="A Sanctuary of the Spirits",b="Spirit Rise crowns Thunder Bluff above the plains of Mulgore, devoted to communion with the elements and ancestor spirits. Rope bridges link it to the central mesa. The Hall of Spirits and the Spiritual Healing pavilion draw young and veteran shaman seeking a deeper bond with earth, air, fire, and water. The Skychaser tribe keeps a strong presence across the rise and guides seekers in ancient traditions.",sp=0},{t="Caves and Crossings",b="Beneath the open-air totem shrines and huts, an entrance leads into the mesa. The steamy Pools of Vision fill a sacred cavern below, where seers peer into waters touched by the spirits.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Spirit Rise known for?",a="Spirit Rise is the spiritual heart of Thunder Bluff, devoted to shamanic practice, healing, and communion with nature spirits and ancestors. It also opens onto the Pools of Vision.",al={"what is spirit rise","spirit rise purpose","why visit spirit rise"},it="purpose"},{q="Which tauren tribe leads activities on Spirit Rise?",a="The Skychaser tribe guides activity on Spirit Rise, fostering spiritual traditions, divination rituals, and shamanic training.",al={"who runs spirit rise","spirit rise tribe","skychaser tribe"},it="residents"},{q="What can I find underneath Spirit Rise?",a="A descent through Spirit Rise leads to the Pools of Vision, a humid cavern of steaming waters where seers and spiritual practitioners meditate and seek visions.",al={"spirit rise cave","below spirit rise","pools of vision entrance"},it="place"},{q="What is Spirit Rise?",a="Spirit Rise is one of the elevated mesas making up Thunder Bluff, situated to the northwest of the central bluff. It serves as the spiritual heart of the city, dedicated primarily to shamanistic studies, spirit communion, and ancestral guidance. Connected to the rest of the city by rope bridges, the rise houses the Hall of Spirits and sits above the subterranean cavern known as the Pools of Vision.",al={"what is spirit rise","spirit rise info","spirit rise thunder bluff"},it="place",add="a67a2478"},{q="Is Spirit Rise dangerous?",a="Not in the slightest. Spirit Rise is a sanctuary within the sovereign capital of the tauren. You will find shamans, spiritual healers, and visiting travelers here rather than hostile beasts or invaders. The only real peril is the sheer drop off the cliffs if you happen to lose your footing near the edge of the mesa or its suspension bridges.",al={"is spirit rise safe","danger spirit rise","enemies on spirit rise"},it="danger",add="6e710860"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman of the Horde, Spirit Rise is an essential gathering place to consult trainers, perform elemental rites, and commune with ancestral spirits.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you find your people’s deep spiritual roots on the rise, with solace from secular duties and the mystical waters of the Pools of Vision."},kw={"hall of spirits","mulgore","pools of vision","shaman","skychaser","spirit rise","thunder bluff"},rel={"zone:thunderbluff","subzone:pools-of-vision","zone:orgrimmar"},src={"Spirit Rise"}}
E["zone:thunderbluff"] = {t="city",n="Thunder Bluff",z="thunderbluff",s="High above the grasslands of Mulgore, Thunder Bluff rises on windswept red mesas. It is the capital of the tauren, and the heart of their spirit, their culture and their trade. Swaying rope bridges and wooden lifts join its heights. Safe from the centaur marauders, it is a place of peace for travelers from all over Kalimdor.",h="High above the grasslands of Mulgore, Thunder Bluff rises on windswept red mesas.",sec={{t="A Permanent Haven",b="For countless generations, the tauren wandered Kalimdor, fighting the centaur for their very survival. That age ended in the Third War, when High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof joined forces with Warchief Thrall. Together the orcs and tauren broke the centaur's assaults, and won the pastures of Mulgore. Then Cairne led the allied tribes up onto these bastions of stone, and founded Thunder Bluff. It was the first lasting home the united tribes had known in centuries.",sp=0},{t="A City in the Clouds",b="The central bluffs hold the markets, the bank and the inn, and a towering roost for the wind riders. Three more mesas branch out across the abyss, each with its own calling. Scouts and trackers live on Hunter Rise. The lorekeepers live on Elder Rise, with the Cenarion Circle under Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem.\n\nAnd Spirit Rise is given to the spirits. There dwell the shaman and the priests. Deep beneath them lie the caverns called the Pools of Vision.",sp=0},{t="Uneasy Unity",b="Cairne Bloodhoof commands the respect of almost every tribe, but the recently settled tauren do not all agree. The Grimtotem tribe, led by Elder Crone Magatha Grimtotem, keeps to Elder Rise. Magatha questions Cairne’s conciliatory ways and his allegiance to the Horde’s foreign races. Peace holds under Cairne’s watch, though divisions persist among the council fires above the plains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who rules Thunder Bluff?",a="High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof rules Thunder Bluff and leads the united tauren tribes. His wisdom, patience, and strength are revered. He founded the city after allying with Thrall’s Horde and driving the centaur from Mulgore, uniting the nomadic tribes under the New Horde.",al={"leader of thunder bluff","who is in charge","thunder bluff chieftain","cairne"},it="in_charge",nx={8,9}},{q="How do you get up to Thunder Bluff?",a="If you arrive on foot or by kodo, ride one of the large wooden platform lifts on the southwestern or northeastern side of the central mesa. You can also take a Wind Rider flight across Kalimdor.",al={"thunder bluff elevator","how to get in","thunder bluff entrance","getting up"},it="arrival"},{q="Why did the tauren build on high mesas instead of the ground?",a="Centaur clans harried the tauren during centuries of nomadic life. The bluffs’ steep cliffs guard their homes, smiths, and sacred elders from attacks on the ground, giving the tauren a place to settle in peace.",al={"why mesas","why are they on cliffs","thunder bluff cliffs","tauren high ground"},it="history"},{q="What are the different rises of the city?",a="The central mesa has lower, middle, and high tiers, with three outer mesas around it. Hunter Rise holds warriors, hunters, and tracking lodges. Druids, wisemen, and the Grimtotem tribe dwell on Elder Rise. Spirit Rise has shrines to the Earth Mother, trainers of shamans, priests, and mages, and the Pools of Vision below, offering shelter for shamans and priests devoted to spiritual communion.",al={"thunder bluff areas","what are the rises","districts of thunder bluff"},it="place"},{q="What are the Pools of Vision?",a="The Pools of Vision are sacred caverns beneath Spirit Rise. Tauren seers, spiritwalkers, and practitioners of the arcane gather at these quiet, mist-shrouded waters to commune with the elements and read omens about their people’s future.",al={"pools of vision","spirit rise cave","thunder bluff cave"}},{q="Who is Magatha Grimtotem?",a="Magatha Grimtotem is the matriarch and Elder Crone of the Grimtotem clan. She lives on Elder Rise and takes part in Cairne’s council, but distrusts outsiders and challenges the Bloodhoof tribe’s welcoming stance toward the Horde.",al={"magatha","elder crone","who is the grimtotem leader"},it="identity"},{q="What is Thunder Bluff?",a="Thunder Bluff is the capital city of the tauren, perched high atop the windswept mesas of northern Mulgore. Established by High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof after driving back the centaur with Thrall's Horde, it provides a safe, permanent sanctuary for a people who lived as wandering nomads for generations.",al={"what is this city","tell me about thunder bluff","thunder bluff city"},it="place",add="6fa5b073"},{q="Is Cairne Bloodhoof a king?",a="No. Cairne Bloodhoof holds the title of High Chieftain of the united tauren tribes. Tauren society does not crown monarchs; Cairne governs through the deep respect, wisdom, and strength he has demonstrated over decades, rather than hereditary royal divine right.",al={"cairne bloodhoof king","is cairne a king","tauren king"},it="leader",add="fc90632b"},{q="Does Cairne Bloodhoof answer to Thrall?",a="Thrall is the Warchief of the Horde, but his bond with Cairne is grounded in mutual honor and alliance rather than strict subjugation. Cairne pledged his people to the Horde out of gratitude and shared vision, standing as one of Thrall's most trusted counselors and equals.",al={"does cairne answer to thrall","is thrall cairne's boss","cairne and thrall"},it="side",add="047fa056"},{q="Why did the tauren join the Horde?",a="Centaur marauders had pushed the nomadic tauren to the brink of extinction across the Barrens. When Warchief Thrall and the orcs landed on Kalimdor, they aided Cairne's people in breaking the centaur siege and securing Mulgore, forging an unbreakable bond between their cultures.",al={"why join horde","tauren horde alliance","how did tauren join"},it="history",add="85c1a10f"},{q="What's the deal with the Grimtotem tribe?",a="The Grimtotem are a fierce and aggressive clan led by the elder crone Magatha. Unlike the peaceful Bloodhoof, they harbor deep suspicion toward outsiders and openly question Cairne's peaceful leadership, believing tauren should conquer Kalimdor and drive out the other races.",al={"grimtotem tribe","who are the grimtotem","grimtotem tauren"},it="threat",add="3180b5ca",nx={12}},{q="Are the Grimtotem enemies of Cairne?",a="Openly, they remain part of the united tauren nation, and Magatha even resides on Elder Rise. Beneath the surface, however, bitter political rivalry simmers, as Magatha constantly schemes and believes that she alone possesses the rightful vision to rule the tauren.",al={"are grimtotem evil","grimtotem against cairne","magatha vs cairne"},it="hostile",add="ca8246e8"},{q="Is Thunder Bluff dangerous?",a="Within the city, the brave guards maintain order and safety from the beasts and quilboar prowling the plains below. The biggest immediate hazard for visitors is the sheer drop—one careless misstep off the mesa edges or wooden bridges will prove fatal.",al={"is thunder bluff safe","threats in thunder bluff","danger here"},it="danger",add="54829977"},{q="How did I end up in Thunder Bluff?",a="If you are a young tauren, your journey began south upon the sheltered grasslands of Red Cloud Mesa and passed through Bloodhoof Village before bringing you here. The road leads to the base of these towering mesas, where great wooden rope elevators hoist travelers hundreds of feet into the sky. Alternatively, visitors journeying from distant lands across Kalimdor often arrive by wyvern at the central Wind Rider Roost atop the bluffs.",al={"how did i get here","how did i get to thunder bluff","how do i reach thunder bluff"},it="arrival",add="7db56847"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Thunder Bluff?",a="Thunder Bluff is the spiritual and cultural heart of the united tauren tribes. Here you can seek advanced training from elder shamans, druids, hunters, and warriors gathered across the rises. High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof and the tribal elders also rely on capable champions to protect Mulgore from lingering threats—including prowling centaur raiders, the encroaching Venture Company, harpies, and rebellious quilboars—before sending you eastward into the wider trials of the Horde.",al={"what should i do in thunder bluff","why am i here","what is my purpose here"},it="purpose",add="347b5cac"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Thunder Bluff marks your people’s hard-won unity and rebirth after generations of wandering and centaur attacks under High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof.",["class:Druid"]="On Elder Rise, Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem leads the Horde’s foremost sanctuary of nature magic. He is the first tauren druid taught in thousands of years.",["class:Shaman"]="On Spirit Rise, the Pools of Vision offer a quiet place to honor and hear elemental spirits and the spirits of your tauren ancestors.",["faction:Horde"]="Thunder Bluff brings a pastoral presence to the New Horde’s southern reach in Kalimdor, far calmer than Orgrimmar’s harsh battlements."},kw={"cairne bloodhoof","elder rise","elevators","hamuul runetotem","hunter rise","magatha grimtotem","mulgore","pools of vision","spirit rise","thunder bluff"},rel={"npc:cairne-bloodhoof","zone:mulgore","npc:magatha-grimtotem","subzone:pools-of-vision","subzone:elder-rise","subzone:hunter-rise","subzone:spirit-rise"},src={"Thunder Bluff"}}
